      "name": "ReceiveQueueData",
      "signature": "ushort ReceiveQueueData(uint * pQueue, byte * pbDest, ushort wMaxSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "ushort",
      "comment": "Dequeues data from a synchronized linked-list queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section at queue offset +4\n2. Get head node pointer from offset +0x1c\n3. If head is NULL, return 0\n4. If data size > wMaxSize, set error flag and return 0\n5. Copy data from node+8 to destination buffer\n6. Free current node, advance head to next node\n7. If queue empty, clear tail pointer at offset +0x20\n8. Leave critical section, return bytes copied\n\nParameters:\n- pQueue (uint*): Queue structure with CRITICAL_SECTION at +4, head at +0x1c, tail at +0x20\n- pbDest (byte*): Destination buffer for dequeued data\n- wMaxSize (ushort): Maximum bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes copied on success, 0 if queue empty or buffer too small\n\nStructure Layout:\n- +0x00: Error flag (set to 1 if buffer too small)\n- +0x04: CRITICAL_SECTION\n- +0x1c: Head node pointer\n- +0x20: Tail node pointer\n\nNode Structure:\n- +0x00: Data size (ushort)\n- +0x04: Next node pointer\n- +0x08: Data bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:f8e27aea009234a8de0fdc8716090e75",
