      "name": "ProcessSocketPackets",
      "signature": "void ProcessSocketPackets(void * pSocket, byte * pbBuffer, int nBufEnd)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes incoming socket data buffer extracting and dispatching packets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop through buffer reading packet size from header offset\n2. Compare remaining bytes against header size and packet size\n3. If insufficient data, copy remainder to output and return\n4. Validate packet size < 0x2000 (8KB max), assert on failure\n5. If dispatcher callback exists, validate and call it\n6. Enqueue message to socket queue at pSocket+0x16c\n7. Signal event handle at pSocket+0x114\n8. Advance buffer pointer by packet size, repeat\n\nParameters:\n- pSocket (void*): Socket context structure\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Source data buffer to process\n- nBufEnd (int): End address of valid buffer data\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies pbBuffer in-place with unprocessed remainder)\n\nSocket Context Fields:\n- +0x114: HANDLE hEvent (signaled after each packet)\n- +0x118: int nHeaderSize\n- +0x11c: int nSizeOffset (offset to size field in header)\n- +0x164: FARPROC fpDispatcher (optional callback)\n- +0x168: void* pDispatcherContext\n- +0x16c: Message queue structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2000 (8192): Maximum allowed packet size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
