      "name": "CreateNetSession",
      "signature": "void * CreateNetSession(char * szIpAddr, int nPort, char * szDescription)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a network session structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates szIpAddr is not NULL (asserts if NULL)\n2. Validates strlen(szIpAddr) < 0x103 (MAX_PATH + 1)\n3. Allocates 400-byte session structure via Ordinal_10042\n4. Zero-initializes all 100 dwords of the structure\n5. Copies IP address to offset 0x8 (max 0x104 bytes)\n6. Copies description to offset 0x124, or \"UNKNOWN\" if NULL\n7. Stores port at offset 0x10c\n8. Initializes critical section at offset 0x16c\n9. Sets state fields: [0x118]=2, [0x11c]=0\n\nParameters:\n- szIpAddr: IP address string (required, max 258 chars)\n- nPort: Port number for the connection\n- szDescription: Session description (optional, uses \"UNKNOWN\" if NULL)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated session structure on success\n- NULL if allocation fails\n\nStructure Layout (400 bytes):\n- 0x008: char[0x104] IP address\n- 0x10c: int port\n- 0x118: int state (initialized to 2)\n- 0x11c: int flags (initialized to 0)\n- 0x124: char[0x40] description\n- 0x16c: CRITICAL_SECTION lock",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:8",
