      "comment": "Encodes a 32-bit integer into a 4-byte base-255 buffer with +1 offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract value mod 255, add 1, store at lpszBuffer[0]\n2. Divide by 255, extract mod 255, add 1, store at lpszBuffer[1]\n3. Divide by 255^2 (0xfe01), extract mod 255, add 1, store at lpszBuffer[2]\n4. Divide by 255^3 (0xfd02ff), extract mod 255, add 1, store at lpszBuffer[3]\n5. Return overflow (quotient after 255^4 division)\n\nParameters:\n- lpszBuffer (char*): Output buffer receiving 4-byte encoded value\n- dwValue (uint): 32-bit integer value to encode\n\nReturns:\n- Overflow quotient (dwValue / 255^4), 0 for inputs under 4.2 billion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xff (255): Encoding base, ensures no null bytes in output\n- 0xfe01 (65025): 255^2 for third byte extraction\n- 0xfd02ff (16581375): 255^3 for fourth byte extraction\n- +1 offset on each byte prevents null terminators in string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
