      "name": "GenerateGammaTable",
      "signature": "void GenerateGammaTable(int nGammaValue, void * pOutTable, double dPercentLinear, int nEntrySize, int nEntryCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Generates a gamma correction lookup table with configurable entry sizes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nEntrySize is 1, 2, or 4 bytes (assert otherwise)\n2. Validate nGammaValue >= 0 (assert otherwise)\n3. Validate dPercentLinear in range [0.0, 1.0] (assert otherwise)\n4. Loop from 0 to nEntryCount-1, computing gamma-corrected values\n5. Store each value based on entry size (byte, short, or dword)\n\nParameters:\n- nGammaValue (int): Gamma correction value (must be >= 0)\n- pOutTable (void*): Output buffer for the lookup table\n- dPercentLinear (double): Linear interpolation factor [0.0 to 1.0]\n- nEntrySize (int): Bytes per entry (1, 2, or 4)\n- nEntryCount (int): Number of entries to generate\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0.0, 1.0: Valid range bounds for dPercentLinear\n- 1, 2, 4: Valid entry sizes in bytes",
