      "name": "ClearBitInArray",
      "signature": "void ClearBitInArray(byte * pbArray, uint dwBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears a single bit in a byte array using inverse bit masks.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte offset: dwBitIndex >> 3 (divide by 8)\n2. Calculate bit position: dwBitIndex & 7 (mod 8)\n3. Look up inverse mask from gdwInvBitMasks table\n4. AND the target byte with the inverse mask to clear the bit\n\nParameters:\n- pbArray (byte*): Pointer to bit array buffer\n- dwBitIndex (uint): Zero-based index of bit to clear\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10121: Toggle bit (XOR)\n- Ordinal_10122: AND bit arrays",
