      "name": "ToggleBit",
      "signature": "void ToggleBit(byte * pbBitArray, uint dwBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Toggles a bit at a specified index in a bit array using XOR.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute byte offset (dwBitIndex >> 3) within bit array\n2. Compute bit position (dwBitIndex & 7) within byte\n3. Lookup bitmask from gdwBitMasks table for bit position\n4. XOR target byte with bitmask to toggle the bit\n\nParameters:\n- pbBitArray (byte*): Pointer to byte array treated as bit array\n- dwBitIndex (uint): Zero-based bit index to toggle\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7 (7): Mask for bit position (0-7) within byte\n- >> 3: Divide by 8 to get byte offset from bit index",
