      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs bitwise OR of two buffers into a destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert bit count to byte count ((nBitCount + 7) / 8)\n2. Calculate aligned 4-byte chunk count\n3. Process aligned chunks via 32-bit OR operations\n4. Handle remaining 1-3 trailing bytes individually\n\nParameters:\n- pbSrc1 (byte*): First source buffer\n- pbSrc2 (byte*): Second source buffer\n- pbDst (byte*): Destination buffer for OR result\n- nBitCount (int): Number of bits to process\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Exported as Ordinal 10123\n- Optimizes by processing 4 bytes at a time when possible",
