      "comment": "XORs key and source buffers, storing result in destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Converts nBitCount to byte count: (nBitCount + 7) / 8\n2. Calculates DWORD-aligned portion: byteCount / 4 * 4 \n3. Processes aligned DWORD chunks via XOR loop\n4. Handles remaining 1-3 bytes individually via fall-through switch\n\nParameters:\n- pbKeyData (byte*): Key buffer for XOR operation\n- pbSrcData (byte*): Source data buffer to be XORed  \n- pbDestData (byte*): Destination buffer for XOR result\n- nBitCount (int): Number of bits to process\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pbDestData)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7 (7): Bit rounding for byte alignment\n- 0x3: Mask for DWORD alignment calculation",
