      "name": "WriteBitsToBuffer",
      "signature": "void WriteBitsToBuffer(int * pBitBuf, uint dwValue, int nBitCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Writes bits to a bit buffer structure for packet/data serialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer has enough space: (nByteIdx * 8 + nBitOffset + nBitCount) <= nMaxBits\n2. If at byte boundary (nBitOffset == 0), initialize current byte to 0\n3. Loop while bits remain to write:\n   a. Calculate bits available in current byte (8 - nBitOffset)\n   b. Mask and shift value bits into current byte position\n   c. Update bit offset; if byte complete (offset == 8):\n      - Advance buffer pointer and byte index\n      - Reset bit offset to 0\n      - Initialize next byte to 0 if within bounds\n   d. Shift remaining value bits and decrement count\n\nParameters:\n- pBitBuf (int*): Pointer to BitBuffer structure:\n  [0] = byte* pCurByte - current write position\n  [1] = int nMaxBits - total buffer capacity in bits\n  [2] = int nByteIdx - current byte index\n  [3] = int nBitOffset - bit position within current byte (0-7)\n- dwValue (uint): Value containing bits to write (LSB first)\n- nBitCount (int): Number of bits to write from dwValue\n\nReturns:\n- void (asserts on buffer overflow via Ordinal_10023)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x165 (357): Assert line number in Fog source\n- g_adwBitMasks: Lookup table [0,1,3,7,15,31,63,127] for bit masking",
