      "signature": "uint AddTableEntry(uint dwKey, uint dwValue1, uint dwValue2, HashTable * pTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Adds an entry to a hash table structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Hash dwKey via Ordinal_502 (SStrHash)\n2. Read current entry count from pTable->nCount\n3. Calculate offset as count * 0xc (12-byte entries)\n4. If total size exceeds 0x400 bytes, return error 0xe\n5. Store hash at entries[count].dwHash\n6. Store dwValue1 at entries[count].dwValue1\n7. Store dwValue2 at entries[count].dwValue2\n8. Increment entry count\n9. Return 0 for success\n\nParameters:\n- dwKey (uint): Key to hash for table entry\n- dwValue1 (uint): First associated value\n- dwValue2 (uint): Second associated value\n- pTable (HashTable*): Target hash table structure\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success, entry added\n- 0xe (14): Table overflow, entry not added\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc (12): Entry stride (sizeof(HashTableEntry))\n- 0x14 (20): Header + first entry offset check\n- 0x400 (1024): Maximum table size in bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:5",
