      "name": "UnpackString",
      "signature": "void UnpackString(int * pStrPack, char * szOutput, byte * pbBuffer, int nByteCount, int nMaxLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unpacks a bit-compressed string using a StringPack lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pStrPack, szOutput, pbBuffer (assert non-null)\n2. Validate pStrPack->nPackedBits is non-zero\n3. Calculate max chars: (nByteCount * 8 + 7) / nPackedBits\n4. Clamp to min(nMaxChars, nMaxLen - 1)\n5. Initialize bit buffer for reading\n6. Loop: read nPackedBits bits, lookup char at pStrPack[0x103 + index]\n7. Write char to output, break on null terminator\n8. Null-terminate output string\n\nParameters:\n- pStrPack (int*): StringPack structure with nPackedBits at offset 0 and char table at offset 0x103\n- szOutput (char*): Output buffer for unpacked string\n- pbBuffer (byte*): Packed bit data buffer\n- nByteCount (int): Size of packed data in bytes\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum output string length including null\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x103 (259): Offset to character lookup table in StringPack\n- 0x8: Bits per byte for max chars calculation\n- 0x7: Rounding adjustment for ceiling division\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10135: PackString - inverse operation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:6a2ff2a6738ba413861681d0ac70bc01",
