      "name": "EscapeStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "byte * EscapeStringToBuffer(byte * pbDest, byte * pbSrc, int nDestSize, byte byQuoteChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Escapes control characters in source string to destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert pbDest is non-NULL (fatal error if NULL)\n2. If pbSrc is NULL, copy \"<NULL>\" to dest and return\n3. If byQuoteChar is non-zero, write it as opening quote\n4. Copy bytes from pbSrc to pbDest, escaping control chars:\n   - CR (0x0D) -> \\r\n   - LF (0x0A) -> \n\n   - Tab (0x09) -> \\t\n   - Other < 0x20 -> \\xNN (hex escape)\n5. If byQuoteChar is non-zero, write it as closing quote\n6. Null-terminate the result\n\nParameters:\n- pbDest (byte*): Destination buffer (ECX, __fastcall)\n- pbSrc (byte*): Source string to escape (EDX, __fastcall)\n- nDestSize (int): Size of destination buffer\n- byQuoteChar (byte): Quote character to wrap result (0 = none)\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to pbDest on success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5C (92): Backslash '\\' for escape sequences\n- 0x72 (114): 'r' for carriage return escape\n- 0x6E (110): 'n' for newline escape\n- 0x74 (116): 't' for tab escape\n- 0x78 (120): 'x' for hex escape prefix\n- 0x30 (48): '0' ASCII base for hex digits 0-9\n- 0x37 (55): 'A'-10 base for hex digits A-F",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:68360cb7734ed344625693d3017d4d17",
