      "comment": "Formats a 64-bit integer as a comma-separated decimal string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clamp buffer size to maximum of 32 characters\n2. Combine nLow and nHigh into single 64-bit value\n3. Extract digits via modulo 10 into temporary buffer\n4. Insert comma separator every 3 digits\n5. If buffer would overflow, fill with asterisks instead\n6. Reverse the digit string into output buffer\n7. Null terminate result string and return\n\nParameters:\n- szOutBuf (char*): Output string buffer to receive formatted number\n- dwBufSize (uint): Size of output buffer (auto-clamped to 32 max)\n- nLow (int): Low 32 bits of the 64-bit value to format\n- nHigh (int): High 32 bits of the 64-bit value to format\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to szOutBuf containing the formatted decimal string\n- Returns asterisks like \"***\" if number too large for buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum buffer size limit\n- 0x2c (44): ASCII comma character for thousand separators\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII digit '0' base value\n- 0x2a (42): ASCII asterisk for overflow indication",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:5b0a7812e1d8ffe2db30da489713205b",
