      "name": "InitializeNetworkContext",
      "signature": "int * InitializeNetworkContext(int nNetworkMode, int nMaxConnections, ushort wPort, int nUseWinNT, int nOnConnect, int nOnDisconnect, int nOnReceive, int nOnSend)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Initializes the Storm network context structure for TCP/IP communication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate network context structure (0xC4C bytes)\n2. Zero-initialize structure and copy global config values\n3. Allocate connection arrays and initialize critical sections\n4. Allocate send/receive buffer arrays\n5. Store callback function pointers for network events\n6. Check if running on Windows NT via Ordinal_10176\n7. Call WSAStartup to initialize Winsock 1.1\n8. Start server (listen) or client mode based on nNetworkMode\n\nParameters:\n- nNetworkMode: 1=server, 2=client, other=auto-detect\n- nMaxConnections: Max simultaneous connections\n- wPort: TCP port to bind/connect\n- nUseWinNT: Force non-NT mode if non-zero\n- nOnConnect: Callback for connection events\n- nOnDisconnect: Callback for disconnection events\n- nOnReceive: Callback for data receive events\n- nOnSend: Callback for data send completion\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated network context structure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC4C (3148): Total context structure size\n- 0x313 (787): DWORDs to zero (0xC4C/4)\n- 0x18 (24): Critical section stride\n- 0x101: Winsock version 1.1",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
