      "name": "BroadcastDataToAllSockets",
      "signature": "int BroadcastDataToAllSockets(int * pNetManager, byte * pbData, uint dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Broadcasts data to all active sockets in the network manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return success if no slots exist\n2. For each slot in the manager:\n   a. Acquire slot's critical section lock\n   b. Traverse linked list of socket entries\n   c. Skip entries marked as inactive (offset 0xC != 0)\n   d. Send data via direct send or queued send based on manager mode\n   e. Release critical section\n3. Return 1 (always succeeds)\n\nParameters:\n- pNetManager (int*): Network manager structure\n  - [0x00]: Mode flag (0=direct send, non-zero=queued send)\n  - [0x08]: Number of slots\n  - [0x14]: Pointer to slot array (linked lists of socket entries)\n  - [0x1C]: Base address of critical sections array\n- pbData (byte*): Data buffer to broadcast\n- dwDataSize (uint): Size of data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): Stride between critical sections (sizeof CRITICAL_SECTION)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:52a0dd72a38325233b4d111bea1df32a",
