      "name": "DisconnectClient",
      "signature": "void DisconnectClient(void * pServer, dword nClientId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Disconnects a client by ID and cleans up all associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Find client in hash table by ID (hash bucket = nClientId & mask)\n2. Return early if client not found or already disconnecting\n3. Set disconnect flag, close socket via Ordinal_10000\n4. Decrement reference count; if still referenced, defer cleanup\n5. Remove from client ID hash table\n6. Remove from IP address hash table\n7. Remove from IP reference count table via FUN_6ff66000\n8. Free pending write queue entries\n9. Delete critical section and free client structure\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Pointer to server context structure\n- nClientId (uint): Client ID to disconnect\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Hash mask offset in server\n- 0x14: Client ID hash table pointer offset\n- 0x1c: Critical section array offset\n- 0x18: Critical section stride (24 bytes)\n- 0x20: IP hash table pointer offset\n- 0x28: IP table critical section offset\n- 0x854: Server-wide client count critical section\n- 0x880: Active client count offset\n- 0xbc8: Optional callback function pointer offset\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff63af0: Full client cleanup (decrements ref, removes from tables)\n- FUN_6ff66000: Remove IP reference from tracking table\n- HashTableFindEntry: Find client by ID",
