      "name": "HashTableFindEntry",
      "signature": "uint * HashTableFindEntry(FogHashTable * pHashTable, uint dwKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Finds an entry in a hash table by key.\\n\\nUses bucket locking to ensure thread-safe lookup\\nin a chained hash table implementation.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Compute bucket index using mask: (mask & key)\\n2. Calculate critical section offset: index * 0x18\\n3. Enter critical section for this bucket\\n4. Traverse linked list searching for matching key\\n5. Leave critical section\\n6. Return found entry or NULL\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pHashTable (FogHashTable*): Hash table context\\n  +0x0C: dwMask - bitmask for bucket calculation\\n  +0x14: ppBuckets - pointer to bucket array\\n  +0x1C: pCritSections - critical section array\\n- dwKey (uint): Key value to search for\\n\\nReturns:\\n- Pointer to hash entry node if found\\n- NULL if key not found in table\\n- Entry format: [0]=key, [4]=pNextNode",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:fc72d054cea08c5e0defe5eade6bcfb5",
