      "name": "ReleaseClientConnection",
      "signature": "void ReleaseClientConnection(uint * pServerCtx, uint * pClient)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases a client connection when reference count reaches zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Decrement client ref count via InterlockedDecrement\n2. If ref count > 0, return (other references exist)\n3. Call optional callback at pServerCtx+0xBC8 if set\n4. Lock client hash bucket (0x18 stride per bucket)\n5. Find client in hash table by client ID, unlink from list\n6. Decrement server client count at pServerCtx+0x880\n7. Log disconnect with inet_ntoa for client IP\n8. Remove client from IP-based hash table at pServerCtx+0x20\n9. Remove from third table at pServerCtx+0x40 with ref decrement\n10. Log any remaining packet counts\n11. Free pending packet linked list at pClient+0x74\n12. Delete client critical section, free client memory\n\nParameters:\n- pServerCtx (uint*): Server context with hash tables and locks\n- pClient (uint*): Client structure to release\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18: Hash bucket stride (CRITICAL_SECTION + data)\n- 0xBC8: Server callback function pointer offset\n- 0x854: Server-wide client count lock offset\n- 0x880: Active client count offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
