      "name": "ProcessClientMessages",
      "signature": "void ProcessClientMessages(void * pServer, uint * pClient)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes incoming client messages in a loop, handling rate limiting and message queuing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call message parser callback at pServer+0xBC0 to extract messages from client buffer\n2. Based on return code: 2=process msg, 3=done, 4=error disconnect, 5=continue\n3. Apply rate limiting: if bytes > 1000, check IP against CIDR allow list\n4. Allocate message buffer from pool (pServer+0x878) or create new (0x5C0 bytes)\n5. Copy message data from client buffer and enqueue to message list\n\nParameters:\n- pServer (void*): Server context structure\n- pClient (uint*): Client connection structure with message buffer at +0x90\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xBC0: Offset to message parser callback pointer\n- 0x5C0 (1472): Size of message buffer allocation\n- 0x3E8 (1000): Rate limit threshold in bytes\n- 0xC8 (200): Rate decay amount per second\n- 0x5B4 (1460): READ_BUFFER_SIZE maximum\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6ff65cc0: Disconnect client with reason code\n- FUN_6ff72470: Memory move for buffer compaction",
