      "name": "SendClientData",
      "signature": "int SendClientData(uint * pClientMgr, uint dwClientId, void * pvData, uint dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Sends data to a connected client via the network manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for custom dispatch callback at offset 0xbcc (protocol modes 1 or 2)\n2. If callback exists, invoke it directly with data size and return its result\n3. Hash client ID to locate bucket in hash table (mask at offset 0x0c)\n4. Enter critical section for thread-safe bucket access\n5. Search linked list at bucket for entry matching client ID\n6. Leave critical section after search completes\n7. If entry found and not marked as disconnected (offset 0x0c == 0):\n   - Sync mode (*pClientMgr == 0): Call direct send via FUN_6ff66530\n   - Async mode: Queue data via FUN_6ff67360 for deferred transmission\n8. Return 0 if client not found or is disconnected\n\nParameters:\n- pClientMgr (uint*): Client manager structure pointer\n- dwClientId (uint): Unique client identifier/hash key\n- pvData (void*): Pointer to data buffer to send\n- dwDataSize (uint): Size of data in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful send or queue\n- 0 if client not found, disconnected, or send failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x21b (539): Protocol mode field (1=mode1, 2=mode2)\n- 0x2f3 (755): Custom dispatch callback pointer\n- 0x18 (24): Critical section entry size/stride\n- 0x0c: Client entry disconnect status field",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:52a0dd72a38325233b4d111bea1df32a",
