      "name": "HashTableLookupValue",
      "signature": "uint HashTableLookupValue(void * pHashTable, uint dwKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Looks up a value in a thread-safe hash table by key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute bucket index by masking key with table's bitmask (offset 0xC)\n2. Lock the bucket's critical section (offset 0x1C + index * 0x18)\n3. Walk the linked list at bucket array (offset 0x14 + index * 4)\n4. Compare each entry's key (offset 0x0) against dwKey\n5. If found, return value at entry offset 0x18; else return 0\n6. Unlock critical section before returning\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (void*): Hash table structure with:\n  - 0x0C: Bitmask for bucket calculation\n  - 0x14: Pointer to bucket array (linked list heads)\n  - 0x1C: Pointer to critical section array (stride 0x18)\n- dwKey (uint): Key to search for\n\nReturns:\n- Value stored at entry+0x18 if key found, 0 if not found\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): Critical section structure stride\n- 0x0C, 0x14, 0x1C: Hash table structure field offsets",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
