      "name": "DestroyClientContext",
      "signature": "void DestroyClientContext(void * pClient)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys a client context structure and frees all associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section at offset 0x2c\n2. Call cleanup stubs for resources at offsets 0x8 and 0x4 if non-null\n3. Walk linked list at offset 0x74, freeing each node via Ordinal_10043\n4. Clear list head pointer\n5. Delete the critical section\n6. Free the client structure itself via Ordinal_10043\n\nParameters:\n- pClient (void*): Pointer to client context structure to destroy\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nStructure Layout:\n- +0x04: Resource pointer (cleaned via NullStubProc)\n- +0x08: Resource pointer (cleaned via NullStubProc)\n- +0x2c: CRITICAL_SECTION\n- +0x74: Linked list head (nodes have next ptr at +0x4)",
