      "name": "GetHackListSize",
      "signature": "void GetHackListSize(void * pQServer, char * szFile, int nLine)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Returns hack list size for debugging purposes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if hack list size field (offset 0xBD0) is non-zero\n2. If non-zero, call debug logging stub with:\n   - Category \"HACK\"\n   - Format string with file/line info\n   - Server internal value (offset 0x890)\n   - Caller file name and line number\n\nParameters:\n- pQServer (void*): QS server context structure\n  - Offset 0x890: Internal server value used in debug output\n  - Offset 0xBD0: Hack list size counter\n- szFile (char*): Source file name (debug, ignored in release)\n- nLine (int): Source line number (debug, ignored in release)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Export ordinal 10167\n- Debug stub is NullStubProc (no-op in release build)\n- Uses __stdcall convention with 3 parameters (RET 0xC)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:022b43cd1cfacde9c75907c9a48c99e9",
