      "name": "HashTableSetValue",
      "signature": "void HashTableSetValue(FogHashTable * pHashTable, uint dwKey, uint dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a value for a key in a thread-safe hash table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return early if key is 0 (invalid)\n2. Compute bucket index: (hashMask & key)\n3. Lock bucket's critical section\n4. Walk linked list searching for matching key\n5. Unlock critical section\n6. If entry found, set entry[8] (offset 0x20) to value\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTable (FogHashTable*): Hash table structure\n- dwKey (uint): Key to look up (0 is invalid)\n- dwValue (uint): Value to store at entry offset 0x20\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): Critical section stride\n- 0x20 (32): Value offset in entry (element[8])",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:fc72d054cea08c5e0defe5eade6bcfb5",
