      "name": "CheckIpInBlockList",
      "signature": "bool CheckIpInBlockList(void * this, uint dwIpAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if an IP address matches any entry in the block list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get entry count from this+0x848\n2. Loop through entries at this+0x4c (8-byte stride)\n3. Apply CIDR netmask lookup via g_adwCidrNetmasks[prefixLen]\n4. Compare masked IP with stored network address\n\nParameters:\n- this (void*): Block list object (entries at +0x4c, count at +0x848)\n- dwIpAddress (uint): IP address to check (network byte order)\n\nReturns:\n- true if IP matches any block list entry\n- false if no match found\n\nStructure Layout (each entry is 8 bytes):\n  +0x00: Network address (masked IP)\n  +0x04: CIDR prefix length index into g_adwCidrNetmasks",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:6eb2ca7045932473a93446ad6f346f71",
