      "name": "SignalAndCloseWorkerThreads",
      "signature": "void SignalAndCloseWorkerThreads(int * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Signals worker threads to terminate and closes their handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Lock critical section at pContext+0x854\n2. Collect up to 8 thread handles from primary array at +0xbd8\n3. Set termination flag (offset+0x20=1) for each primary thread\n4. If secondary mode enabled (+0xc18), collect handles from +0x44 offset\n5. Set termination flag (offset+0x64=1) for secondary threads\n6. Unlock critical section\n7. Wait up to 1000ms for all collected threads to terminate\n8. Close all primary thread handles and clear slots\n9. Close secondary handles if mode enabled\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (int*): Network context structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x854: Critical section offset in context\n- 0xbd8: Primary thread handle array base\n- 0xc18: Secondary mode flag offset\n- 0x20 (32): Stride to primary termination flag\n- 0x44 (68): Offset to secondary thread handle\n- 0x64 (100): Stride to secondary termination flag\n- 1000: WaitForMultipleObjects timeout in ms",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:52defcaf8f91fd263317628181b0caed",
