      "name": "AcceptConnectionsThreadProc",
      "signature": "uint AcceptConnectionsThreadProc(uint * pThreadParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Accept connections thread procedure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Logs thread startup with listen socket info\n2. Enters main accept loop with GetTickCount timing\n3. Calls select() to wait for incoming connections\n4. On timeout (0), sleeps 20ms and retries\n5. On socket ready, queries performance counter\n6. Accepts new connection via accept()\n7. Sets socket to non-blocking via ioctlsocket()\n8. Validates IP: CheckConnectionRateLimit, ValidateIpAgainstAllowList, CheckIpInBlockList\n9. If validation fails, adds IP to block cache and closes socket\n10. Creates client entry via QSrvAddClient\n11. Associates socket with I/O completion port\n12. Initiates async read via BeginClientRead\n13. Updates per-tick statistics\n14. Loops to accept next connection\n\nParameters:\n- pThreadParams (uint*): Pointer to [pServerContext, nListenerIndex] array\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on clean shutdown\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7D0 (2000): Max tick drift threshold (ms)\n- 0x8004667e: FIONBIO ioctl for non-blocking mode\n- 0x10: sockaddr_in size",
