      "name": "ReadThreadProc",
      "signature": "dword ReadThreadProc(ReadThreadContext * pThreadContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Read thread procedure for processing I/O completion port events.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - thread entry point invoked by CreateThread\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract pServer and nChannelIdx from thread context structure\n2. Free the thread context allocation (no longer needed after extraction)\n3. Assert readInThread flag is enabled at offset 0xC18 in server struct\n4. Log thread startup message with channel index\n5. Loop while shutdown flag at offset 0xC3C + nChannelIdx*4 is 0:\n   - Call ProcessCompletionPortEvents with 50ms timeout to handle I/O\n6. Enter critical section at server offset 0x854\n7. Clear shutdown flag to 0 to acknowledge termination request\n8. Leave critical section\n9. Return 1 indicating successful completion\n\nParameters:\n- pThreadContext (ReadThreadContext*): Pointer to 8-byte context structure:\n  - pServer (void*): Server context pointer at offset 0x00\n  - nChannelIdx (int): Channel index 0-3 at offset 0x04\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success after clean shutdown\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x29B: Source line number for ReleasePoolAllocation call\n- 0x29C: Source line number for readInThread assertion\n- 0x2A3: Source line number for EnterCriticalSection call\n- 0x32 (50): Timeout in milliseconds for ProcessCompletionPortEvents\n- 0x854: Offset to critical section in server structure\n- 0xC18: Offset to readInThread enable flag in server structure\n- 0xC3C: Offset to per-channel shutdown flags array in server\n\nThread Lifecycle:\n- Created by CreateListenSocket when readInThread flag is set in server config\n- Runs continuously until shutdown flag is set by another thread\n- Complements AcceptConnectionsThreadProc for asynchronous network I/O\n- Uses IOCP for efficient overlapped I/O event processing",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
