      "name": "SendClientQueuedData",
      "signature": "bool SendClientQueuedData(void * pServerCtx, uint * pClient)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Sends queued data buffer to client via WriteFile.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if send buffer exists (offset 0x74)\n2. Increment client ref count during operation\n3. Validate socket handle != INVALID_HANDLE\n4. Call WriteFile with overlapped I/O\n5. On success or IO_PENDING (0x3E5): set flag 0x4 and return 1\n6. On failure: release ref, disconnect client, return 0\n\nParameters:\n- pServerCtx (void*): Server context pointer\n- pClient (uint*): Client structure with socket at 0x10, send buffer at 0x74\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success or I/O pending\n- 0 on write failure (client disconnected)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3E5 (997): ERROR_IO_PENDING\n- 0x4: Write pending flag (offset 0x70)\n- 0x74: Send buffer pointer offset\n- 0x10: Socket handle offset",
