      "name": "LogOutOfMemoryStatus",
      "signature": "void LogOutOfMemoryStatus(uint dwUnused, SIZE_T nTotalPhys, SIZE_T nAvailPhys, SIZE_T nTotalPage, SIZE_T nAvailPage, SIZE_T nTotalVirt, SIZE_T nAvailVirt)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Logs memory status information when out-of-memory error occurs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x1040 bytes of stack space for MEMORYSTATUS and buffers\n2. Formats timestamp and log header\n3. Outputs \"ERROR: Out of memory!\" message\n4. Calls GlobalMemoryStatus to get current memory info\n5. Formats and logs total/available physical, page file, and virtual memory\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused (uint): Unused parameter\n- nTotalPhys (SIZE_T): Total physical memory bytes\n- nAvailPhys (SIZE_T): Available physical memory bytes\n- nTotalPage (SIZE_T): Total page file bytes\n- nAvailPage (SIZE_T): Available page file bytes\n- nTotalVirt (SIZE_T): Total virtual memory bytes\n- nAvailVirt (SIZE_T): Available virtual memory bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FormatInt64WithCommas: Formats memory sizes with comma separators\n- Ordinal_10030: Log output function\n- GlobalMemoryStatus: Win32 API for memory info",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:30d20bcb5ae96378c7deb9abd9fa1b63",
