      "name": "AllocPoolMemory",
      "signature": "void * AllocPoolMemory(int * pPool, int nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a pool using size-class buckets and bitmaps.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Use default pool if pPool is NULL\n2. Initialize memory subsystem if not already done (Ordinal_10142)\n3. If pool disabled (*pPool != 0), use direct malloc + 4-byte header\n4. Calculate size class using BSR (bit scan reverse) for log2\n5. If size exceeds max pool class, fall back to direct malloc\n6. Otherwise select bucket from pool, lock critical section\n7. Find/allocate PoolBlock with free slots using bitmap scan\n8. Mark slot as used in bitmap, return pointer to slot\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (int*): Memory pool context (NULL = default pool)\n- nSize (int): Allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated memory on success\n- NULL on allocation failure (error logged)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3ff (1023): Hash mask for malloc tracking table\n- 0x30 (48): PoolBucket stride (sizeof PoolBucket)\n- 0x18 (24): PoolBlock header size\n- 0x1f (31): Bits per DWORD minus 1 for bitmap calculations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:1d90f190d6c54308df7c4fc6d8b6fc96",
