      "name": "PoolReallocateInternal",
      "signature": "byte * PoolReallocateInternal(int * pMemPool, byte * pbSrcBuffer, int nNewSize, dword dwParam4, byte * pbParam5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Reallocates memory within a memory pool, handling size expansion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Use default pool (g_pDefaultMemPool) if pMemPool is NULL\n2. If pbSrcBuffer is NULL, allocate new memory via AllocPoolMemory\n3. Enter critical section and binary search chunk list for containing chunk\n4. If no chunk found or ptr below chunk base, use PoolHashReallocEntry\n5. Calculate slot index from (ptr - chunk_base) / slot_size\n6. If new size fits in existing slot, return original buffer\n7. Otherwise allocate new buffer, copy data (DWORD then byte aligned), free old\n\nParameters:\n- pMemPool (int*): Memory pool structure, NULL uses default pool\n- pbSrcBuffer (byte*): Existing buffer to reallocate, NULL for new alloc\n- nNewSize (int): Requested new buffer size in bytes\n- dwParam4 (dword): Tracking flags passed to subfunctions\n- pbParam5 (byte*): Additional tracking parameter\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to reallocated buffer on success\n- Calls fatal error handler (FUN_6ff71ca1) on allocation failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:e9e3d143748a076d75352645a0c76ae0",
