      "name": "FreeUnusedPoolBlocks",
      "signature": "void FreeUnusedPoolBlocks(MemPool * pPool)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Iterates through all pool sections and frees blocks with zero reference count.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Default to g_pDefaultMemPool if pPool is NULL\n2. Lock pool critical section\n3. For each section (0x30 bytes stride):\n   a. Lock section critical section\n   b. Walk block linked list from head\n   c. If block refcount (offset 0x8) == 0:\n      - Unlink from doubly-linked list (prev at 0xC, next at 0x10)\n      - Update head/tail pointers if necessary\n      - Decrement section block count\n      - Binary search block in sorted address list\n      - Remove from address list via memmove\n      - Update pool overhead stats at offset 0x102C\n      - Free block memory and header\n   d. Unlock section\n4. Unlock pool\n\nParameters:\n- pPool (MemPool*): Memory pool to compact, or NULL for default pool\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x30 (48): Pool section structure stride\n- 0x1C: Offset to section count in pool\n- 0x20: Offset to section array pointer\n- 0x24: Offset to block count in pool\n- 0x2C: Offset to block address list\n- 0x102C: Offset to pool overhead statistics",
