      "name": "InitInterlockSystem",
      "signature": "void InitInterlockSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the interlocked read/write system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize g_csInterlock critical section\n2. Test OsInterlockedWrite with value 0x29a (666)\n3. Test OsInterlockedRead to verify write succeeded\n4. If test fails, assert with error and exit\n5. Store current timestamp in g_qwInitTimestamp\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x29a (666): Test value for interlock verification\n- 0x3c (60): Source line number for assertion",
