      "name": "GetUptimeSeconds",
      "signature": "int GetUptimeSeconds(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Returns elapsed seconds since initialization timestamp.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current tick count via GetTickCount()\n2. Atomically read 64-bit timestamp (total seconds + last tick)\n3. If elapsed > 30000ms (30s), refresh timestamp:\n   a. Re-assert current thread priority (THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN check)\n   b. Recalculate Unix timestamp via FUN_6ff72d9a\n   c. Atomically update g_qwInitTimestamp with new values\n4. Return total seconds + (elapsed ticks / 1000)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Elapsed seconds since initialization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7530 (30000): 30 second refresh threshold in milliseconds\n- 0x7FFFFFFF: THREAD_PRIORITY_ERROR_RETURN sentinel\n- 1000: Milliseconds to seconds divisor",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
