      "name": "GetFreeDiskSpace",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetFreeDiskSpace(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Returns free disk space in bytes for the current working directory's drive.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current directory path via Ordinal_10115 (GetCurrentDirectory)\n2. Load kernel32.dll and try to get GetDiskFreeSpaceExA\n3. If GetDiskFreeSpaceExA available:\n   - Call it to get 64-bit free bytes available\n   - Return the FreeBytesAvailableToCaller value\n4. Fallback to GetDiskFreeSpaceA:\n   - Truncate path to root (find first backslash)\n   - Get sectors/cluster, bytes/sector, free clusters\n   - Return freeClusters * bytesPerSector * sectorsPerCluster\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- ulonglong: Free bytes available on disk\n- 0 on failure (kernel32 load failed)\n\nNote: dwLowDWord is a decompiler artifact - EBX is zeroed via XOR at 0x6ff69613.\nThe Ex path returns adDiskParams[1:2] (FreeBytesAvailableToCaller) via EAX:EDX.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:15d5448f67d211ccd91694c33f3cbe79",
