      "name": "ParseExcelTabDelimitedData",
      "signature": "int * ParseExcelTabDelimitedData(char * szData, int nDataLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Parses tab-delimited Excel-style data into a tracking structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 16-byte parse state structure\n2. Scan data for tab (0x09) and CR+LF (0x0D 0x0A) delimiters\n3. Replace tabs with null terminators, count cells\n4. Validate CR must be followed by LF (SYM_EOL check)\n5. On first CR+LF, store pointer to second row data\n6. Check for \"Expansion\" header and remove if present\n7. Continue parsing remaining rows\n\nParameters:\n- szData (char*): Tab-delimited text buffer (modified in-place)\n- nDataLen (int): Length of data buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to parse state structure on success\n- NULL if no valid row data found\n\nStructure Layout (returned pointer):\n| Offset | Type | Description           |\n|--------|------|-----------------------|\n| 0x00   | ptr  | Data start pointer    |\n| 0x04   | ptr  | First data row ptr    |\n| 0x08   | int  | Row count (after hdr) |\n| 0x0C   | int  | Column/cell count     |\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Parse state structure size\n- 0x09: Tab character (cell delimiter)\n- 0x0D 0x0A: CR+LF (row delimiter)\n- 0x118 (280): Maximum cell count limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ad934869f83d794df2909b624f0ec244",
