      "name": "PopulateExcelTableFromText",
      "signature": "void PopulateExcelTableFromText(uint dwFileSize, void * pTxtData, void * pExcelIndex, void * pOutputBuffer, uint dwRowStride)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Populates an Excel table structure from parsed tab-delimited text data.\nConverts text columns to typed values based on Excel column type definitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (dwFileSize > 0, dwRowStride > 0)\n2. Allocate hash table (0x400 entries) on stack via AllocaStackProbe\n3. Build hash lookup of column name strings from pExcelIndex\n4. For each row in text data (delimited by 0x0A newlines):\n   a. Parse column values separated by null terminators\n   b. Compute hash index from column name string\n   c. Look up column definition in hash chain\n   d. Convert value based on column type:\n      - EXCEL_TYPE=0x0A (10): DWORD value\n      - EXCEL_TYPE=0x0C (12): BYTE value\n      - EXCEL_TYPE=0x0E (14): WORD value\n      - EXCEL_TYPE=0x0F (15): 32-char string to numeric\n      - EXCEL_TYPE=0x10 (16): 4-char code to DWORD\n5. Write converted values to pOutputBuffer at row offset\n6. Advance output pointer by dwRowStride for each row\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileSize (uint): Size of the text file data in bytes\n- pTxtData (void*): Pointer to metadata with row/column counts at offsets +0x4, +0x8, +0xC\n- pExcelIndex (void*): Pointer to Excel column definitions, stride 0x14 per entry\n- pOutputBuffer (void*): Destination buffer for typed table data\n- dwRowStride (uint): Byte offset between consecutive rows in output\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; populates pOutputBuffer with converted data\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x400 (1024): Hash table size for column name lookup\n- 0x138C (5004): Stack frame size for local storage\n- 0x14 (20): Excel column definition entry stride\n- 0x118 (280): Maximum indexed columns before assert\n- 0x7FFF: Sentinel marking unmapped column index\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InsertStringIndexNode: Builds sorted string tree for lookups\n- InsertSortedIndexEntry: Inserts into binary search tree\n- ToUpperInPlace: Normalizes column name case\n- AllocaStackProbe: Allocates stack space with guard page check",
