      "name": "InsertStringIndexNode",
      "signature": "void InsertStringIndexNode(StringIndexNode * * ppRoot, StringIndexNode * pNewNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Inserts a node into a binary search tree keyed by string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If tree is empty, set root to new node and return\n2. Compare new node's key with current node using strcmp\n3. If less, traverse left subtree; if greater, traverse right\n4. If equal (duplicate key), free the new node and return\n5. Repeat until insertion point found, then link new node\n\nParameters:\n- ppRoot (StringIndexNode**): Pointer to tree root or child pointer\n- pNewNode (StringIndexNode*): Node to insert (0x2c bytes, key at offset 0)\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies tree in place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24: Offset to pLeft child pointer\n- 0x28: Offset to pRight child pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10216: Allocates node and calls this to insert",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
