      "name": "ShutdownAsyncData",
      "signature": "void ShutdownAsyncData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Shuts down the async data system and releases all resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if async event array exists, if not just clear enabled flag\n2. Iterate through all async events (stride 0xC, up to g_nAsyncEventCount)\n3. For each valid event handle, call CloseHandle and zero the entry\n4. Call ReleasePoolAllocation to free memory pool\n5. Zero all async data globals (array ptr, count, enabled flag)\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitAsyncData (Ordinal 10089): Initialization counterpart",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:a2aea5392e96e425e61cc4384186c232",
