      "name": "CompleteAsyncOperation",
      "signature": "void CompleteAsyncOperation(int * pAsyncData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Completes an async operation, resetting event and freeing resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if operation already completed (flag 0x1 in dwFlags)\n2. If event handle exists, reset it and mark as signaled\n3. Release any file handle via Ordinal_10103\n4. Set completion flag in dwFlags\n5. If pending buffer exists, free current buffer and swap in pending\n\nParameters:\n- pAsyncData (int*): Pointer to async data structure (magic 0x41737960)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Layout (offsets in dwords):\n- [0x00]: File handle\n- [0x04]: Pool handle\n- [0x1C-0x38]: Buffer region (7 dwords, cleared on completion)\n- [0x30]: Pending buffer address\n- [0x34]: Pending buffer size\n- [0x38]: Event handle structure\n- [0x3C]: Current buffer address\n- [0x40]: Current buffer size\n- [0x48]: Flags (bit 0 = completed)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10093: Wait for async completion\n- Ordinal_10103: Release file handle",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:08764863ea6831a4d9a54f7fda5bacb8",
