      "name": "AllocAsyncEvent",
      "signature": "void * AllocAsyncEvent(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates an async event structure from the global pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if async system is enabled (g_fAsyncEnabled)\n2. Scan existing events for one with pending flag set, return if found\n3. Wait on each event handle (timeout=0) to find signaled event\n4. If signaled, process via helper and return that event slot\n5. If pool not full (<0x400), create new event via CreateEventA\n6. Return NULL if disabled or pool exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global async event pool)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to 12-byte event structure (HANDLE, flag, param)\n- NULL if async disabled or pool full (0x400 max)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xC (12): Event structure stride (HANDLE + flag + param)\n- 0x400 (1024): Maximum async event pool size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:acce3f75ad7422b343bda7714c8498a0",
