      "name": "PostponeAsyncDataPriorityChanges",
      "signature": "void PostponeAsyncDataPriorityChanges(int nEnter)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Controls deferral of async data priority changes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nEnter != 0, increment g_nAsyncPendingCount (enter defer mode)\n2. If nEnter == 0, decrement count\n3. If count reaches zero, process pending list:\n   - Iterate g_pAsyncPendingList linked via offset 0x50\n   - For each entry where priority differs from saved, call Ordinal_282\n   - Clear pending flag and reset saved priority fields\n4. Assert if decrementing when count is already zero\n\nParameters:\n- nEnter (int): Non-zero to enter defer mode, zero to exit\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c: AsyncData heap handle offset\n- 0x44: AsyncData current priority offset\n- 0x48: AsyncData flags offset (bit 3 = pending change)\n- 0x4c: AsyncData saved priority offset\n- 0x50: AsyncData next pending pointer offset",
