      "name": "FreeAsyncData",
      "signature": "void FreeAsyncData(int * pAsyncData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Frees an async data structure and all associated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pAsyncData pointer is non-null\n2. Validate async data magic number (0x41737960 = \"Asy`\")\n3. If flagged as pending (flag 0x8), unlink from g_pAsyncPendingList\n4. If not yet completed (flag 0x1 not set), wait for operation to finish\n5. If buffer allocated (flag 0x2 set), free the buffer via FreePoolMemoryTracked\n6. Free the async data structure itself\n\nParameters:\n- pAsyncData (int*): Pointer to async data structure to free\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x41737960: Async data signature (ASCII \"Asy`\" with high nibble flags)\n- 0x1: ASYNC_FLAG_COMPLETE - operation finished\n- 0x2: ASYNC_FLAG_BUFFER_ALLOCATED - buffer needs freeing\n- 0x8: ASYNC_FLAG_PENDING - in pending list\n\nStructure Layout (pAsyncData offsets):\n- 0x04: Pool ID for memory tracking\n- 0x38: Pointer to event handle structure\n- 0x3C: Buffer pointer\n- 0x48: Flags (low nibble=magic, high nibble=state flags)\n- 0x50: Next pointer in pending list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
