      "name": "InitHuffmanDecodeTables",
      "signature": "void InitHuffmanDecodeTables(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes Huffman decode table buffers and builds decode tables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Zero first two DWORDs of source buffer (g_adwHuffmanSrc)\n2. Copy 0x1fe (510) DWORDs from source to destination buffer\n3. Zero four Huffman state globals\n4. Tail-call BuildHuffmanDecodeTables with static bit lengths table\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global state only)\n\nReturns:\n- void (state stored in globals)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1fe (510): DWORD count to copy (2040 bytes)\n- 0x6ff822d0: Static bit lengths table address",
