      "name": "PrintCpuInfo",
      "signature": "void PrintCpuInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Detects and prints CPU identification information using CPUID instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global platform flag for special cases (values 3 or 4)\n2. Execute CPUID(0) to get vendor string\n3. Compare vendor to GenuineIntel, AuthenticAMD, CyrixInstead\n4. Execute CPUID(1) to get version info (family, model, stepping, type)\n5. Based on vendor and version, select processor name string\n6. Print formatted CPU info via Ordinal_10029\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Platform type check for early return\n- 0x4: Platform type check for early return\n- 0x1: Intel vendor code (internal)\n- 0x2: AMD vendor code (internal)\n- 0x3: Cyrix vendor code (internal)\n\nCPU Family/Model Detection:\n- Intel: Pentium, Pentium MMX, Pentium Pro/II/III, Celeron, Pentium 4\n- AMD: K5, K6, K6-2, K6-3, Athlon, Duron\n- Cyrix: MediaGX, 6x86, M2\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10029: Print formatted string\n- cpuid_basic_info: CPUID leaf 0\n- cpuid_Version_info: CPUID leaf 1",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
