      "name": "CreateStringPool",
      "signature": "int * CreateStringPool(char * szPoolName, int nElemSize, int nMaxElems)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a string pool structure for managing named data elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total size: header (0x120 bytes) + data area (nElemSize * nMaxElems)\n2. Allocate memory via FogMemAlloc\n3. Zero-initialize the 0x120-byte header (0x48 DWORDs)\n4. Copy pool name string (max 0x100 chars) into header\n5. Store element size, max count, and data pointer in header fields\n6. Initialize current count to 0\n\nParameters:\n- szPoolName (char*): Name string for the pool (up to 256 chars)\n- nElemSize (int): Size in bytes of each element\n- nMaxElems (int): Maximum number of elements the pool can hold\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated pool structure on success\n- NULL (0) on allocation failure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Field\n  0x000   szName[0x100] - Pool name string\n  0x100   nElemSize     - Element size\n  0x104   nMaxElems     - Max element count\n  0x108   nCurCount     - Current count (init 0)\n  0x11c   pDataArea     - Pointer to data (offset 0x120)\n  0x120   Data area starts here",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:1e34e8a3cbb6e15a51d0a6d55425848e",
