      "name": "DataArrayRemoveEntry",
      "signature": "void DataArrayRemoveEntry(void * pDataArray, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes an entry from a data array structure by clearing it and updating bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get slot via Ordinal_10067 using index, assert if not found\n2. Clear slot value to 0\n3. Extract row index from high 16 bits of nIndex\n4. Update nMinRow if this row is lower than current minimum\n5. If this was nMaxRow, scan backwards to find new max (first non-zero slot)\n6. Decrement nEntryCount\n\nParameters:\n- pDataArray (void*): Data array structure\n- nIndex (int): Combined index (low16=key/version, high16=row)\n\nReturns:\n- void (asserts on invalid index via FogAssert)\n\nStructure Offsets:\n- 0x104: nRowStride (bytes per row)\n- 0x10C: nMinRow (minimum active row)\n- 0x110: nMaxRow (maximum active row) \n- 0x114: nEntryCount (active entries)\n- 0x11C: pData (array pointer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:1b39623e29d407472e349bf338072514",
