      "name": "ValidateCriticalSection",
      "signature": "void ValidateCriticalSection(uint * pCritSect)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates critical section structure integrity for debug builds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If debug flag (DAT_6ffa0708) disabled, return immediately\n2. Check DebugInfo pointer (pCritSect[0]): non-null, aligned, valid range\n3. Check LockCount (pCritSect[1]): <= 10 or -1 (unlocked)\n4. Check RecursionCount (pCritSect[2]): <= 10\n5. Verify OwningThread matches, LockSemaphore and SpinCount valid\n6. If any check fails, log error and terminate process\n\nParameters:\n- pCritSect (uint*): Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n\nReturns:\n- void (terminates process on validation failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fffffff: Maximum valid pointer address\n- 0x3: Pointer alignment mask (must be 0)\n- 10: Maximum reasonable lock/recursion count\n- 0x18: Size of validation data logged\n- 0x20: Size of debug info logged",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:e727c8dc688ebb9fadb5f64a8c47cad7",
