      "name": "DebugPrintf",
      "signature": "void DebugPrintf(uint dwFlags, char * szFormat, ...)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper for OutputDebugMessage that converts stdcall params to register convention.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load dwFlags from stack to ECX\n2. Load szFormat from stack to EDX\n3. Push varargs pointer (ESP+0xc)\n4. Call OutputDebugMessage\n\nParameters:\n- dwFlags (uint): Output flags controlling behavior\n- szFormat (char*): Printf-style format string\n- ... (varargs): Format arguments\n\nFlag Bits (dwFlags):\n- 0x01: Write to log file\n- 0x02: Suppress OutputDebugStringA\n- 0x04: Prepend timestamp (HH:MM:SS.mmm)\n- 0x18: Check Caps Lock state\n\nReturns:\n- void (return value from OutputDebugMessage is discarded)",
