      "name": "HandleCriticalException",
      "signature": "int HandleCriticalException(dword dwExceptionCode, dword dwExceptionFlags, void * pExceptionAddr, HMODULE hModule, dword dwExceptionInfo0, dword dwExceptionInfo1, word wReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Handles critical CPU exceptions and displays crash information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire exception handler lock via InterlockedIncrement on g_nExceptionLock\n2. If lock already held (non-zero), skip to decrement and return\n3. Set g_fExceptionActive flag to 1 to indicate crash handling\n4. Register WriteLogHeader callback for exception logging\n5. Map NTSTATUS exception code to human-readable string via switch\n6. Use FormatMessageA on NTDLL for unknown exception codes\n7. Query VirtualQuery to identify module containing fault address\n8. Parse PE headers to identify section within module\n9. Log exception details via Ordinal_10030 (format string logging)\n10. Log CPU register state (EAX-EDI, EIP, ESP) via Ordinal_10030\n11. Log stack memory dump (0x1000 bytes) via Ordinal_10032\n12. Log code memory at EIP (0x20 bytes) via Ordinal_10032\n13. Duplicate current thread handle for crash context\n14. Call crash callback g_dwFogParam2 if registered\n15. Build message box strings with Ordinal_578 (SStrPrintf)\n16. Display MessageBoxA with MB_ICONEXCLAMATION to user\n17. Release exception handler lock via InterlockedDecrement\n\nParameters:\n- dwExceptionCode (dword): NTSTATUS exception code (e.g. 0xC0000005)\n- dwExceptionFlags (dword): Exception flags (continuable/non-continuable)\n- pExceptionAddr (void*): Address where exception occurred\n- hModule (HMODULE): Module handle for context\n- dwExceptionInfo0 (dword): Additional info (access address for AV)\n- dwExceptionInfo1 (dword): Additional info (read/write flag for AV)\n- wReserved (word): Reserved parameter\n- IMPLICIT: in_stack_00001330 = EXCEPTION_POINTERS* from SEH chain\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns 1 (exception handled by this filter)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5A4D: DOS MZ header signature\n- 0x4550: PE signature\n- 0x0A00: FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_HMODULE | FORMAT_MESSAGE_FROM_SYSTEM\n- 0x1000: Stack dump size (4KB)\n- 0x20: Code context dump size (32 bytes)\n- 0x30: MB_ICONEXCLAMATION | MB_SETFOREGROUND",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4de3b80db0a5833c3b0778fc2e7a52ec",
