      "name": "CheckExceptionReentrance",
      "signature": "int CheckExceptionReentrance(char * szSourceFile, int nLineNumber, char * szExpression)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if error handling is already active and logs a nested exception warning.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_fExceptionActive flag is set (already handling an error)\n2. If active, log \"ENCOUNTERED ERROR DURING ERROR HANDLING\" via Ordinal_10030\n3. Return 1 to indicate reentrance detected (caller should skip processing)\n4. Return 0 if no active exception (safe to proceed with error handling)\n\nParameters:\n- szSourceFile (char*): Source filename for assert logging\n- nLineNumber (int): Line number for assert logging\n- szExpression (char*): Expression/message for assert logging\n- NOTE: Parameters passed through to logging but unused in reentrance check\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Reentrance detected (error handling already in progress)\n- 0: No active exception (safe to proceed)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10028: Main error handler that calls this function\n- Ordinal_10030: Logging function called on reentrance detection",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
