      "name": "DisplayErrorMessageBox",
      "signature": "void DisplayErrorMessageBox(byte * pbFormat, dword * pdwFormatArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Displays an error message dialog box with formatted error details.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x3100 bytes of stack space for message buffers\n2. Write log header entry\n3. If no format string, assert error and terminate\n4. Format the error message with vsprintf into buffer\n5. Copy formatted message to intermediate buffer\n6. Build window title with error type prefix\n7. Append newline suffix to message\n8. Log message to context\n9. Show MessageBoxA with MB_ICONEXCLAMATION (0x30)\n\nParameters:\n- pbFormat (byte*): Format string for error message (via stack at 0x3108)\n- pdwFormatArgs (dword*): Varargs pointer for format (via stack at 0x310c)\n- IMPLICIT: ECX contains error type index used for title lookup\n- IMPLICIT: EDX contains flag indicating extended error info\n\nReturns:\n- void (does not return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3100: Total stack allocation for message buffers\n- 0x1000: Individual buffer size (4KB)\n- 0x30: MB_ICONEXCLAMATION flag for MessageBoxA\n- 0x6c0 (1728): Line number in ErrorManager.cpp\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10028 (ReportExceptionContext): Primary caller\n- FUN_6ff72fbe: vsprintf variant for formatting",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:dbf5b745bb0b04927e74b2f845c6f89d",
