      "name": "StackWalkThreadProc",
      "signature": "dword StackWalkThreadProc(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Stack walk thread procedure for generating stack traces of target threads.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Wait on g_hStackWalkEvent for stack walk requests\n2. If wait fails or returns non-zero, clean up all handles and exit\n3. Assert if target thread equals this thread (can't stack walk self)\n4. Suspend target thread with SuspendThread\n5. Zero CONTEXT struct (0xB3 dwords = 716 bytes) and set ContextFlags = 0x10007\n6. Call GetThreadContext to capture thread state\n7. Call GenerateStackTraceReport with captured context\n8. Resume target thread, close handle, signal completion via g_hStackWalkDone\n\nParameters:\n- None (standard thread procedure, lpParameter unused)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on clean shutdown (wait failed or signaled to exit)\n- Never returns normally (asserts if target == self)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: INFINITE wait timeout\n- 0x10007: CONTEXT_FULL (CONTEXT_CONTROL | CONTEXT_INTEGER | CONTEXT_SEGMENTS)\n- 0xB3 (179): CONTEXT struct size in dwords (716 bytes)\n- 0xAA (170): Assert line number\n\nRelated Functions:\n- GenerateStackTraceReport: Called to process the captured CONTEXT",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3460c5c5a6f9115494b11d0ef4a1cdca",
