      "name": "IffCreate",
      "signature": "void * IffCreate(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new IFF (Interchange File Format) buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x400 (1024) bytes via Ordinal_401 (FogMemAlloc) with 8-byte alignment\n2. Writes \"BOND\" signature (0x444e4f42) to buffer start\n3. Returns pointer to allocated IFF buffer\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to newly allocated IFF buffer with \"BOND\" signature\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x400 (1024): IFF buffer size\n- 0x5a (90): Source line number (IFF.cpp)\n- 0x8: Memory alignment\n- 0x444e4f42: \"BOND\" signature (IFF format marker)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
