      "name": "LookupEntryByKey",
      "signature": "int LookupEntryByKey(int nKey, void * pTable, int * pnOutValue1, int * pnOutValue2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Searches a table for an entry matching the given key and returns associated values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if table has any entries (count at pTable+4)\n2. Iterate through entries starting at pTable+8 with 12-byte stride\n3. Compare each entry's key (offset +0) with search key\n4. If match found, write values at offsets +4 and +8 to output pointers\n5. Return 0 on success, 0x16 (EINVAL) if not found\n\nParameters:\n- nKey: Key value to search for\n- pTable: Pointer to lookup table (count at +4, entries at +8)\n- pnOutValue1: Output pointer for first value (entry offset +4)\n- pnOutValue2: Output pointer for second value (entry offset +8)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Entry found, values written to output pointers\n- 0x16 (22): Entry not found in table\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x16 (22): EINVAL error code indicating invalid argument\n- 0x0C (12): Entry stride size (key:4 + value1:4 + value2:4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:8eeeaccb9d000c5340d888b5bf43754b",
