      "name": "ShutdownLogManager",
      "signature": "void ShutdownLogManager(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Shuts down the LogManager subsystem and frees all queued messages.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set shutdown flag to signal worker thread\n2. Wait for worker thread to complete (30s timeout)\n3. Close thread handle\n4. Enter critical section\n5. Loop: free all queued log messages via SMemFree\n6. Clear all LogManager global state variables\n7. Leave critical section\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7530 (30000): Thread wait timeout in milliseconds\n- 0xFFFFFFFE (-2): SMemFree flags parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
