      "name": "LogWriterThreadProc",
      "signature": "dword LogWriterThreadProc(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Background thread entry point for asynchronous log message writing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop infinitely until shutdown flag set\n2. Lock log manager, dequeue one message from g_nLogMessageCount list\n3. Adjust linked list pointers and decrement counters\n4. Release lock, check shutdown timeout (15 seconds max wait)\n5. If message exists, lock log files and write:\n   - If hex dump flag (offset 0x2C), call WriteHexDumpToLog\n   - Else open/get log file, print timestamp, write message data\n6. Unlink and free the message node\n7. If not shutting down, sleep and call ManageLogFileRotation/CleanupOldBackupFiles\n\nParameters:\n- None (thread entry point)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on shutdown completion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3A98 (14999): Shutdown timeout in ms (15 seconds)\n- 0x32 (50): Sleep interval when queue empty\n- 0x38: Offset to message size in node\n- 0x2C: Offset to hex dump flag in node",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:8700f9e8bc88dd75d53696325ee2fd3e",
