      "name": "WriteHexDumpToLog",
      "signature": "void WriteHexDumpToLog(void * pLogContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Writes hex dump of memory region to log file with timestamp.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Opens or gets existing log file via OpenOrGetLogFile\n2. Gets current time and formats timestamp (HH:MM:SS.mmm)\n3. Iterates through data buffer in 16-byte chunks\n4. For each chunk:\n   a. Writes address line (%s%s%08X: or %s%s%04X:)\n   b. Validates memory with IsBadReadPtr\n   c. Formats hex bytes with spacing every 4 bytes\n   d. Appends ASCII representation (non-printable as '.')\n   e. Pads output to fixed width\n5. Writes formatted line to log via FUN_6ff7347f\n\nParameters:\n- pLogContext (void*): Log context structure containing:\n  - +0x18: Log filename string\n  - +0x2c: Pointer to data buffer\n  - +0x30: Size of data to dump\n  - +0x34: Address format flag (0=8-digit, 1=4-digit)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10 (16): Bytes per hex dump line\n- 0x20 (32): Max timestamp/padding length\n- 0x100 (256): Line buffer size\n- 0x7f: ASCII mask for printable test\n- 0x2e (46): Period char for non-printable\n\nRelated Functions:\n- OpenOrGetLogFile: Gets/creates log file handle\n- FUN_6ff7347f: Writes string to log with formatting\n- Ordinal_578: SStrPrintf - formatted string output\n- Ordinal_503: SStrConcat - string concatenation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:744c65e40de802c8e02230642f7eca2e",
