      "name": "CleanupOldBackupFiles",
      "signature": "void CleanupOldBackupFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleans up old d2*.txt backup files based on age.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if 24 hours (0x5265c00 ms = 86399999 ms) elapsed since last cleanup\n2. If interval passed: shutdown log files, refresh critical section\n3. Get current time and convert to FILETIME for age comparison\n4. Build search path: executable_dir + \"d2*.txt\" wildcard\n5. Iterate matching files, delete those older than threshold\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5265c00 (86399999): Milliseconds in ~24 hours minus 1ms\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH buffer size\n\nRelated Functions:\n- DeleteOldBackupFile: Checks file age and deletes if old\n- ShutdownLogFiles: Closes current log handles before cleanup",
