      "name": "CleanBackupFileByAge",
      "signature": "void CleanBackupFileByAge(_FILETIME * pCurrentTime, LPCSTR lpszFilePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Deletes backup files older than ~2.75 years based on embedded YYMMDD date in filename.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get string length via strlen (Ordinal_506)\n2. Parse date from last 6 chars before extension using format \"%2d%2d%2d\" (YYMMDD)\n3. Convert 2-digit year: Y < 91 => 2000+Y, else 1900+Y\n4. Build SYSTEMTIME and convert to FILETIME\n5. If file date is > 0x3ED (1005) FILETIME high units older than current time, delete\n\nParameters:\n- pCurrentTime (_FILETIME*): Current time for age comparison\n- lpszFilePath (LPCSTR): Full path to backup file with YYMMDD in name\n\nReturns:\n- void (file deleted if old enough)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 10: Offset from end to YYMMDD date portion\n- 0x5B (91): Y2K pivot year threshold\n- 0x76C (1900): Century base for years >= 91\n- 0x7D0 (2000): Century base for years < 91\n- 0x3ED (1005): Max age in FILETIME high units (~2.75 years)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:dba0c01f87159fff3b268de3f7945557",
