      "name": "UnlinkLogMessageListNodes",
      "signature": "void UnlinkLogMessageListNodes(LogMsgListCtrl * pList)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unlinks all nodes from a log message linked list structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to head node at pList->pHead\n2. Loop while pList->pCurrent pointer is positive (valid node)\n3. For each node with non-null forward pointer:\n   a. Get link offset from node[1]\n   b. If offset negative, use bitwise NOT for absolute address\n   c. Otherwise calculate relative address from backlink\n   d. Update target's forward pointer\n   e. Update forward node's backlink\n   f. Clear current node's pointers to zero\n4. After loop, unlink the head node using same offset logic\n5. Clear pList->pHead and pList->pCurrent to finalize cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- pList (LogMsgListCtrl*): Pointer to list control structure\n  - pHead: Head node pointer\n  - pCurrent: Current/tail node pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:fcb2acde869164cee4abdac9566309a1",
