      "name": "StartWinsockService",
      "signature": "bool StartWinsockService(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes Windows Sockets (Winsock) version 1.1 for network operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate WSADATA structure on stack (0x190 bytes)\n2. Call WSAStartup with version 0x101 (Winsock 1.1)\n3. Convert return value to boolean using NEG/SBB/INC sequence\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- true (1) if WSAStartup succeeded (returned 0)\n- false (0) if WSAStartup failed (returned non-zero error code)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x101: Winsock version 1.1 (MAKEWORD(1,1))\n- 0x190: sizeof(WSADATA) = 400 bytes",
