      "name": "CreateTcpConnection",
      "signature": "int * CreateTcpConnection(char * szHostAddress, ushort wPort, LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE pfnThreadProc, LPVOID pThreadParam, char * szConnectionName, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Creates a TCP connection to the specified host and port.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x78-byte connection state structure via FogMemAlloc\n2. Zero-initialize structure and copy connection name (max 0x40 chars)\n3. Initialize critical section for thread safety\n4. Call WSAStartup to initialize Winsock (version 1.1)\n5. Create TCP socket (AF_INET=2, SOCK_STREAM=1)\n6. Set socket options: TCP_NODELAY, SO_KEEPALIVE, SO_RCVTIMEO=3000ms\n7. If dwFlags & 1, set non-blocking mode via FIONBIO\n8. Connect to host:port, handle WSAEWOULDBLOCK (0x2733) for non-blocking\n9. Cache local IP address in g_szCachedLocalIP if not already set\n10. Create worker thread if pfnThreadProc provided\n\nParameters:\n- szHostAddress (char*): IP address string to connect to\n- wPort (ushort): TCP port number\n- pfnThreadProc (LPTHREAD_START_ROUTINE): Optional thread callback\n- pThreadParam (LPVOID): Parameter passed to thread callback\n- szConnectionName (char*): Descriptive name for connection (default \"UNKNOWN\")\n- dwFlags (uint): Bit 0 = non-blocking mode\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to connection state structure on success, NULL on failure\n\nStructure Layout (0x78 bytes):\n- +0x00: Connected flag (1 when connected)\n- +0x04: Connecting flag (1 during async connect)\n- +0x08: SOCKET handle\n- +0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION (0x18 bytes)\n- +0x24: Thread handle\n- +0x28: Thread ID\n- +0x30: Error code (1=WSAStartup, 2=socket, 3=connect)\n- +0x34: WSA error code\n- +0x38: Connection name (0x40 chars)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x78: Connection state structure size\n- 0x101: WSA version 1.1\n- 0xBB8 (3000): Socket receive timeout in ms\n- 0x2733 (10035): WSAEWOULDBLOCK error code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
