      "name": "GetLocalIPAddress",
      "signature": "char * GetLocalIPAddress(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Retrieves the local machine's IP address using Winsock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Winsock with WSAStartup(0x101)\n2. Get hostname via gethostname, then resolve via gethostbyname\n3. If hostname resolution fails, attempt UDP socket method:\n   - Create UDP socket (AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM)\n   - Connect to external IP 209.67.136.168:7 (echo service)\n   - Use getsockname to get local address bound by OS\n4. Format IP as dotted-decimal string via sprintf\n5. Cleanup Winsock and return pointer to static buffer\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to static buffer g_szCachedLocalIP containing IP string\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x101: Winsock version 1.1\n- 0x100 (256): Hostname buffer size\n- 2: AF_INET (address family)\n- 2: SOCK_DGRAM (UDP socket type)\n- 7: Echo protocol port\n- 0x10 (16): sizeof(sockaddr_in)",
