      "name": "ResolveHostnameToIP",
      "signature": "char * ResolveHostnameToIP(char * szHostname)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Resolves a hostname to a dotted-decimal IP address string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input is already an IP address using sscanf with %d.%d.%d.%d pattern\n2. If already IP (4 matches), return input directly\n3. Call gethostbyname to resolve hostname\n4. If Winsock not initialized (error 0x276d), initialize with WSAStartup(0x101), resolve, cleanup\n5. Convert resolved address via inet_ntoa and copy to global buffer\n\nParameters:\n- szHostname (char*): Hostname string or IP address to resolve\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to IP string (input if already IP, or g_szCachedLocalIP global buffer)\n- NULL if resolution fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x276d (10093): WSANOTINITIALISED error code\n- 0x101: Winsock version 1.1\n- 4: Expected match count for valid IP address format",
