      "name": "FormatVarArgsToBuffer",
      "signature": "int FormatVarArgsToBuffer(char * szBuffer, int nBufferSize, char * szFormat)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Formats a string with varargs into buffer with size limit (vsnprintf-like).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy buffer pointer to write context structure\n2. Set mode to 0x42 ('B' for buffered output)\n3. Store buffer size for limit tracking\n4. Call format processor FUN_6ff74762 with format string\n5. Decrement remaining size counter\n6. If size becomes negative, call unget handler FUN_6ff7464a\n7. Otherwise, null-terminate the output buffer\n8. Return character count from format processor\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Destination buffer for formatted string\n- nBufferSize (int): Maximum bytes to write including null\n- szFormat (char*): printf-style format string\n- IMPLICIT: Stack+0x10 contains varargs pointer\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of characters written (excluding null)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42 (66): Buffer mode flag ('B' for buffered output)",
