      "name": "ReadStreamData",
      "signature": "uint ReadStreamData(byte * pbDestBuf, uint dwElemSize, uint dwElemCount, int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Reads elements from a stream into a buffer (fread-like).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate total bytes to read (dwElemSize * dwElemCount)\n2. Return 0 immediately if total bytes is zero\n3. Determine buffer size from stream or use default 0x1000\n4. Loop while bytes remain:\n   a. If buffered data available, copy via memmove (FUN_6fdd74b0)\n   b. If remaining >= buffer size, read directly via FUN_6fdd72be\n   c. Otherwise read single byte via FUN_6fdd71a6\n5. On EOF or error, set stream error flag (0x20)\n6. Return count of complete elements read\n\nParameters:\n- pbDestBuf (byte*): Destination buffer for read data\n- dwElemSize (uint): Size of each element in bytes\n- dwElemCount (uint): Number of elements to read\n- pStream (int*): FILE stream structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Number of complete elements read (0 to dwElemCount)\n- Returns partial count on EOF or error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000: Default buffer size for unbuffered streams\n- 0x108: Buffered stream mode flag mask\n- 0x10c: Stream read flags mask\n- 0x20: Error/EOF flag set on failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
