      "name": "ExtractFloatComponents",
      "signature": "float10 * ExtractFloatComponents(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, uint dwLowBits, uint dwHighBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Extract normalized mantissa and exponent from double-precision floating point value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reconstruct double from low/high 32-bit components using CONCAT operations\n2. Check for special case: if value equals global constant _DAT_10027cf8, return zero mantissa and exponent\n3. Detect subnormal numbers by checking if exponent field (bits 20-30) is zero\n4. For subnormal numbers with non-zero mantissa or low bits:\n   - Initialize exponent to -1021 (-0x3fd) \n   - Normalize by left-shifting mantissa until bit 20 (0x10 in high byte) is set\n   - Decrement exponent for each shift operation\n   - Preserve carry from low bits to high bits during shifting\n5. For normal numbers: extract exponent by masking bits 20-30, subtract bias (0x3fe = 1022)\n6. Call ConstructExtendedFloat to convert normalized mantissa to extended precision\n7. Store final exponent via output pointer and return mantissa as float10\n\nParameters:\ndwLowBits - Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double-precision value\ndwHighBits - High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double-precision value  \npnExponent - Pointer to store extracted/computed exponent value\nIMPLICIT wExponentBits (CX) - Exponent bits passed to ConstructExtendedFloat\nIMPLICIT dwMantissaHigh (ESI) - High mantissa bits for ConstructExtendedFloat\n\nReturns:\nfloat10 - Normalized mantissa as extended precision floating point\nZero - When input equals special constant _DAT_10027cf8\n\nSpecial Cases:\nValue equals _DAT_10027cf8 (0x10027cf8) - Returns zero mantissa, zero exponent\nSubnormal numbers (exp=0, mantissa!=0) - Normalized via left-shifting until bit 20 set\nNormal numbers - Standard IEEE 754 exponent extraction with bias removal\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x7ff00000 - IEEE 754 exponent field mask (bits 20-30 of high word)\n0xfffff - IEEE 754 mantissa field mask (bits 0-19 of high word) \n0x80000000 - Sign bit mask for carry detection\n0x10 - Normalization target bit (bit 4 of mantissa high byte)\n-0x3fd (-1021) - Initial exponent for subnormal normalization\n-0x3fe (-1022) - Exponent bias adjustment for normal numbers\n_DAT_10027cf8 - Special value constant requiring zero result\n\nFlag Bits:\nBit manipulations on IEEE 754 double format:\n- Bits 63: Sign bit\n- Bits 62-52: 11-bit exponent field \n- Bits 51-0: 52-bit mantissa field\nFunction focuses on exponent field (bits 20-30 of high word) and mantissa normalization.\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking - assumes valid IEEE 754 input format\nSpecial value _DAT_10027cf8 handled as algorithmic case, not error condition",
