      "name": "InitStdStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "int InitStdStreamBuffer(FILE * pFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes buffering for stdin (iVar3=0) or stdout (iVar3=1) streams.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate file descriptor via FUN_6ff7ad97\n2. Identify stream as stdin (0x6ff86390) or stdout (0x6ff863b0)\n3. Increment global open stream count\n4. Check if stream already has incompatible flags (0x10c)\n5. Allocate 0x1000 byte buffer if not already cached\n6. If malloc fails, use small 2-byte internal buffer (_charbuf)\n7. Configure FILE structure fields and set flags 0x1102\n\nParameters:\n- pFile (FILE*): Pointer to FILE structure (stdin or stdout only)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Buffer initialized successfully\n- 0: Invalid file descriptor, not stdin/stdout, or incompatible flags\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Standard buffer size\n- 0x10c: Flag mask for incompatible stream states\n- 0x1102: Flag bits set after initialization (buffered mode)",
