      "name": "ComputeExtendedFloatRemainder",
      "signature": "void ComputeExtendedFloatRemainder(uint dwMantissaLo, uint dwMantissaHi, ushort wExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Computes IEEE floating-point remainder for 80-bit extended precision floats.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates operand exponents via lookup table at DAT_6ff8686c\n2. Checks for special cases (infinity, denormals, zero divisor)\n3. If exponent difference > 63, uses iterative subtraction with scaling\n4. Otherwise uses hardware FPREM instruction directly\n5. Applies sign correction based on dividend sign bit\n\nParameters:\n- dwMantissaLo (uint): Low 32 bits of dividend mantissa\n- dwMantissaHi (uint): High 32 bits with exponent in upper word\n- wExponent (ushort): Exponent/sign word of dividend\n- IMPLICIT: Divisor passed via caller stack frame at [ESP+0x28]\n\nReturns:\n- Result in EAX (passthrough from input), FPU ST0 contains remainder\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fff: Exponent mask (15-bit biased exponent)\n- 0x8000: Sign bit mask\n- 0x700: Exponent validation bits\n- 0x3f (63): Maximum single-step exponent difference\n- DAT_6ff8689c: Scaling factor (0.5) for iterative reduction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:04a723f02725879527b49570997a0f2a",
