      "signature": "float10 ComputeExtendedPrecisionRemainder(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10",
      "comment": "Computes extended precision (80-bit) floating-point remainder.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If divisor exponent is non-zero, call helper for scaled remainder\n2. If dividend mantissa is non-zero, scale both operands by 2^64 and compute\n3. Otherwise use hardware FPREM for direct remainder\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 contains dividend\n- IMPLICIT: ST1 contains divisor\n\nReturns:\n- Remainder in ST0 (dividend mod divisor)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fff0000: Exponent mask for extended precision\n- 0x43F0000000000000: Scaling factor (2^64 as double)\n- 0x7fbe: Exponent threshold for direct vs scaled computation",
