      "name": "ClassifyDoubleFloatingPoint",
      "signature": "uint ClassifyDoubleFloatingPoint(uint dwDoubleLow, uint dwDoubleHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Classifies a 64-bit double-precision floating-point value into IEEE 754 categories\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent field from high 32-bit word using mask 0x7ff0\n2. Check if exponent equals 0x7ff0 (infinity or NaN)\n   a. Call ClassifyFloatingPointValue to determine specific type\n   b. Map result: 1\u21920x200 (signaling NaN), 2\u21924 (quiet NaN), 3\u21922 (infinity), other\u21921\n3. Check for subnormal numbers (zero exponent with non-zero mantissa)\n   a. Test if exponent bits are zero: (dwDoubleHigh & 0x7ff00000) == 0\n   b. Test if mantissa is non-zero: (dwDoubleHigh & 0xfffff) != 0 OR dwDoubleLow != 0\n   c. Return sign-adjusted subnormal classification: 0x80 or 0x110\n4. Check for exact zero by comparing reconstructed double with global zero constant\n   a. Return sign-adjusted zero classification: 0x40 or 0x20\n5. Default case: normal finite numbers\n   a. Return sign-adjusted normal classification: 0x100 or 0x108\n\nParameters:\n- dwDoubleLow (uint): Low 32 bits of double-precision floating-point value\n- dwDoubleHigh (uint): High 32 bits containing sign, exponent, and high mantissa bits\n\nReturns:\n- 0x200: Signaling NaN\n- 4: Quiet NaN  \n- 2: Infinity\n- 1: Default special value\n- 0x80: Positive subnormal number\n- 0x110: Negative subnormal number  \n- 0x40: Positive zero\n- 0x20: Negative zero\n- 0x100: Positive normal number\n- 0x108: Negative normal number\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input represents 64-bit double split across two 32-bit parameters\n- Sign bit extraction uses bitwise operations: (dwDoubleHigh & 0x80000000) != 0\n- Exponent mask 0x7ff0 targets bits [14:4] of high word for IEEE 754 double format\n- Global constant _g_dZeroConstant used for exact zero comparison via FPU\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x7ff0: IEEE 754 double exponent mask (shifted 4 bits left)\n- 0x7ff00000: Full exponent field mask in high 32-bit word\n- 0xfffff: Mantissa mask for high 20 bits in double format\n- 0x80000000: Sign bit mask\n- 0x200: Signaling NaN classification constant\n- 0x110, 0x80: Subnormal number classifications (negative/positive)\n- 0x40, 0x20: Zero value classifications (positive/negative)  \n- 0x108, 0x100: Normal number classifications (negative/positive)",
