      "name": "BufferStreamPutChar",
      "signature": "uint BufferStreamPutChar(byte byChar, uint * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Writes a character to a buffered stream with position and mode tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: check if byChar != 0xFFFFFFFF\n2. Load stream flags from pStream[3]: check if write enabled (0x01) or (0x80 set AND 0x02 clear)\n3. Initialize stream if position pStream[2] is zero via InitializeBufferStream()\n4. Check if write position pStream[0] equals capacity pStream[2]: if so, check error flag pStream[1]\n5. If error flag set, return 0xFFFFFFFF (write failed)\n6. If no error, increment write position pStream[0] by 1\n7. Check mode flag 0x40 in pStream[3]: if clear (normal write mode):\n   a. Decrement write position pStream[0]\n   b. Write byChar to buffer at position pStream[0]\n8. If flag 0x40 set (verify mode):\n   a. Decrement write position pStream[0]\n   b. Read byte at pStream[0], compare with byChar\n   c. If mismatch, increment position and return 0xFFFFFFFF (verification failed)\n9. Increment character count pStream[1] by 1\n10. Update flags: clear 0x10, set 0x01 in pStream[3]\n11. Return byChar (masked to byte value 0x00-0xFF)\n12. On any validation failure, return 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nParameters:\nbyChar (byte): Character to write to stream (0x00-0xFF)\npStream (uint *): Pointer to stream structure\n  [0] = write position (current offset)\n  [1] = character count written\n  [2] = stream capacity\n  [3] = flags (0x01=write_enabled, 0x02=?, 0x40=verify_mode, 0x80=?)\n\nReturns:\nuint: Masked character value (byChar & 0xFF) on success, 0xFFFFFFFF on failure\n  Failure cases: input invalid, stream full, verification failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nNote: Function has 3-byte stack padding alignment after byChar parameter, non-renameable assembly artifact.\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n0      | 4    | position   | uint | Current write position in buffer\n4      | 4    | count      | uint | Number of characters written\n8      | 4    | capacity   | uint | Stream buffer capacity\n12     | 4    | flags      | uint | Control flags (write_enabled, verify_mode, etc)",
