      "name": "ValidateExceptionHandlerAndInitializeFields",
      "signature": "void ValidateExceptionHandlerAndInitializeFields(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates C++ exception handler structure and initializes game state fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy field from stack [EBP - 0x28] to [ESI - 0x4]\n2. Get structure pointer via FUN_6fb9c171()\n3. Store value from [EBP - 0x1c] into structure field at offset 0x1b (0x6c bytes)\n4. Get structure pointer via FUN_6fb9c171() again\n5. Store value from [EBP - 0x20] into structure field at offset 0x1c (0x70 bytes)\n6. Validate exception handler: check if pExceptionInfo[0] == 0xe06d7363\n7. Verify pExceptionInfo[4] == 0x3 (exception type)\n8. Verify pExceptionInfo[5] == 0x19930520 (exception signature)\n9. Check if [EBP - 0x24] == 0 (error flag not set)\n10. Check if [EBP - 0x2c] != 0 (handler data present)\n11. If all checks pass: call abnormal termination and process exception via FUN_6fb9c011()\n\nParameters: (IMPLICIT parameters via unaffected registers)\n- nFramePointer (EBP): Frame base pointer, accesses stack locals at negative offsets\n- nSrcIndex (ESI): Destination base for field copy at [ESI - 0x4]\n- pExceptionInfo (EDI): Pointer to C++ exception handler structure\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0xe06d7363: C++ exception handler signature ('msE' in little-endian)\n- Magic number 0x19930520: Exception type identifier signature\n- If exception validation fails, function returns early (RET at 0x6fb9be22)\n- If validation succeeds, calls abnormal termination handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.09d",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:b8d821347a0eb2918a2bdd3c6ba58507",
