      "comment": "Initializes Windows SEH (Structured Exception Handling) and dispatches exception handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current ExceptionList to restore on return\n2. Validate pExceptionRecord is non-NULL\n3. Dereference pExceptionRecord[0x1c] to get handler table base\n4. Load function pointer from handler table[0x4]\n5. Validate function pointer is non-NULL\n6. Clear dwFlags (local_8) to 0\n7. Install new exception frame: ExceptionList = &pPrevExceptionList\n8. Call DispatchJumpTableEntry with handler table pointer and function pointer\n9. Restore original ExceptionList\n10. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionRecord (void *) - Exception record structure with handler info\n    Offset 0x1c: pointer to handler dispatch table\n    Offset 0x18: pointer to handler frame data\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, exception handling installed and dispatched\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns silently if pExceptionRecord is NULL\n  - Returns silently if dispatch function pointer is NULL (no handler installed)\n  - Exception frame properly restored even if exception occurs\n\nNote: Function uses 2 decompiler-generated temporaries (puStack_10, puStack_c) optimized by compiler.",
