      "name": "SetObjectFields0x118_0x120",
      "signature": "void SetObjectFields0x118_0x120(void * pObject, uint dwValue0x118, uint dwValue0x11c, uint dwValue0x120)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets three consecutive dword values in an object structure at offsets 0x118, 0x11c, and 0x120.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pObject pointer from first parameter (ESP+4)\n2. Check if pObject is NULL using TEST EAX,EAX\n3. Jump to return if NULL, skipping all writes\n4. Load dwValue0x118 from second parameter (ESP+8)\n5. Load dwValue0x11c from third parameter (ESP+C)\n6. Write dwValue0x118 to offset +0x118 in object\n7. Load dwValue0x120 from fourth parameter (ESP+10)\n8. Write dwValue0x11c to offset +0x11c in object\n9. Write dwValue0x120 to offset +0x120 in object\n10. Return to caller with callee cleanup (RET 0x10)\n\nParameters:\n- pObject: void* - Pointer to object structure. If NULL, function returns without modification.\n- dwValue0x118: uint - First dword value to write at offset +0x118\n- dwValue0x11c: uint - Second dword value to write at offset +0x11c\n- dwValue0x120: uint - Third dword value to write at offset +0x120\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function modifies object fields in-place.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check: If pObject is NULL, all write operations are skipped\n- The three writes are consecutive dword values at fixed offsets\n- __stdcall convention: Callee cleans up 0x10 bytes (4 parameters \u00d7 4 bytes)",
