      "comment": "Signals a Windows event handle stored within a game object.\n\n## Algorithm\n1. Load pGameObject from stack (ESP+4)\n2. Check if pGameObject is NULL\n3. If NULL, exit without error\n4. Load event handle from pGameObject[0x114]\n5. Call SetEvent Windows API via import table at 0x6ff750ec\n6. Return with 4-byte stack cleanup\n\n## Parameters\npGameObject (void *) - Pointer to game object containing event handle at +0x114\n\n## Returns\nvoid - No return value. Success/failure indicated by SetEvent Windows API.\n\n## Special Cases\nNULL pointer returns immediately without signaling event",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "EXP",
