      "name": "WaitOnObjectHandle",
      "signature": "uint WaitOnObjectHandle(void * pObject, uint dwTimeoutMs)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Waits on a game object handle with optional timeout.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load object pointer from first stack parameter (ESP + 4)\\n2. Load and check reference count at offset 0x0 in object\\n3. If reference count is non-zero, return 0 (invalid state)\\n4. If reference count is zero, load HANDLE at offset 0xbd4 from object\\n5. Move HANDLE to stack parameter for function call\\n6. Call WaitForSingleObject with HANDLE and timeout value\\n7. Return wait result (WAIT_OBJECT_0, WAIT_TIMEOUT, WAIT_ABANDONED, or WAIT_FAILED)\\n\\nParameters:\\npObject - Pointer to game object structure; contains reference count at offset 0x0 and HANDLE at offset 0xbd4\\ndwTimeoutMs - Timeout value in milliseconds passed to WaitForSingleObject\\n\\nReturns:\\n0 if pObject reference count is non-zero (invalid state)\\nOtherwise returns WaitForSingleObject result code\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Early validation exit returns 0 when object is in invalid state (reference count != 0)\\n- Direct pass-through of WaitForSingleObject result on valid objects\\n- No error handling for null pObject pointer (assumes valid pointer always passed)\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nObject structure referenced:\\n- Offset 0x0: Reference count (DWORD) - checked for zero\\n- Offset 0xbd4: HANDLE to wait object",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ed189147b995a460d3cbbbe9672e6ad4",
