      "signature": "char * BuildSymbolSearchPath(char * pOutputPath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Constructs a semicolon-delimited symbol search path from multiple sources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer to empty string\n2. Obtain home directory via ExtractModuleDirectory and append with semicolon if available\n3. Query current working directory using GetCurrentDirectoryA\n4. If current directory differs from home directory (case-insensitive comparison), append with semicolon\n5. Query _NT_SYMBOL_PATH environment variable; if set, append with semicolon\n6. Query _NT_ALTERNATE_SYMBOL_PATH environment variable; if set, append with semicolon\n7. Query SYSTEMROOT environment variable; if set, append with semicolon\n8. Remove trailing semicolon from the final path string\n9. Log operation result: error message if path is empty, success message with path if populated\n10. Return pointer to output buffer if non-empty, NULL otherwise\n\nParameters:\npOutputPath (char*): Caller-allocated buffer receiving semicolon-separated symbol paths\n\nReturns:\nchar*: Pointer to pOutputPath if at least one valid path was added, NULL if no paths found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Path segments are separated with literal semicolon (0x3B) character\n- Home directory comparison uses case-insensitive string matching via __stricmp\n- Each environment variable is read into a 512-byte temporary buffer\n- Stack frame allocates 0x400 bytes (1024 total) for two 512-byte buffers\n- Return value conversion uses NEG/SBB bit manipulation to convert boolean (output[0] != 0) to pointer\n- Called from InitializeSymbolHandler and DumpThreadCallStackWithSymbols\n\nStructure Layout:\nStack offsets (relative to ESP after SUB ESP, 0x400):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name                Type          Description\n  0x000   0x200 tempEnvironmentBuffer    char[512]    Temp buffer for environment variables\n  0x200   0x200 currentDirectoryBuffer   char[512]    Current working directory path\n  0x400   0x4   EBP (saved frame pointer) int          Calling function frame pointer\n  0x404   0x4   Return Address            void*        Return address to caller",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:236f574b953133142779bd9bba355dc5",
