      "name": "UnlinkListNode",
      "signature": "void UnlinkListNode(ListNode * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a node from an intrusive linked list and clears its pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract next node pointer from pNode->pNext (offset 0x0)\n2. If next node pointer is null, exit early (empty list)\n3. Extract offset value from pNode->dwOffset (offset 0x4) \n4. Calculate target pointer location using offset-based addressing:\n   - If offset is negative (MSB set): use bitwise NOT operation (~dwOffset)\n   - If offset is positive: calculate relative address as pNode + (dwOffset - nextNode->dwOffset)\n5. Store next node pointer at calculated target location (*ppTargetNode = pNextNode)\n6. Update next node's offset field with current node's offset (nextNode->dwOffset = pNode->dwOffset)\n7. Clear current node pointers: set pNode->pNext = NULL and pNode->dwOffset = 0\n\nParameters:\npNode (ListNode *): Pointer to list node to unlink, containing next pointer and offset\n  IMPLICIT: ECX register contains pNode (__fastcall convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value. Modifies list structure in-place and clears unlinked node.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles null pNext gracefully with early exit to prevent access violations\n- Processes negative offsets using bitwise NOT operation (0x6fadc38e-0x6fadc390)\n- Maintains list integrity by updating both forward pointers and offset chains\n- Clears unlinked node completely to prevent dangling references\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name  | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-------------|-------|---------------------------\n0x00   |  4   | pNext       | void* | Pointer to next list node\n0x04   |  4   | dwOffset    | uint  | Offset value for addressing calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bf2cf5e2d01486392f917db7052df210",
