      "signature": "void ProcessStaleFileHandles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes file handles that have exceeded their timeout thresholds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetTickCount() to retrieve current system time in milliseconds\n2. Initialize slot index (ESI) to 0 for iteration\n3. Loop through file handle slots (stride 4 bytes per slot, max 20 slots = 0x50 bytes):\n   a. Load FILE* pointer from g_LogFilePointers array at [ESI + 0x6ff81900]\n   b. If pointer is NULL, skip to next slot\n   c. Load first timeout timestamp from g_LogFileFirstAccessTime at [ESI + 0x6ff81950]\n   d. Calculate elapsed time: currentTickCount (EDI) - firstTimeout\n   e. Compare elapsed with 0x3a98 (15000 decimal = 15 seconds)\n   f. If elapsed >= 15 seconds, close file and clear pointer\n   g. Otherwise, load second timeout timestamp from g_LogFileLastAccessTime at [ESI + 0x6ff818a8]\n   h. Calculate elapsed time: currentTickCount (EDI) - secondTimeout\n   i. Compare elapsed with 0x1388 (5000 decimal = 5 seconds)\n   j. If elapsed >= 5 seconds, close file and clear pointer\n   k. Increment slot index by 4 bytes (pointer arithmetic)\n4. Loop condition: continue until slotIndex >= 0x50 (20 slots processed)\n5. Restore saved registers and return\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value\n\nParameters:\nnone - takes no parameters\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0x3a98 = 15000ms (15 second timeout for first access), 0x1388 = 5000ms (5 second timeout for last access)\n- File handle slot stride: 4 bytes per slot (sizeof(FILE*))\n- Total slots monitored: 20 handles (0x50 bytes / 4 bytes per slot)\n- Uses C runtime _fclose() to properly close file handles\n- Clears pointer entry to NULL (0) after closing to prevent double-close\n- NULL pointer check prevents accessing invalid handles\n\nGlobal Data:\n- g_LogFilePointers: Array of 20 FILE* pointers at 0x6ff81900 (80 bytes total)\n- g_LogFileFirstAccessTime: Array of 20 DWORD timestamps at 0x6ff81950 (80 bytes total)\n- g_LogFileLastAccessTime: Array of 20 DWORD timestamps at 0x6ff818a8 (80 bytes total)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
