      "name": "CalculateStreamLineCount",
      "signature": "int CalculateStreamLineCount(char * szStreamBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculate total line count in stream, including newline-aware counting.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get stream ID from buffer offset +0x10\n2. If stream position at +0x4 is negative, clear bytes 4-7\n3. Call FUN_6fb9ed0a to get line count adjustment\n4. If result negative, return error (-1)\n5. Check stream flags at offset +0xc:\n   - If flags 0x108 clear, return immediate adjustment (early exit)\n   - If flags have bit 0x3 set, count newlines in buffer range\n   - Access g_pStreamPropertyTables with stream ID to check line-count flag (0x80)\n6. If line-count flag set, iterate buffer from start to current position counting 0x0A bytes\n7. If flag 0x1 set and position non-zero, handle secondary position calculation:\n   - Recompute secondary position using offset +0x18 if needed\n   - Count newlines in secondary range\n   - Check flag 0x20 at offset +0xd for adjustment\n8. Return total line count (adjusted result + counted lines)\n\nParameters:\nszStreamBuffer (char *) - Stream state buffer containing position and flag data\n\nReturns:\nPositive int - Total line count in stream\n-1 - Error during initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If stream position negative, zeros are written to clear state\n- Flag 0x80 in property table gates newline counting logic\n- Multiple buffer ranges may be counted depending on flags\n- Flag 0x1 enables secondary position calculation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:84b2916a3c1491486029ed95da0dd44d",
