      "rvas": {
        "LoD/1.10": "0x15FA7",
        "LoD/1.11": "0x2889",
        "LoD/1.11b": "0x28C0",
        "LoD/1.12a": "0x1F50",
        "LoD/1.13c": "0x2A85",
        "LoD/1.13d": "0x27B0"
      },
      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.10": 141,
        "LoD/1.11": 143,
        "LoD/1.11b": 143,
        "LoD/1.12a": 143,
        "LoD/1.13c": 143,
        "LoD/1.13d": 143
      },
      "name": "ValidateStreamOptions",
      "signature": "int ValidateStreamOptions(uint * pStreamConfig, int nStartLine, uint dwMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validate stream configuration flags and mode, then prepare for line processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate stream configuration: Check if pStreamConfig[3] (flags) has 0x83 bits set AND dwMode in {0, 1, 2}\n   - If flags not set or mode invalid (not 0, 1, 2): Get error code pointer from GetErrorCodeBuffer(), set error 0x16, return -1\n2. Clear 0x10 flag from pStreamConfig[3] unconditionally\n3. If dwMode == 1: Calculate actual line count via CalculateStreamLineCount(), add to nStartLine parameter, set dwMode to 0\n4. Process stream via ProcessStreamState(pStreamConfig)\n5. Load updated flags: dwFlags = pStreamConfig[3]\n6. If high bit (0x80) is SET: Clear low 2 bits (0x03) from flags, store back\n7. Else if high bit CLEAR: Check bits 0x01 and 0x08 are SET and 0x400 is CLEAR\n   - If true: Set pStreamConfig[6] = 0x200 (likely buffer size or capacity indicator)\n8. Call ProcessLineIndexing(pStreamConfig[4], nStartLine, dwMode) with return in dwLineIndex\n9. Set nResult = (dwLineIndex != 0xffffffff) - 1 = {-1 if failure, 0 if success}\n10. Return nResult (0=success, -1=failure)\n\nParameters:\n- pStreamConfig: uint* - Pointer to stream configuration structure (accessed at offsets [3], [4], [6])\n- nStartLine: int - Starting line number, may be incremented if dwMode==1\n- dwMode: uint - Stream mode flag: 0=normal, 1=line-count, 2=special (invalid if not in {0,1,2})\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Configuration validated and processing successful\n- -1: Invalid flags or mode, or line processing failed (check error code via GetErrorCodeBuffer())\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Phantom register spills: Decompiler shows iVar2, DVar3 in locals but optimized by compiler\n- Flag 0x83: Required flags for valid stream (0x80 | 0x02 | 0x01)\n- Flag 0x10: Unconditionally cleared (reset/synchronization flag)\n- Flag 0x80: High byte bit; if set, clears mode bits 0x01-0x02 (disable flags)\n- Flag 0x400: When clear with 0x08, enables special buffer setup (0x200)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x83: Required flag bitmask (0x80 | 0x02 | 0x01)\n- 0xef: Mask to clear 0x10 bit (NOT 0x10)\n- 0x80: High bit flag check (mode disable indicator)\n- 0x200: Buffer size/mode value set in pStreamConfig[6]\n- 0xffffef / 0xfffffffc: Bitwise AND masks for flag clearing\n- 0xffffffff: Sentinel return value indicating processing error",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.10",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:4673c56db10348ea3180eb8dbc4be700",
