      "name": "InitializeExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void InitializeExceptionHandler(undefined4 * pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize Structured Exception Handler (SEH) for protected resource cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current FS:[0] exception handler pointer for restoration\n2. Push exception code marker (-1) to identify frame type\n3. Push SEH handler callback address (g_pfnExceptionHandlerCallback)\n4. Calculate next handler slot offset (pExceptionRecord + 0x4) into ECX\n5. Install current ESP as new FS:[0] exception handler frame\n6. Zero all handler fields in exception record\n7. Create self-referential forward pointer for exception chain\n8. Compute bitwise NOT of pointer as canary/validation signature\n9. Store inverted canary as exception handler validation field\n10. Store sentinel marker (0xFFFFFFFF) in frame marker field\n11. Restore saved FS:[0] pointer to re-link to previous handler\n12. Clean up SEH frame (ADD ESP, 0xC) and return\n\nParameters:\npExceptionRecord (undefined4 *) - Pointer to SEH exception record structure for handler chain\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Exception handler frame is installed in FS:[0] and ready for processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses Windows Structured Exception Handling via FS register\n- Bitwise NOT creates linked-list canary for validation\n- Standard MSVC runtime initialization for _try/_except blocks\n- RET 0x4 performs stdcall parameter cleanup",
