      "name": "HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown",
      "signature": "void HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown(uint removedElementIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes the last element from a binary min-heap and performs sift-down operation to restore heap ordering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the removed element's parent pointer and index fields at offsets +0x4 and +0x8\n2. Load current heap size from header at offset +0x4\n3. Calculate parent element pointer from element array (size > 0 ? array[size-1] : NULL)\n4. Calculate new size as oldSize - 1\n5. Check if capacity growth is needed: if (newSize > header[0] && newSize > header[1])\n6. Load growth size from header at offset +0xc (or call GetHighestPowerOfTwo if zero)\n7. Calculate aligned capacity: if (newSize % growthSize != 0) then capacity = newSize + (growthSize - remainder)\n8. Call GrowHeapCapacity to expand the array if needed\n9. Update heap size to newSize\n10. If removed element was not at last position, perform sift-down:\n    a. Calculate parent boundary as (size - 3) >> 1\n    b. Loop while currentIndex <= parentBoundary:\n       - Calculate left child index as currentIndex * 2 + 1\n       - Check if right child exists and is smaller than left child\n       - If so, use right child (currentIndex * 2 + 2)\n       - Call comparison function to compare removed element with selected child\n       - If removed element is smaller or equal, break (sift complete)\n       - Move child element up to current position\n       - Update child's parent pointer and index\n       - Move currentIndex to child position and continue\n    c. Place removed element at final position\n    d. Update element's parent pointer and index\n\nParameters:\nremovedElementIndex - Index in the element array of the element being removed\npHeap - Pointer to HeapHeader structure\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 3 at 0x6ff51597: Used to calculate parent boundary as (size - 3) >> 1 for sift loop\nComparison function result: Zero means child is smaller (continue sifting), non-zero means done\n\nStructure Layout:\nHeapHeader structure (16 bytes):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | capacity        | uint  | Maximum number of elements heap can hold\n0x04   | 4    | size            | uint  | Current number of elements in heap\n0x08   | 4    | pElementArray   | uint* | Pointer to array of element offsets\n0x0c   | 4    | growthSize      | uint  | Size increment for capacity growth (0 = dynamic)\n0x10   | 4    | baseOffset      | uint  | Base offset added to element array offsets\n\nHeap Element structure (accessed at baseOffset + elementArray[index]):\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type  | Description\n-------|------|-----------------|-------|------------------------------------------\n0x00   | 4    | pCompareFunc    | void* | Pointer to comparison function\n0x04   | 4    | pParentHeap     | void* | Pointer to parent heap (cleared on removal)\n0x08   | 4    | heapIndex       | uint  | Element's index in heap array (cleared on removal)\n\nNote: Function cannot be decompiled due to control flow complexity. Documentation based on disassembly analysis.",
