      "name": "UnwindHeapDestructor",
      "signature": "void UnwindHeapDestructor(void * pHeapContainer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exception unwind handler that safely destroys a heap-containing object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current exception handler state from FS:[0x0] (Windows EH chain)\n2. Establish new exception context with unwind filter (g_ExceptionUnwindHandler)\n3. Set virtual function pointer at offset +0x0 to g_HeapCleanupVtable (0x6ff78388)\n4. Load heap data pointer from offset +0x4 and test for validity\n5. If heap data exists (non-NULL), call HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown with heap pointer from offset +0x8\n6. Restore original exception handler state to FS:[0x0]\n7. Clean up stack frame (12 bytes local + 4 bytes parameter) and return\n\nParameters:\n  pHeapContainer - Pointer to heap container object structure\n    Offset +0x0: vfptr - Virtual function table pointer (set to cleanup handler)\n    Offset +0x4: Heap data validity pointer (checked before cleanup)\n    Offset +0x8: Heap structure pointer (passed to sift-down function)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; performs in-place cleanup of heap structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If heap data pointer at +0x4 is NULL, skips HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown call\n  - Uses Windows structured exception handling via FS:[0x0] exception list chain\n  - Exception code 0xFFFFFFFF indicates normal unwind state (no active exception)\n  - Calling convention is __stdcall with 4-byte parameter cleanup (RET 0x4)\n  - EDX register contains implicit heap header parameter for HeapRemoveLastAndSiftDown\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type      Description\n------  ----  ------------------   -------   ------------------------------------\n+0x0    4     vfptr                pointer   Virtual function table pointer\n+0x4    4     pHeapData            pointer   Heap data validity check pointer\n+0x8    4     pHeapStructure       pointer   Heap structure for unwinding\nTotal: 12+ bytes",
