      "name": "WriteFormattedWideStringToFile",
      "signature": "int WriteFormattedWideStringToFile(FILE * pFile, wchar_t * pwszFormat, ...)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Write formatted wide-character string to file stream with thread-safe buffering.\n\nThis is the wide-character implementation of fprintf that formats variadic arguments\naccording to a format string and writes the result to a FILE stream. The function\nimplements thread-safe file access through mutex locking and manages buffering\nautomatically with exception safety through SEH (Structured Exception Handling).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Establish SEH exception frame for cleanup on error (PUSH 0x14, PUSH 0x6ff75358)\n2. Acquire exclusive lock on FILE stream to prevent concurrent access (__lock_file)\n3. Setup buffered I/O state, storing previous buffer flag (__stbuf)\n4. Process format string and write formatted wide-character output (ProcessFormatSpecifier)\n5. Restore previous buffer state and flush pending writes (__ftbuf)\n6. Release FILE lock in exception handler or normal exit (UnlockFileOnExit via SEH)\n7. Return number of wide characters written or negative on error (in EAX)\n\nParameters:\n  pFile (FILE*) - Pointer to FILE stream structure for output\n  pwszFormat (wchar_t*) - Wide-character format string with %d, %s, %ls specifiers\n  ... (variadic) - Variable number of arguments matching format specifiers\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of wide characters written on success\n        Negative value on write error or invalid format\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - SEH frame at 0x6ff75358 ensures file unlock on exception\n  - Buffer flag from __stbuf determines flush behavior (0x0 vs 0xffffffff)\n  - Format specifier processing handles wide-char conversions via ProcessFormatSpecifier\n  - Variadic args accessed via stack pointer at [EBP+0x10] (third parameter onward)\n\nLibrary Function:\n  This implements Visual C++ Runtime Library function fwprintf() from stdio.h\n  Signature: int fwprintf(FILE* stream, const wchar_t* format, ...)\n  Part of wide-character I/O subsystem in MSVCRT.dll or static CRT",
