      "name": "ReleaseFileStreamLock",
      "signature": "void ReleaseFileStreamLock(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases FILE stream lock during exception unwinding or normal exit.\n\nThis function serves as a cleanup helper for WriteFormattedWideStringToFile (fwprintf)\nand is invoked as part of the Structured Exception Handling (SEH) unwinding process.\nIt accesses the FILE pointer from the caller's stack frame using an implicit parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load FILE* pointer from caller's stack at offset EBP-0x20\n2. Call __unlock_file() to release the mutex lock on the FILE stream\n3. Return to caller or exception handler\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT: FILE* pointer at [EBP-0x20] from calling function's stack frame\n            This location is established by WriteFormattedWideStringToFile before\n            calling __lock_file() and is accessed during exception cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Designed for use in SEH (Structured Exception Handling) cleanup chains\n  - Depends on specific stack frame layout of WriteFormattedWideStringToFile\n  - The FILE pointer location (EBP-0x20) is part of the ABI contract between\n    WriteFormattedWideStringToFile and this cleanup function\n  - Must not be called directly; only invoked via exception handler registration",
