      "name": "UnlockFileStream",
      "signature": "void UnlockFileStream(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases the lock on a FILE stream object.\n\nThis thunk function serves as a cleanup wrapper that releases file locks\nacquired by __lock_file. It is called after file operations complete to\nensure the FILE object is accessible to other threads.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve FILE pointer from stack parameter at [EBP + 8]\n2. Call __unlock_file to release the lock on the FILE stream\n3. Return to caller with stack cleanup (callee cleans 4 bytes)\n\nParameters:\npFile - Pointer to FILE structure to unlock\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall convention: callee cleans the stack (RET implied)\n- Called from _ftell and other C runtime file operations as cleanup routine\n- Bridges high-level C runtime code with low-level file locking mechanism",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
