      "name": "DestructorWithCleanup",
      "signature": "void DestructorWithCleanup(type_info * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "C++ type_info Virtual Destructor - RTTI type information cleanup\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH exception handling frame with size 0x8\n2. Set up exception handling via __SEH_prolog call\n3. Store this pointer in ESI for safe reference\n4. Set vftable pointer at offset 0 to type_info class vtable\n5. Acquire exclusive lock on global typeinfo state (lock level 0xe)\n6. Load name/description string pointer from this+4 offset\n7. Test if pointer is NULL to prevent invalid deallocation\n8. If non-NULL, push pointer and call _free() to deallocate\n9. Set exception frame cleanup state via OR with 0xffffffff\n10. Release global typeinfo lock via ReleaseLockForTypeinfo()\n11. Clean up exception handling frame via __SEH_epilog\n12. Execute RET instruction to return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pThis (type_info *): Pointer to type_info object instance being destroyed\n\nReturns:\n  void: Destructor performs in-place cleanup with no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL pointer at this+4 is handled safely, skip deallocation if NULL\n  - Exception frame management prevents stack unwinding issues\n  - Global lock ensures thread-safe typeinfo system state\n  - __thiscall convention passes this pointer in ECX register",
