      "name": "LeaveCriticalSectionAfterCloseDispatcher",
      "signature": "void LeaveCriticalSectionAfterCloseDispatcher(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper dispatcher for critical section cleanup after file close operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve ESI register on stack (acts as implicit parameter)\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionDispatcher with ESI as critical section pointer/index\n3. Pop return address into ECX (unusual calling sequence)\n4. Return to caller with critical section state updated\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT ESI: Critical section pointer or index value for dispatch\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; delegates critical section leave to dispatcher\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ESI register preserved for critical section parameter passing\n- Unusual calling convention with ECX used for return address\n- Wrapper function called during file stream close (CloseFileStreamIfNotLocked)",
