      "name": "AllocateGameBuffer",
      "signature": "void * AllocateGameBuffer(void * pContext, int nBufferSize, char * szFileName, int nLineNumber)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates a game buffer with error handling and automatic shutdown on failure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls AllocateAndInitializeBuffer with context, size, and source file/line info\n2. Stores allocation result in ESI\n3. Tests if allocation succeeded (result != NULL)\n4. On success: returns the allocated buffer pointer to caller\n5. On failure: calls LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 2 and file/line diagnostics\n6. LogErrorAndShutdown does not return (causes application shutdown)\n\nParameters:\npContext (ECX) - Memory pool or allocation context pointer\nbufferSize (EDX) - Size in bytes of buffer to allocate\nfileName (Stack+4) - Source code file name where allocation was requested\nlineNumber (Stack+8) - Source code line number where allocation was requested\n\nReturns:\nvoid * - Pointer to allocated and initialized buffer on success\nNULL - Never returned (LogErrorAndShutdown prevents error return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function does not return on allocation failure; LogErrorAndShutdown terminates application\n- Uses fastcall calling convention with pContext in ECX, bufferSize in EDX\n- Callee cleans up 12 bytes from stack (RET 0xc)\n- File name and line number used for diagnostic logging on allocation failure\n- Error code 2 indicates allocation failure requiring immediate shutdown",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:0e0d573cf4ec8a1e2fdaabd991414fe3",
