      "name": "SearchResourceTableByThreshold",
      "signature": "void * SearchResourceTableByThreshold(void * pResourceManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Binary search through sorted resource table to find resource matching threshold value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section lock on resource manager\n2. Load resource count and threshold array pointer from resource manager structure\n3. Perform standard binary search on sorted array using threshold values at offset +4\n4. Compare input threshold with array element thresholds (accessed via [EDI + EAX*8 + 4])\n5. Adjust search bounds: if input < array_threshold, search lower half; else search upper half\n6. When search completes, verify result index bounds (0 <= index < count)\n7. Fetch resource pointer from array at verified index (accessed via [EDI + EAX*8])\n8. Return NULL if result index out of bounds\n9. Release critical section lock\n10. Return resource pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\npResourceManager (EAX): Pointer to resource manager structure\n  - Offset 0x4: Critical section lock pointer\n  - Offset 0x7a0: Count of resources in array (DWORD)\n  - Offset 0x7a8: Pointer to array of threshold entries (8 bytes each)\ndwThresholdValue (Stack +0xC): Threshold value to search for\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Pointer to ResourcePoolNode if found, NULL if not found or out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty array (count <= 0): Returns NULL\n- Result index < 0: Returns NULL (no match before first element)\n- Result index >= count: Returns NULL (no match after last element)\n- Array element structure: 8 bytes per entry, threshold value at offset +4\n- Function uses critical section to synchronize access to resource table\n- Binary search divides search range by 2 each iteration via SAR EAX,1",
