      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Finds the next available slot in a pool node slot array based on encoded node descriptor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract region index from node descriptor (EAX >> 5), initialize slot offset accumulator to 0\n2. Compare region index against 7 for initial dispatch:\n   - If region <= 7: use jump table at 0x6ff6acb8 to dispatch to slot check (cases 0-7)\n   - For each case, load corresponding slot pointer from array and check if non-sentinel\n3. Check all 8 slot pointers in order (slots 0-7) for non-sentinel values:\n   - If slot pointer != 0xffffffff: call FindFirstClearBitPosition helper\n   - Compute and return result with appropriate offset: (slotId + slotOffsetAccumulator + offset)\n   - Offsets per slot: slot0=0x00, slot1=0x20, slot2=0x40, slot3=0x60, slot4=0x80, slot5=0xa0, slot6=0xc0, slot7=0xe0\n4. If all slots in current region exhausted (region > 8): proceed to remainder handling\n5. Remainder handling: decrement region counter, advance array pointer by 8 bytes (0x20 bytes), accumulate 0x100 per region\n6. Loop back to region limit check until all regions processed\n\nParameters:\n  pNodeArray - Pointer to PoolNodeSlotArray structure containing 8 pointers to slot data\n  nodeDescriptor (EAX, implicit) - Encoded node: upper bits = region index (0-...), lower 5 bits = slot position\n\nReturns:\n  int - Computed slot address offset in EAX, or -1 (0xffffffff) if no valid slot found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Sentinel values: 0xffffffff marks uninitialized/invalid slots\n  Region stride: 0x20 bytes per slot access, 0x100 bytes per region in accumulator\n  Dispatch table: Located at 0x6ff6acb8, handles initial 8 regions via indexed jump\n  Fallthrough: Multiple CMP instructions fall through to next check without break\n  Global sentinel table: g_dwSentinelMaskTable at 0x6ff76cb0 used for remainder position validation\n\nStructure Layout (PoolNodeSlotArray at pNodeArray):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name    Type       Description\n  0x00    4     slot0         pointer    First slot pointer\n  0x04    4     slot1         pointer    Second slot pointer\n  0x08    4     slot2         pointer    Third slot pointer\n  0x0c    4     slot3         pointer    Fourth slot pointer\n  0x10    4     slot4         pointer    Fifth slot pointer\n  0x14    4     slot5         pointer    Sixth slot pointer\n  0x18    4     slot6         pointer    Seventh slot pointer\n  0x1c    4     slot7         pointer    Eighth slot pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
