      "name": "CalculateBitLength",
      "signature": "int CalculateBitLength(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates the bit length (position of highest set bit) of an input value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input is in range [3, 16] (0x10): return 0 if input <= 0x10 (invalid)\n2. Check minimum threshold: return -3 (0xfffffffd) if input < 3 (too small)\n3. Decrement input value by 1 to account for one-based semantics\n4. Validate decremented value is not zero: return -4 (0xfffffffc) if zero\n5. Use BSR (Bit Scan Right) instruction to find position of highest set bit\n6. Increment bit position by 1 (to adjust for BSR semantics)\n7. Subtract 4 (0x4) from bit position to get final result\n8. Return adjusted bit position value\n\nParameters:\ninputValue (EAX) - Input value to analyze for bit length. Must be in range [3, 16] or [17, 0xFFFFFFFF]. Values in [3, 16] return 0, values < 3 return -3.\n\nReturns:\nint - Position of highest set bit minus 4, or error code: 0 if input in [3, 16], -3 (0xfffffffd) if input < 3, -4 (0xfffffffc) if (input - 1) == 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic numbers and thresholds:\n- 0x10 (16) is upper threshold for immediate return with 0\n- 0x3 (3) is minimum valid value threshold\n- 0x1f (31) was original max bit position constant (register preserved but unused in final BSR version)\n- 0x4 offset subtracted from bit position result\n- Input decremented by 1 before validation suggests one-based input numbering\n\nBit Range Analysis:\n- Input value 0-2: Returns -3 (invalid)\n- Input value 3-16: Returns 0 (below minimum threshold)\n- Input value 17+: BSR finds highest set bit, adjusted and returned\n\nBSR Instruction Behavior:\n- Scans right from MSB (most significant bit) to find first 1 bit\n- Returns bit position (0-31) in destination register\n- For 32-bit value, position 31 = MSB, position 0 = LSB\n- Incremented by 1 then minus 4 adjustment provides final offset\n\nError Codes (Negative Values):\n-3 (0xfffffffd): Input < 3, invalid range\n-4 (0xfffffffc): Input == 1, equals 1 after decrement (special zero case)",
