      "name": "SetContextValueThreadSafe",
      "signature": "void SetContextValueThreadSafe(ThreadSafeContext * pContext, uint dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a value in a thread-safe context structure using mutual exclusion locking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Accept context pointer (or NULL for default global context) and value to store\n2. Load default global context (g_pDefaultThreadContext) if pContext is NULL\n3. Validate context by checking validity flag at offset +0x1c (non-zero = valid)\n4. If context is invalid, return immediately without modification\n5. If context is valid:\n   a. Compute critical section address at offset +0x4 from context base\n   b. Call synchronization pre-operation at address 0x6ff61690 with magic 0x8ae\n   c. Enter critical section via g_pfnEnterCriticalSection for exclusive access\n   d. Store dwValue to context offset +0x0 (the value field)\n   e. Call synchronization post-operation at address 0x6ff61690 with magic 0x8b2\n   f. Leave critical section via g_pfnLeaveCriticalSection to release lock\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pContext: Pointer to ThreadSafeContext structure, or NULL to use g_pDefaultThreadContext\n- dwValue: 32-bit unsigned value to store in context.value field\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pContext is NULL, operation uses the global default context (g_pDefaultThreadContext)\n- If context validity flag (offset +0x1c) is zero, function returns without modification\n- Magic constants 0x8ae (pre-op) and 0x8b2 (post-op) passed to synchronization function\n- Critical section at offset +0x4 protects concurrent access to context.value\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name          | Type              | Description\n0x0    | 4    | value               | uint              | Stored context value\n0x4    | 24   | criticalSection     | byte[24]          | CRITICAL_SECTION for thread sync\n0x1c   | 4    | validityFlag        | uint              | Non-zero = context initialized",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:62ea6eefb994ddcf321760239c499701",
