      "name": "AllocatePoolBlockFromSlot",
      "signature": "void * AllocatePoolBlockFromSlot(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from the game resource pool using hash table chain management.\n\nThis function allocates memory and links it into a hash table for efficient pool management.\nThe allocation includes a 4-byte header for internal linked list management. The hash table\nuses 1024 slots (indices 0-0x3ff) indexed by the block address modulo 0x3ff, supporting\nO(1) allocation with collision handling via linked list chaining.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Adds 4 bytes to requested size for internal header storage\n2. Calls malloc() to allocate memory; triggers shutdown on failure\n3. Computes hash slot as (block_address % 0x3ff) for hash table indexing\n4. Enters critical section (gameContext+0x4) to protect concurrent access\n5. Loads existing block at hash table slot [gameContext+0x7ac + slot*4]\n6. Stores existing block pointer in new block's 4-byte header for linked list\n7. Updates hash table slot to point to new block (becomes new chain head)\n8. Leaves critical section to unlock the pool\n9. Returns pointer offset by +4 bytes, skipping internal header\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EBX: Pointer to game context structure (contains pool state)\n             - gameContext+0x4: CRITICAL_SECTION for hash table protection\n             - gameContext+0x7a0: Pool size/state variable\n             - gameContext+0x7ac: Hash table base (1024 DWORD slots)\nIMPLICIT EAX: Requested allocation size in bytes (adjusted with +4 for header)\n\nReturns:\nvoid *: Pointer to allocated memory with 4-byte offset applied\n        Returns address of user data area (header at offset -4)\n        Does NOT return on allocation failure - calls ShutdownResourcesAndExit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Allocation failure logs pool status to LogMemoryStatus, gets return address for debugging,\n  then calls LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 0x388 and exits with code -1\n- Hash table slot 0x3ff reserved; collisions resolved via linked list chaining\n- Critical section prevents race conditions between allocate and concurrent free operations\n- Internal 4-byte header format: [link_pointer] where link_pointer chains to previous block\n\nPool Hash Table Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\n0x7ac   4096  pool_hash_table   void**      1024 hash table slots (indices 0-0x3ff)\n0x4     4     pool_lock         CRITICAL    Protects concurrent hash table access\n0x7a0   4     pool_size_state   uint        Pool size or status variable",
