      "name": "RemoveResourceFromPool",
      "signature": "void RemoveResourceFromPool(void * pPoolManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a specific resource identified by its ID from the resource pool array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire lock on critical section to ensure thread-safe access to pool\n2. Load pool metadata (array base at +0x7a8, element count at +0x7a0, capacity at +0x7a4)\n3. Perform binary search on sorted resource pool array to locate target resource ID\n   - Search uses sorted array index with 8-byte element stride (resource ID at +0x4 offset)\n   - Track search bounds in low/mid/high indices\n   - Continue until exact match found or search range exhausted\n4. If resource not found in binary search, release lock and log error then terminate\n5. Once target found at index in EAX:\n   - Calculate number of elements remaining after removed element (count - index)\n   - Use memmove to shift remaining elements down by one slot (8 bytes each)\n   - Update pool element count (decrement by 1)\n6. Calculate memory usage adjustment based on resource data embedded at parameter +0x14\n   - Extract size field at +0x1c and count field at +0x20 from resource record\n   - Update cumulative memory metric at pool +0x17a8\n7. Check if post-removal capacity allows shrinking pool (count + 0x40 < capacity)\n   - If capacity reduction needed: reallocate array to smaller size (capacity - 0x20 * 8 bytes)\n   - If reallocation fails, log error and terminate\n8. Release lock and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pPoolManager (ECX): Pointer to resource pool manager structure containing pool array, metadata, and synchronization objects\n  dwResourceId (EDX): Resource ID value to search for and remove from pool\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function terminates on any error condition\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Resource not found: Logs error at 0x2bf, calls shutdown sequence\n  - Reallocation failure: Logs error at 0x2b4, attempts recovery then shutdown\n  - Thread synchronization: Uses critical section lock/unlock at offsets 0x4 (lock at 0x6ff61690)\n  \nStructure Layout (ResourcePoolNode):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\n  ------  ----  -----------------  --------  ----------------------------------\n  +0x0    4     reserved            uint      Reserved space\n  +0x4    ?     lockObject          CRITICAL  Synchronization critical section\n  ...\n  +0x7a0 4     elementCount        uint      Current number of elements in pool\n  +0x7a4 4     capacity            uint      Total allocated capacity\n  +0x7a8 4     pArrayElements      pointer   Base address of sorted element array\n  +0x17a8 4    memoryUsage         uint      Cumulative memory bytes in use",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
