      "name": "InsertPoolBlockSorted",
      "signature": "void InsertPoolBlockSorted(uint * pPoolBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Inserts a pool block pointer into a sorted pool block table using binary search.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load context pointer from EAX and critical section lock address at offset +0x4\n2. Initialize critical section lock with magic value 0x258 for validation\n3. Enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access to pool block table\n4. Check if block table capacity <= current block count\n5. If expansion needed: increment capacity by 0x20 slots\n6. Reallocate block table to new capacity * 8 bytes (8-byte entries)\n7. Check if reallocation succeeded; if failed, log error and exit with code -1\n8. Load pool config pointer from pPoolBlock[5] (offset +0x14)\n9. Calculate slot array size: (config[0x1c] + 0x1f) >> 5 * 4 bytes\n10. Update global memory usage counter at offset 0x17a8\n11. Load current block count from context offset 0x7a0\n12. Initialize binary search: low=0, high=blockCount, mid=0\n13. For each iteration: compute mid = (high - low) >> 1 + low\n14. Compare table[mid].sort_key (offset +4 in entry) with *pPoolBlock\n15. If key < *pPoolBlock: search upper half (low = mid + 1)\n16. If key >= *pPoolBlock: search lower half (high = mid)\n17. Continue until low >= high (insertion point found)\n18. If insertion position < block count, shift existing entries rightward by 8 bytes using memmove\n19. Store pPoolBlock pointer at table[insertionIndex] (offset +0)\n20. Store *pPoolBlock (sort key) at table[insertionIndex] (offset +4)\n21. Increment block count at context offset 0x7a0\n22. Finalize critical section lock with magic value 0x282\n23. Leave critical section and return\n\nParameters:\npPoolBlock - Pointer to pool block structure containing sort key at offset +0 and pool configuration at offset +0x14\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; modifies global pool block table in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall convention with 4-byte stack parameter cleanup\n- Implicit context pointer stored in ESI during execution\n- Block table stored at context+0x7a8 (pointer to table)\n- Block table capacity at context+0x7a4\n- Block count at context+0x7a0\n- Memory usage counter at context+0x17a8\n- Binary search operates on 8-byte entries: {uint *pointer, uint key}\n- Memory allocation failure triggers fatal error shutdown\n- All registers preserved via stack push (EBP, ESI, EDI, EBX)",
