      "signature": "void * AllocateMemorySlotFromPool(void * pPoolConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a pre-allocated pool of fixed-size slots.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pool configuration is non-null, using default config if needed\n2. Initialize pool allocator if not already done (calls InitializePoolAllocator)\n3. Validate input allocation size and calculate required pool index using bit-scan\n4. Acquire critical section lock for thread-safe pool access\n5. Call FindAvailablePoolSlot to locate an unused slot in the computed pool\n6. If slot not found, log error and terminate via LogErrorAndShutdown\n7. Mark the slot as in-use by setting bit in usage bitmap using bit-position math\n8. Update linked list pointers to maintain pool node chain\n9. Calculate return value as (poolBaseAddress + slotIndex * slotStride)\n10. Release critical section lock\n11. Return pointer to allocated memory slot\n\nParameters:\npPoolConfig (void*): Configuration structure for pool memory (uses default if NULL)\nallocationSize (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Pointer to allocated memory slot, or error path terminates program\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Size 0x10 or less returns NULL (minimum size is 0x10)\n- Size 0x1f or less calculated using bit-scan-reverse (BSR) + increment\n- Pool index validated against pool configuration maximum index (offset +0x1c)\n- Slot tracking uses bit-level bitmap at offset +0x1c with 32-bit DWORD entries\n- Multiple pool nodes linked via offset +0x10 (next) and +0xc (previous)\n- Error codes: 0x4f3, 0x4f7, 0x4f8, 0x4ff, 0x50d logged on failure",
