      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a resource buffer with validation and thread-safe synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pExistingBuffer is NULL, allocate new buffer from default resource pool via AllocateMemorySlotFromPool()\n2. If default allocation fails, log error code 0x62d and terminate process\n3. If pExistingBuffer is provided, validate using FindResourceByThreshold() to locate resource metadata\n4. If validation fails, attempt fallback allocation via ReallocateBlockInHashPool() with specified bufferSize\n5. If fallback allocation fails, log error code 0x635 and terminate process\n6. Extract critical section pointer from validated resource metadata at offset +0x14\n7. Calculate buffer element index: (pExistingBuffer - basePointer) / elementSize\n8. Verify index is within valid bounds using maxElements field at offset +0x1c\n9. If index out of bounds, log error code 0x648 and terminate process\n10. Enter critical section lock to protect allocation bitmap check\n11. Test allocation bitmap at [bitmapPtr + (index >> 5) * 4] to verify slot is allocated\n12. If bit not set in bitmap, exit critical section and log error code 0x6a0\n13. If elementSize <= bufferSize, exit critical section and return pExistingBuffer (no copy needed)\n14. If elementSize > bufferSize, allocate new larger buffer from resource pool\n15. If new allocation fails, log error code 0x68b and terminate process\n16. Copy data using optimized REP MOVSD for dword chunks: (elementSize >> 2) dwords\n17. Copy remaining bytes using REP MOVSB: (elementSize & 3) bytes\n18. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement() to clean up original buffer\n19. Return newly allocated and copied buffer pointer\n20. All critical errors (allocation failures, out-of-bounds) call _exit() and do not return normally\n\nParameters:\npResourceNode: Pointer to resource manager/allocator object containing pool metadata\npExistingBuffer: Optional pointer to existing buffer; NULL means allocate from default pool\nbufferSize: Requested size for allocation; compared against elementSize to determine copy behavior\nnReserved_1: Reserved parameter (unused, passed for calling convention alignment)\nnReserved_2: Reserved parameter (unused, passed for calling convention alignment)\n\nReturns:\nvoid *: Pointer to allocated buffer on success (either pExistingBuffer or newly allocated)\nNULL: Never returned for allocation failures (process terminates via _exit)\nFunction never returns normally on critical errors\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pExistingBuffer triggers allocation from default pool without validation\n- Bitmap tracking ensures double allocation prevention via locked bitmap test\n- Critical section synchronization prevents race conditions during bitmap test\n- elementSize at [criticalSection + 0x18] is the authoritative element size, not bufferSize\n- Memory copy is optimized: dword moves (REP MOVSD) then byte moves (REP MOVSB)\n- Total bytes copied = (elementSize >> 2) * 4 + (elementSize & 3) = elementSize\n- Error codes map to file locations: 0x62d=line 621, 0x635=line 629, 0x63c=line 636, 0x648=line 648, 0x68b=line 651, 0x6a0=line 672, 0x69e=line 670\n\nStructure Layout (Resource Pool Control Block):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n0x00    0x4   basePointer             void*     Base address of allocated memory pool\n0x04    0x4   allocationBitmap        uint*     Pointer to bitmap array (1 bit per slot)\n0x14    0x4   criticalSectionPtr      HANDLE    Synchronization object for bitmap access\n0x18    0x4   elementSize             uint      Size of each pool element in bytes\n0x1c    0x4   maxElements             uint      Maximum number of elements in pool",
