      "name": "InitializeEventQueueManager",
      "signature": "EventQueueManager * InitializeEventQueueManager(EventQueueManager * pQueueManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "EventQueueManager *",
      "comment": "Initializes the EventQueueManager structure for multi-threaded event processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Establish SEH exception handling frame for Visual C++ runtime compatibility\n2. Zero out initial 5 DWORD fields (0x00-0x10) in manager structure\n3. Initialize critical section at offset +0x14 for thread-safe access to queue\n4. Store manager pointer in global variable g_pGameEventContext for callback access\n5. Zero out reserved/padding fields at offsets 0x2c-0x38\n6. Create auto-reset event object via CreateEventA with no initial signal\n7. Store event handle at offset +0x3c for signaling queue worker thread\n8. Create event processing worker thread via CreateThread with thread routine\n9. Store thread handle at offset +0x40 and thread ID at offset +0x44\n10. Restore exception handler frame and return initialized manager pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pQueueManager: EventQueueManager* - Uninitialized manager structure (min 72 bytes)\n                Must have space for critical section (24 bytes) + event/thread handles\n\nReturns:\n  EventQueueManager* - Returns input pQueueManager pointer after initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses __stdcall convention; caller removes 4-byte parameter from stack\n  - Exception handling frame for SEH compatibility with Visual C++ runtime\n  - Thread created with default security attributes and stack size\n  - Event is auto-reset type: automatically signals non-signaled after wait\n  - g_pGameEventContext global maintains reference for callback functions\n  - Magic constant 0x6ff61d20 is address of ProcessEventQueueIfInitialized thread routine\n\nStructure Layout (EventQueueManager):\n  Offset | Size | Field            | Type           | Purpose\n  -------|------|------------------|----------------|--------------------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | field_0          | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x04   | 4    | field_4          | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x08   | 4    | field_8          | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x0c   | 4    | field_c          | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x10   | 4    | field_10         | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x14   | 24   | critical_section | RTL_CRIT_SEC   | Thread synchronization critical section\n  0x2c   | 4    | field_2c         | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x30   | 4    | field_30         | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x34   | 4    | field_34         | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x38   | 4    | field_38         | uint           | Reserved/initialized to 0\n  0x3c   | 4    | event_handle     | HANDLE         | Auto-reset event for queue signaling\n  0x40   | 4    | thread_handle    | HANDLE         | Event processing worker thread handle\n  0x44   | 4    | thread_id        | uint           | Worker thread identifier",
