      "name": "FindValueInRangeList",
      "signature": "int FindValueInRangeList(void * pRangeNode, uint dwSearchValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Check if a value falls within a range defined by a range node structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pRangeNode is not NULL\n2. Load the minimum range boundary from the structure\n3. Check if searchValue is less than minimum (unsigned comparison)\n4. Check if searchValue is greater than maximum boundary\n5. Test the result and return 1 (TRUE) if within range, 0 (FALSE) otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pRangeNode (__fastcall ECX): Pointer to range definition structure containing min/max bounds\n- dwSearchValue (__fastcall EDX): Unsigned 32-bit value to check against range\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: 1 (TRUE) if dwSearchValue is within the range defined by pRangeNode, 0 (FALSE) otherwise\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns FALSE if pRangeNode is NULL\n- Uses unsigned comparison for boundary checking\n- Range structure appears to contain minimum at offset +0x0 and maximum at offset +0x4",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:425e755ab4ac9b03d9f7d2bebb596480",
