      "name": "IterateModulesAndLoadSymbols",
      "signature": "char * IterateModulesAndLoadSymbols(void * pModuleListHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Iterates through a module linked list and loads debugging symbols for each module.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessNetworkNodeList to get the head of the module linked list\n2. Initialize logging connections for status and symbol loading messages\n3. Iterate through each module in the linked list:\n   a. Load the next module pointer from offset +0x20c for loop continuation\n   b. Copy the module name (at offset +0) to moduleNameBuffer using byte-by-byte copying\n   c. Copy the symbol path (at offset +0x104) to symbolPathBuffer using byte-by-byte copying\n   d. Call the symbol loader function pointer with module info and both buffers\n   e. If g_dwInitializationCounter equals 0, log the operation result\n      - If loader returned 0 (failure), call GetLastError and log error message\n      - If loader returned non-zero (success), log success message with module name\n4. Return the module list head pointer in EAX\n\nParameters:\npModuleListHandle - Handle or pointer to module list context (passed to symbol loader)\n\nReturns:\nPointer to the module list head (from ProcessNetworkNodeList)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_dwInitializationCounter controls logging - when 0, results are logged; otherwise silent\n- Module structure layout:\n  Offset +0x00: Module name string (null-terminated)\n  Offset +0x104: Symbol path string (null-terminated)\n  Offset +0x204: Module base address (4 bytes)\n  Offset +0x208: Module size/flags (4 bytes)\n  Offset +0x20c: Pointer to next module in linked list (4 bytes)\n- String copying uses byte-by-byte method to fill temporary stack buffers\n- Module list may be empty (NULL pointer check at start)\n- Symbol loader may fail if paths are invalid or symbols not found",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
