      "signature": "int InitializeSymbolHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize symbol handler for the current process with thread-safe synchronization.\\n\\nSummary:\\nInitializes the Ghidra/DbgHelp symbol handler for symbol enumeration and stack walking. Uses a critical section lock to prevent race conditions during initialization, maintains a call counter to support lazy initialization, and manages a linked list of symbol elements that are deallocated during cleanup.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Acquire g_SymbolHandlerCriticalSection lock for thread safety\\n2. Check g_dwSymbolHandlerInitEnabled flag; skip if disabled\\n3. Increment g_dwSymbolInitializeCallCount to track initialization calls\\n4. If first initialization (counter was 0):\\n   a. Check if g_szSymbolSearchPath has been initialized\\n   b. Call BuildSymbolSearchPath to initialize search path if needed\\n   c. Get current process handle via GetCurrentProcess\\n   d. Call symbol handler via g_pfnSymInitialize function pointer\\n   e. If initialization fails: log error via InitializeNetworkConnection, cleanup via g_pfnSymCleanup, reset counter, unlock and return 0\\n   f. Increment counter again for tracking\\n   g. Get current options via g_pfnSymGetOptions function pointer\\n   h. Set SYMOPT_DEFERRED_LOADS flag (0x10) via g_pfnSymSetOptions\\n   i. Load initial symbol elements via LoadSymbolsForModules\\n5. Iterate through linked list of symbol elements:\\n   a. Load next pointer from current element at offset +0x20c\\n   b. Deallocate current element via DeallocateResourcePoolElement\\n   c. Continue with next element if not NULL\\n6. Release g_SymbolHandlerCriticalSection lock\\n7. Return 1 for success or already initialized, 0 for failure\\n\\nReturns:\\n1 if initialization succeeded or was already completed\\n0 if symbol handler initialization failed (failure path taken)\\n\\nParameters:\\n(none) - This function takes no parameters; it operates on global state\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- First call with g_dwSymbolInitializeCallCount == 0 performs full initialization\\n- Subsequent calls skip initialization and return success immediately\\n- Symbol element list deallocated via offset +0x20c next pointer chain\\n- Critical section synchronization prevents concurrent initialization race conditions\\n- If symbol initialization fails, the counter is reset to 0 and cleanup is performed\\n- SYMOPT_DEFERRED_LOADS (0x10) flag enables lazy loading of symbols",
