      "name": "SHA1_Final",
      "signature": "void SHA1_Final(void * this, int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Finalizes SHA1 digest computation by padding message and extracting the 160-bit hash.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 64-bit message length (bit count) from context offsets +0x00 and +0x04\n2. Extract 8 bytes from 64-bit bit count by right-shifting and masking (SHRD/SHR pattern)\n3. Store extracted length bytes on stack (ESP+0x04 to ESP+0x0b)\n4. Calculate padding block size: (0xfffffff7 - (bit_count >> 3)) & 0x3f + 1\n5. Call SHA1InputUpdate with g_SHA1PaddingBlock and calculated padding length\n6. Call SHA1InputUpdate with stack length field (8 bytes) from ESP+0x04\n7. Extract 5 digest DWORDs from context offset +0x08 and onwards\n8. Convert each DWORD to big-endian by shifting and extracting bytes\n9. Write 20 bytes (5 DWORDs) to pDigestOutput in big-endian format\n10. Return with message digest in output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- implicit this (ECX): Pointer to context object containing:\n  - [this+0x00]: Message bit count (lower 32 bits)\n  - [this+0x04]: Message length (upper 32 bits)\n  - [this+0x08]: First digest DWORD (context.state[0])\n  - [this+0x0c-0x1c]: Remaining 4 digest DWORDs (context.state[1-4])\n- pContext: SHA1_CTX_Context structure (passed as second parameter in disassembly)\n- pDigestOutput: Pointer to 20-byte buffer for final 160-bit hash\n\nReturns:\nVoid. Digest written to pDigestOutput[0:19] in big-endian format.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message length stored as 64-bit big-endian value requiring byte extraction\n- Padding calculation accounts for current position using magic value 0xfffffff7\n- Digest DWORDs converted to big-endian format (high byte first in memory)\n- Loop executes exactly 5 times to process all digest state DWORDs\n- Final call with 8-byte length field completes SHA1 finalization per FIPS 180-1 spec\n- Calling convention __thiscall passes implicit context pointer in ECX register",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:2",
