      "name": "SetInitializeFlag",
      "signature": "void SetInitializeFlag(int pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the initialization flag for an object structure and triggers game context initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Write 0x1 to the object's initialization flag field at offset 0x108 (DWORD at array index 0x42)\n2. Tail-call to InitializeGameContext() to perform actual initialization based on flag state\n\nParameters:\npObject (ECX) - Pointer to object structure requiring initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return (tail-call to InitializeGameContext)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nOffset 0x108 corresponds to array index 0x42 in a 4-byte element array. The initialization flag signals the game context that the object requires default value initialization. This is a lightweight initialization trigger function that delegates to InitializeGameContext for the actual setup logic.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
