      "name": "DispatchCpuidLeaf",
      "signature": "uint DispatchCpuidLeaf(uint cpuidLeaf)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Executes CPUID instruction and returns EDX register output\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8 bytes on stack for local storage\n2. Save EBX register to preserve callee-saved register\n3. Store ECX input parameter (cpuidLeaf) to stack at [ESP+4]\n4. Load cpuidLeaf from stack to EAX register\n5. Execute CPUID instruction with leaf in EAX\n6. Store EDX output (CPUID result field) to stack at [ESP+8]\n7. Load EDX value from stack to EAX for return\n8. Restore EBX from stack\n9. Deallocate 8 bytes from stack\n10. Return EDX value to caller\n\nParameters:\n  cpuidLeaf [ECX] - CPUID leaf number (0x0, 0x1, 0x2, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  uint (EAX) - EDX register value from CPUID instruction execution\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses __fastcall convention: input in ECX, output in EAX\n  - Stack frame of 8 bytes supports 2 local DWORD variables\n  - EBX is saved/restored as it is callee-saved register\n  - Direct CPUID execution without dispatcher logic\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Stack Frame (relative to ESP at function entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name         Type    Description\n  ------  ----  -----------------  -----  -----------------------------------------\n  +4      4     cpuidLeafInput     uint   ECX parameter: CPUID leaf number\n  +8      4     edxResult          uint   EDX output from CPUID instruction",
