      "name": "GetCpuVersionInfo",
      "signature": "ulong GetCpuVersionInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulong",
      "comment": "Retrieves CPU version and feature information using the CPUID instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Execute CPUID instruction with EAX=1 to request processor version and feature information\n2. The CPUID instruction atomically executes on the processor, storing:\n   - EAX: Processor version information (stepping ID, model, family, processor type)\n   - EBX: Additional processor info (brand index, CLFLUSH line size, APIC ID, logical processor count)\n3. Store the EAX result on the stack at [ESP + 0x4] for safe preservation across PUSH/POP\n4. Load the preserved EAX result back into EAX for return value\n5. Restore saved registers (EBX, ECX) and return\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nulong - Processor version signature in format combining CPUID(1) results:\n  - Low 32-bits (EAX): Family, Model, Stepping ID\n  - High 32-bits (EBX): Brand Index, Logical CPU count, APIC ID\n  - Used by system initialization to validate CPU capabilities and identify processor type\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- CPUID with EAX=1 is universally supported on all modern x86/x64 processors\n- The CPUID instruction can change CPU state in registers; preserving EBX is critical\n- Result encodes processor family, model, and stepping for version validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
