      "name": "GetCpuVendorString",
      "signature": "ulonglong GetCpuVendorString(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ulonglong",
      "comment": "Retrieves CPU vendor string via CPUID instruction for processor identification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetCpuVersionInfo() to retrieve CPU signature with model/family/stepping bits\n2. Extract model field from signature bits 4-7: (signature >> 8) & 0xF\n3. Call GetCpuVendorId() to check CPUID instruction support (returns 1 if supported)\n4. Validate processor: Check if model >= 7 (always valid) OR (model == 6 AND signature bits 4-7 >= 0x80)\n5. If validation fails, return 0 (processor too old or CPUID unsupported)\n6. If validation passes, execute CPUID instruction with EAX=1 (Get CPU Version/Brand/Feature)\n7. Store vendor string from CPUID EBX register at stack offset +0xc\n8. Load 32-bit vendor string result from stack and return as 64-bit value (EDX:EAX)\n\nParameters:\nNone (no function parameters)\n\nReturns:\n- Success: 64-bit vendor string from CPUID EBX register, e.g., 0x756e6547 = \"uneG\" (GenuineIntel)\n- Failure: 0 (processor doesn't support CPUID 1 or model validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Model field must be >= 6 to support CPUID function 1 (GenuineIntel requirement)\n- Signature bits 4-7 threshold 0x80 represents stepping requirements for model 6 processors\n- CPUID EBX contains first 4 bytes of vendor string; other registers contain remaining bytes\n- Some older Pentium/386 processors lack CPUID instruction entirely\n\nCPU Signature Structure (from GetCpuVersionInfo):\nOffset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n0       8     cpu_sig      uint64    Full CPU signature (EDX:EAX from CPUID 0)\n- bits 0-3: stepping ID (revision level)\n- bits 4-7: model ID (processor variant)\n- bits 8-11: family ID (processor family)\n- bits 12-31: reserved",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:6d918fcf86a14b5893be47d6edc8cfbb",
