      "name": "ComputeCrc16LowercaseString",
      "signature": "ushort ComputeCrc16LowercaseString(char * pString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ushort",
      "comment": "Computes a case-insensitive CRC16 checksum of a null-terminated string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize CRC value to 0xFFFF (standard CRC16 initial state)\n2. Load first character from input string pointer (pString)\n3. Convert character to lowercase using tolower() C library function\n4. Loop through all characters until null terminator:\n   a. XOR lowercase character with low byte of current CRC value\n   b. Use XOR result (masked to 8 bits) as index into CRC lookup table\n   c. Right-shift current CRC value by 2 bits\n   d. XOR the shifted value with looked-up CRC table entry (16-bit value)\n   e. Store XOR result as new CRC value\n   f. Load next character and convert to lowercase\n5. Return final 16-bit CRC value in AX register\n\nParameters:\npString - Pointer to null-terminated input string (char *)\n\nReturns:\nAX - 16-bit CRC16 checksum value (ushort), range 0x0000-0xFFFF\nFor empty string (immediate null terminator), returns 0xFFFF\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- All input characters are converted to lowercase before CRC processing\n- CRC lookup table uses 256 entries (512 bytes total) at g_CrcLookupTable (0x6ff7f010)\n- Table index computed as (lowerChar XOR crcValue) & 0xFF (8-bit mask)\n- CRC is right-shifted by 2 bits (SHR SI, 0x2) each iteration\n- Return uses __stdcall convention: caller pops 4-byte argument\n\nStructure Layout:\nCRC Lookup Table (g_CrcLookupTable at 0x6ff7f010):\n- 256 entries, each 2 bytes (16-bit WORD)\n- Total size: 512 bytes\n- Format: Pre-computed CRC16 polynomial values for all byte combinations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
