      "name": "RegisterSlotIfUnique",
      "signature": "void RegisterSlotIfUnique(void * pSlotTable, uint dwSlotValue, uint slotId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Registers a slot in a slot table if the slot ID is not already present.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current slot count from offset +0x848 in pSlotTable\n2. If count >= 0x100 (256 slots maximum), skip registration and return immediately\n3. Initialize slot index counter to 0\n4. If count > 0, enter loop to search existing slots\n5. Point to first slot entry at offset +0x48 (stride is 8 bytes per entry)\n6. Loop through each slot comparing the slot ID at current entry with incoming slotId\n7. If exact match found, return early (prevents duplicate registration)\n8. If no match found, calculate insertion position as offset +0x48 + (count * 8)\n9. Write slotId to array at calculated position\n10. Write dwSlotValue to adjacent offset +0x4c + (count * 8)\n11. Increment slot count at offset +0x848\n12. Return\n\nParameters:\n- pSlotTable (ECX): Pointer to slot table structure containing slots array and count\n- dwSlotValue (EDX): Associated value to register for this slot\n- slotId (stack param): Slot identifier to register\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, slots registered in-place in pSlotTable)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns silently if slot count already >= 0x100 (table full, no slots added)\n- Early return if slot ID already exists (duplicate prevention)\n- Each slot entry occupies 8 bytes total (2 dwords: slot ID + value)\n- Maximum capacity is 256 slots (0x100)\n- No error indication for full table or duplicates\n\nStructure Layout of pSlotTable:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type        Description\n  +0x48   8*N   slotEntries[]     uint[256]   Array of (slotId, value) pairs, stride 8\n  +0x848  4     dwSlotCount       uint        Current number of registered slots",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:12",
