      "signature": "int InsertHashTableNode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Inserts or increments a node in a hash table using chaining collision resolution.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load hash value from EAX pointer parameter\n2. Calculate hash bucket index using modulo division by bucket count at offset +0x10\n3. Load bucket array pointer from hash table context at offset +0x40\n4. Walk collision chain at bucket index to search for existing match\n5. If matching node found, increment its reference count at offset +0x4 and return 1\n6. If no match found, allocate new 12-byte node from memory pool\n7. Initialize new node: store hash value at +0x0, set count to 1 at +0x4\n8. Link new node into collision chain and insert as bucket head\n9. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\nEAX: Pointer to value to insert (hash value loaded from [EAX])\nEBX: Pointer to hash table context with +0x10 bucket count, +0x40 bucket array\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful insertion or duplicate found\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMemory allocation failure triggers LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 0x914",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:10c847a8e9b4b77bbf6cb145b9ba5290",
