      "name": "CountTotalSlottedEntities",
      "signature": "int CountTotalSlottedEntities(int pManager)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Counts total entities across all slots in a slotted container with thread safety.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate manager pointer; return 0 if null\n2. Initialize entity counter to 0 (EDI register)\n3. Get critical section pointer at offset 0x854 from manager base\n4. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity with magic value 0xaad for unlock/prepare\n5. Enter critical section (LPCRITICAL_SECTION) to synchronize access\n6. Load slot count from manager offset 0x87c into EAX\n7. Load slot array pointer from manager offset 0x870 into ESI\n8. If slot count > 0, iterate through each slot (4-byte strides)\n9. For each slot, load entity pointer and traverse entity chain at offset 0x5bc\n10. Count each entity by incrementing counter, continue until null entity pointer\n11. Exit critical section and return total entity count in EAX\n\nParameters:\npManager (int): Pointer to slotted entity manager structure with offsets:\n  - 0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n  - 0x870: Pointer to array of entity slot pointers  \n  - 0x87c: Count of slots in entity array\n\nReturns:\nint: Total count of entities found across all slots and entity chains, or 0 if manager is null\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if pManager is null (safety check)\n- Handles empty slots gracefully (null pointers skip increment)\n- Thread-safe via critical section for multi-threaded access\n- Each entity links via pointer at offset 0x5bc (chain traversal)\n- Slot array uses 4-byte stride for pointer access",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
