      "name": "ThrottleClientPacketRate",
      "signature": "bool ThrottleClientPacketRate(ClientConnection * pClientConn, uint dwPacketSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__d2call",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Implements client packet rate limiting and throttling with automatic decay.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current system tick count via GetTickCount\n2. Enter critical section to protect packet counter access\n3. Atomically increment packet counter by dwPacketSize bytes\n4. Exit critical section and check if counter exceeds 1000 byte threshold\n5. If counter > 1000: Load permission flags and call ValidatePermissionMask to check if client\n   is banned or has permission to exceed limit, return validation result as bool\n6. Otherwise: Calculate elapsed time since last decay (dwCurrentTick - lastDecayTime)\n7. If elapsed time >= 1000 milliseconds:\n   - Enter critical section again to perform atomic decay\n   - Update lastDecayTime to current tick count\n   - If counter < 200 bytes: reset counter to 0 (underflow prevention)\n   - Else: subtract 200 bytes from counter (rate limit recovery)\n   - Exit critical section\n8. Return true (packet accepted for processing)\n\nParameters:\npClientConn [EBX/__d2call] - Pointer to ClientConnection structure containing rate limit state:\n  +0x18: permissionFlags (uint) - Permission/banned status bitmask (checked by ValidatePermissionMask)\n  +0x24: lastDecayTime (DWORD) - Timestamp of last decay operation (milliseconds)\n  +0x28: packetCounter (uint) - Accumulated packet bytes since last decay (0-1000+ range)\n  +0x2c: criticalSection (CRITICAL_SECTION) - Thread synchronization object (24 bytes)\ndwPacketSize [Stack] - Size of incoming packet in bytes to add to rate limiter counter\n\nReturns:\nbool - true if packet should be accepted for processing, false if throttled/banned:\n  Returns false only if ValidatePermissionMask returns 0 (banned or denied)\n  Returns true for all other paths including decay and counter reset\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 1000: Packet counter overflow threshold triggering permission validation\n- Magic number 1000: Millisecond time interval for counter decay recovery\n- Magic number 200: Number of bytes decayed per interval (represents max 200 bytes/second limit)\n- Counter underflow: If counter < 200 bytes at decay time, reset to 0 instead of negative value\n- Permission validation: Client must pass ValidatePermissionMask to exceed 1000-byte threshold\n\nStructure Layout (ClientConnection):\nOffset  Size  Field Name            Type      Description\n+0x18   4     permissionFlags       uint      Permission/banned flags checked by validator\n+0x24   4     lastDecayTime         DWORD     Timestamp in milliseconds of previous decay\n+0x28   4     packetCounter         uint      Accumulated packet bytes in current interval\n+0x2c   24    criticalSection       CS        RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION for atomic updates",
