      "name": "ClearLinkedListWithCriticalSection",
      "signature": "void ClearLinkedListWithCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears a linked list by iterating through all nodes and deallocating each one under thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to critical section at context + 0x854 offset\n2. Validate critical section structure integrity using magic value 0x9a5\n3. Enter critical section to synchronize list access across threads\n4. Load first node pointer from context + 0x84c (list head offset)\n5. Test if list is empty (first node is NULL)\n6. If empty, jump to cleanup; if not, begin iteration loop\n7. Loop through all nodes:\n   a. Store current node in EAX for processing\n   b. Load next node pointer from offset +0xc within current node\n   c. Push validation magic 0x9ab for node validation\n   d. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate current node\n   e. Test if next node exists (ESI != 0)\n   f. If more nodes, repeat loop from step 7a\n8. Clear the list head pointer by setting context + 0x84c to 0\n9. Leave critical section to release thread lock\n10. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- Context implicit in EBX: Base pointer to structure containing:\n  * Linked list head pointer at offset +0x84c\n  * Critical section handle at offset +0x854\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee cleanup (RET)\n- EBX is unaffected register providing implicit context parameter\n- Critical section ensures thread-safe list clearing across multiple threads\n- Linked list nodes contain next pointer at offset +0xc from node base address\n- Magic validation numbers: 0x9a5 for critical section, 0x9ab for node processing\n- Each node is deallocated via DeallocateResourcePoolElement before moving to next\n- Validates critical section before acquiring lock to detect corruption\n- Source file path reference at 0x6ff78fac used for error reporting\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe context structure (passed implicitly in EBX) has the following fields:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n0x84c   4     dwListHeadPointer       DWORD       Points to first node in linked list\n0x854   4     lpCriticalSection       CRITICAL_SECTION* Handle to synchronization object\nThe linked list node structure has:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type        Description\n0x0     ?     [node data]             varies      Node-specific data\n0xc     4     pNextNode               void*       Pointer to next node in list",
