      "comment": "Removes expired entries from a timeout-managed linked list in thread-safe manner.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount() for timeout calculations\n2. Lock access to linked list with EnterCriticalSection() at context+0x854\n3. First pass: Remove expired entries from head of list\n   - Load head pointer from context+0x84c\n   - While head exists and age > 15000ms (0x3a98):\n     - Load node timestamp at offset +4\n     - Calculate age: current_tick - timestamp\n     - If expired, load next pointer at offset +0xc\n     - Update head to point to next, call DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n4. Second pass: Remove stale entries from interior of remaining list\n   - For each remaining node, check its next pointer\n   - If next node age >= 15000ms, unlink it and deallocate\n   - Otherwise advance to next node\n5. Unlock critical section with LeaveCriticalSection()\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- Implicit EAX (pContextData): Context pointer structure\n  - Offset 0x84c: Head pointer to timeout entries linked list\n  - Offset 0x850: Tail pointer to linked list\n  - Offset 0x854: CRITICAL_SECTION for thread synchronization\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success (always returns 1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0x3a98 (15000 decimal): Timeout threshold in milliseconds\n- Two-pass algorithm: First removes oldest entries from head, then stale interior entries\n- Thread-safe: All operations wrapped in critical section\n- Handles empty list: Checks for NULL pointers before dereferencing\n- Node structure: ID(0), timestamp(+4), count(+8), next(+0xc)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
