      "name": "FindHashTableEntryById",
      "signature": "int FindHashTableEntryById(int pHashTable, int nEntryId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for an entry with a specific ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate hash bucket index from nEntryId using bitwise AND\n2. Calculate critical section address offset (24 bytes per bucket)\n3. Enter critical section to serialize access to hash table\n4. Load the head of the linked list for the calculated bucket\n5. Iterate through the linked list comparing node IDs with nEntryId\n6. If a matching ID is found, retrieve the associated node data from offset +0x10\n7. Exit critical section and return the node data pointer, or -1 if not found\n\nParameters:\npHashTable - Pointer to the hash table structure containing bucket array and list heads\nnEntryId - ID value to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\nEAX - Pointer to the found entry node data (from offset +0x10), or -1 if entry not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If the entry ID is not found in the hash table, the function returns 0xFFFFFFFF (-1)\n- The bucket index calculation masks nEntryId with a value from offset +0xC in the hash table\n- Each bucket is 24 bytes apart (ESI*3*8), suggesting 3 items per bucket or stride pattern\n- The function uses critical sections (EnterCriticalSection/LeaveCriticalSection) to ensure thread-safe access",
