      "name": "RetrieveSocketPeerAddress",
      "signature": "void RetrieveSocketPeerAddress(void * pSocketManager, uint socketId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Retrieves the peer address for a given socket within a socket manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate local stack space for socket node pointer and socket handle storage (20 bytes)\n2. Save EBX register (callee-saved)\n3. Load socket manager pointer parameter into EBX\n4. Load socket ID parameter into EAX\n5. Enter critical section to protect socket list access\n6. Calculate socket node address using: (socket_id << 1) + (socket_id << 3) for array indexing\n7. Load current socket node from calculated offset\n8. Test if socket node is valid (non-zero)\n9. If invalid, jump to check_socket_valid to skip processing\n10. Load socket handle from node offset (+0xc)\n11. Compare socket handle with target socket ID\n12. If handles match, jump to socket_found to process\n13. If not matching, test for next node pointer\n14. If next node exists, jump to socket_found and continue\n15. Otherwise, proceed to error handling section\n16. In error handler: call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity for validation\n17. Call getpeername to retrieve peer socket address\n18. Load and store peer address information\n19. Leave critical section to unlock\n20. Clear EAX register (return void)\n21. Restore EBX register (callee-saved)\n22. Cleanup stack (callee cleanup with RET 0x8)\n\nParameters:\n- pSocketManager (EBX): Pointer to socket manager structure containing socket list\n- socketId (EAX): Socket ID to retrieve peer address for\n\nReturns:\n- void (returns in EAX, typically 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Socket list validation performed through ValidateDataStructureIntegrity call\n- Critical section protects concurrent access to socket list\n- Socket node array indexed by socket ID with stride calculation\n- If socket not found or invalid, skips to error handler\n- getpeername may fail if socket not connected or closed",
