      "name": "SearchHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "uint SearchHashTableEntry(void * pHashTable, uint searchValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for an entry matching the given search value.\\n\\nAcquires a critical section lock to ensure thread-safe access, then\\nperforms a hash table lookup by calculating the slot index from the search\\nvalue and traversing the collision chain at that slot. Validates the data\\nstructure integrity before traversing and handles both found and not-found\\ncases, returning the matching entry address or zero.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Save registers (EDI)\\n2. Enter critical section to acquire lock for thread safety\\n3. Calculate hash slot index: (searchValue & mask) << 2 + base\\n4. Load initial entry pointer at calculated slot\\n5. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity to verify table consistency\\n6. If initial entry is NULL, return 0 (not found)\\n7. Loop: compare current entry key with searchValue\\n8. If key matches, return current entry address\\n9. If key doesn't match, load next entry from collision chain\\n10. If next entry is NULL, return 0 (not found)\\n11. Continue loop with next entry\\n12. Exit critical section to release lock\\n13. Return result (entry address or 0)\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pHashTable (void*): Pointer to the hash table structure containing\\n  slot array and collision chain entries\\n- searchValue (uint): The search key value to locate in the table\\n\\nReturns:\\n- uint: Address/pointer to the matching hash table entry if found,\\n  or 0 if no matching entry exists in the table\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Thread safety ensured via critical section lock during entire operation\\n- Empty table (NULL entry at slot) returns 0\\n- Collision chains are NULL-terminated\\n- Data structure validation guards against corrupted table\\n- Returns entry pointer (not offset or index) for direct use",
