      "name": "SearchHashTableForNetworkAddress",
      "signature": "void SearchHashTableForNetworkAddress(int pHashTable, uint dwNetworkAddress, byte * pOutResult, int nReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Searches for a network address in a thread-safe hash table and returns the result via inet_ntoa conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash index by ANDing dwNetworkAddress with mask at pHashTable+0xc\n2. Calculate critical section offset by multiplying hash index by 0x18 (24 bytes per entry)\n3. Obtain critical section pointer from pHashTable+0x1c plus calculated offset\n4. Initialize critical section structure via ValidateDataStructureIntegrity\n5. Enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access during search\n6. Load head pointer of hash bucket from array at pHashTable+0x14 using hash index\n7. Iterate through linked list nodes, comparing node[0] with dwNetworkAddress\n8. If match found, extract network address from node[6] (12-byte offset)\n9. Convert network address to string via inet_ntoa function\n10. Call ImportTrampoline_Ordinal_501_JmpTarget to process converted result\n11. Leave critical section and return\n12. If end of list reached without match, set *pOutResult to 0 and return\n\nParameters:\n  pHashTable (int): Base address of hash table structure\n    +0x0c: Hash mask value (typically power-of-2 minus 1)\n    +0x14: Pointer to array of linked list head pointers\n    +0x1c: Pointer to array of critical section structures (24 bytes each)\n  dwNetworkAddress (uint): Network address to search for (IP in numeric form)\n  pOutResult (byte *): Output pointer for result flag (set to 0 if not found)\n  reserved (int): Reserved/unused parameter, passed for stdcall stack cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void. Result returned via side effect of inet_ntoa call or *pOutResult assignment.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty bucket: If hash bucket head pointer is NULL, returns immediately with *pOutResult=0\n  - Thread safety: All operations protected by critical section lock during entire search\n  - Data structure: Each critical section entry is 24 bytes (_RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION structure)\n  - Linked list stride: Node pointers are 4-byte offsets, next pointer at node[1]\n  - Network address field: Located at node offset +0x18 (24 bytes from node base)\n  - Hash computation: Uses simple AND operation with mask for O(1) lookup\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type              Description\n  ------  ----  ---------------   ----------------  -----------------------------------\n  +0x0c   4     dwHashMask        uint              Mask for hash index computation\n  +0x14   4     ppBucketHeads     uint**            Array of linked list head pointers\n  +0x1c   4     pCritSections     RTL_CRITICAL_SECTION*  Array of synchronization objects",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:2",
