      "signature": "int TrackConnectionUsageAndValidateLimit(ClientConnection * pConnection)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and tracks connection usage within timeout and rate limits.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if any connections are currently tracked (count > 0)\n2. If no connections, immediately return success\n3. Get current system tick count via GetTickCount()\n4. Calculate maximum allowed usage count as 2*connection_count + 3\n5. Enter critical section to protect connection list access\n6. Retrieve cleanup function pointer for expired entries\n7. Iterate through connection list looking for matching connection ID:\n   a. Compare node ID with target connection ID\n   b. If ID matches, check elapsed time vs 15000ms timeout\n   c. If not timed out, increment usage counter and validate against limit\n   d. If usage exceeds limit, leave critical section and return failure (0)\n   e. If timed out, reset usage counter and timestamp\n   f. Continue to next node if ID doesn't match\n8. If connection not found in list, allocate new connection entry:\n   a. Call memory allocation function to create new node\n   b. If allocation fails, log error and continue\n9. Initialize new node with connection ID, current timestamp, and usage=1\n10. Add new node to tail of linked list:\n    a. If list empty, set as head\n    b. If list has elements, link from previous tail\n11. Update list tail pointer to new node\n12. Leave critical section\n13. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\npConnection: Pointer to ClientConnection structure containing connection management state\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 if connection tracking succeeded, 0 if usage limit exceeded or error occurred\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Timeout value: 15000 milliseconds (0x3a98)\n- Dynamic limit: 2*active_connections + 3 (prevents resource exhaustion)\n- Empty list: Skips iteration and allocates first entry\n- Allocation failure: Logs error but continues processing\n- Critical section protection: Prevents race conditions during list traversal\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n------  ----  --------------------  ----------  -----------------------------------\n0x84c   4     list_head            pointer     Head of connection tracking list\n0x850   4     list_tail            pointer     Tail of connection tracking list\n0x884   4     active_count         dword       Count of active connections\n\nConnection Node Structure (accessed via [node+offset]):\nOffset  Size  Field Name           Type        Description\n------  ----  --------------------  ----------  -----------------------------------\n0x0     4     connection_id        dword       Connection identifier for lookup\n0x4     4     last_tick_count      dword       System tick at last activity/reset\n0x8     4     usage_counter        dword       Usage count (incremented per check)\n0xc     4     next_node            pointer     Next node in doubly-linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
