      "name": "FindAndActivateHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "bool FindAndActivateHashTableEntry(uint dwEntryId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Searches hash table for entry matching ID and activates it if found\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that the data structure is initialized and intact\n2. Enter critical section to ensure thread-safe access to hash table\n3. Calculate hash bucket index from entry ID using division\n4. Search the collision chain at the calculated bucket for matching entry\n5. If entry found with matching ID, mark it as active/activated\n6. If entry not found or validation fails, return false\n7. Leave critical section and return status (true if activated, false otherwise)\n\nParameters:\n- dwEntryId: The hash table entry ID to find and activate (DWORD, passed on stack)\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: bool value (true if entry found and activated, false if not found or error)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns false if data structure validation fails during entry\n- Returns false if entry with matching ID not found in hash table\n- Thread-safe operation protected by critical section locks\n- Handles hash collisions through linked list traversal\n\nStructure Layout:\nHash table entries are accessed through collision chains. Each entry\ncontains a unique ID field that must match dwEntryId. The activation\nfield is set when a matching entry is found.",
