      "name": "FindItemById",
      "signature": "void * FindItemById(int itemId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table structure for an item with the specified ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load item container count from structure offset +0x8\n2. Test if count is zero; if so, return NULL (early exit)\n3. Initialize bucket index to 0 and offset to 0\n4. For each bucket up to container count:\n   a. Calculate section base address: base_ptr + offset\n   b. Call validation function (0x6ff61690) with ID 0x33f\n   c. Enter critical section using g_pfnEnterCriticalSection\n   d. Load bucket head array pointer from structure offset +0x14\n   e. Get first item in bucket: bucket_head[bucket_index * 4]\n   f. Search linked list of items in bucket:\n      - Compare item ID at offset +0x10 with search ID\n      - If match found, jump to item_found handler\n      - Load next item from offset +0x4, continue if not NULL\n   g. Leave critical section when search completes\n   h. Increment bucket index and add 0x18 to offset for next bucket\n5. If item found in bucket, leave critical section and return item pointer in EAX\n6. If no match found after all buckets, return NULL\n\nParameters:\nitemId (int): The item ID to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\nvoid*: Pointer to the Item structure if found, NULL if not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty container (count <= 0): Returns NULL immediately\n- Item ID matching: Compares at offset +0x10 in item structure\n- Thread safety: Uses critical section locks before bucket searches\n- Bucket stride: Each bucket takes up 0x18 bytes of offset space\n- Bucket indexing: Uses scaled indexing with bucket_index * 4 for array access",
