      "signature": "uint * InitializeServerConnection(uint peerIPAddress, uint peerPort)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new server connection structure with client connection details.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x664 bytes (409 dwords) from memory pool for connection structure\n2. Zero-initialize the entire allocated structure using REP STOSD\n3. Enter main critical section to assign unique connection ID\n4. Increment global connection ID counter and store in structure offset +0x0\n5. Calculate ID hash bucket index using (connectionID AND hashMask)\n6. Enter ID hash bucket lock and insert connection into ID hash list by chaining\n7. Calculate port hash bucket index using (peerPort AND hashMask)\n8. Enter port hash bucket lock and insert connection into port hash list by chaining\n9. Initialize connection's internal critical section for synchronization\n10. Store peer IP at offset +0x10 and peer port at offset +0x18\n11. Store initialization timestamp (from CalculateElapsedTimeInSeconds) at offsets +0x98, +0x9c, +0xa0, +0xa4\n12. Insert connection into main global hash table via InsertHashTableNode\n13. Increment connection reference count via InterlockedIncrement\n14. Increment global connection counter at context offset +0x880\n15. Convert IP address to string representation via inet_ntoa\n16. Return pointer to initialized connection structure\n\nParameters:\npeerIPAddress: Client IP address in network byte order (32-bit unsigned integer)\npeerPort: Client port number in host byte order (32-bit unsigned integer)\nThis parameter (EBX): Pointer to game context structure containing:\n  - Offset +0x4: Connection ID counter (incremented for each new connection)\n  - Offset +0xc: Hash mask value (used to calculate bucket indices)\n  - Offset +0x14: Base pointer to ID hash list array\n  - Offset +0x1c: Base pointer to ID hash lock array\n  - Offset +0x20: Base pointer to port hash list array\n  - Offset +0x28: Port hash bucket lock array base\n  - Offset +0x854: Main synchronization critical section\n  - Offset +0x880: Global connection counter\n\nReturns:\nPointer to newly allocated and initialized connection structure (0x664 bytes).\nStructure layout (offsets in dwords):\n  +0x0: Connection ID (unique identifier)\n  +0x1: Next pointer for ID hash list chain\n  +0x2: Reference count (protected by InterlockedIncrement)\n  +0x4: Next pointer for port hash list chain\n  +0x5: Peer IP address (network byte order)\n  +0x6: Peer port number\n  +0x9-0xa: Reserved/initialization flags\n  +0x10: Critical section for connection synchronization\n  +0x16: State flag (set to 1)\n  +0x1c: Connection status (set to 2)\n  +0x1d: Reserved field\n  +0x26-0x29: Creation timestamp and maintenance timestamps\n  +0x98-0xa4: Timestamp cache fields\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Memory allocation failure logs error via LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 2\n- Hash collisions are handled via chaining in both ID and port hash lists\n- Both ID and port hash tables allow O(1) lookup on average for connection retrieval\n- Critical section locking prevents race conditions during concurrent connection creation\n- Structure is zero-initialized to ensure all fields have predictable initial state",
