      "name": "DisconnectSocketByIP",
      "signature": "void DisconnectSocketByIP(void * pSocketManager, in_addr ipAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Disconnects all socket connections associated with a specific IP address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate the socket manager structure integrity\n2. Convert the IP address to a string representation using inet_ntoa\n3. Acquire the critical section lock to ensure thread-safe access\n4. Iterate through all socket entries in the socket manager's hash table\n5. For each socket entry, check if it matches the target IP address\n6. If a match is found, call CloseSocketEntryAndCleanup to disconnect and release resources\n7. Release the critical section lock when done\n\nParameters:\npSocketManager: Pointer to socket manager structure containing socket connection table\nipAddress: in_addr structure containing the IP address to disconnect (4-byte value)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function uses a critical section to prevent concurrent access to socket structures\n- All socket entries matching the IP address are closed, not just the first match\n- The hash table iteration uses a mask to properly enumerate all entries\n- IP comparison is done after converting addresses to string format via inet_ntoa\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe socket manager structure contains:\n- Offset +0x00: Hash table mask (used for iteration bounds)\n- Offset varies: Critical section lock for thread synchronization\n- Variable offsets: Socket entry table with hash-based organization",
