      "comment": "Retrieves a specific field value from a hash table entry identified by search key.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls FindHashTableEntry to locate the hash table node matching the search key\n2. If entry found, loads field value from offset +0x8C within the entry structure\n3. Obtains critical section lock from FindHashTableEntry output parameter\n4. If critical section exists, releases the lock via LeaveCriticalSection\n5. Returns field value in EAX or 0 if entry not found\n\nParameters:\n- pHashTableManager: Pointer to the hash table manager structure\n- dwSearchKey: Key value to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Field value from entry at offset +0x8C, or 0 if entry not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If FindHashTableEntry returns NULL, field value defaults to 0\n- Lock is conditional: only released if FindHashTableEntry provided a valid critical section\n- Field offset +0x8C is a fixed location within the hash table entry structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe function accesses hash table entries with the following layout:\nOffset  Size   Field Name              Type    Description\n+0x8C   4      EntryFieldValue         DWORD   The field value being extracted",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
