      "name": "GetHashTableEntryNetworkValue",
      "signature": "u_short GetHashTableEntryNetworkValue(int hashTablePtr, uint key)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "u_short",
      "comment": "Retrieves a network-byte-order value from a hash table entry and converts it to host byte order.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize the critical section pointer to NULL\n2. Call FindHashTableEntry to locate the entry for the given key\n3. Initialize return value to 0\n4. If entry pointer is not NULL:\n   - Extract the u_short value at offset 0x7a from the entry\n   - Call ntohs() to convert from network byte order to host byte order\n   - Store result in return value\n5. If critical section pointer is not NULL:\n   - Call LeaveCriticalSection() to release the lock\n6. Return the converted value (or 0 if entry not found)\n\nParameters:\n  hashTablePtr (int): Pointer to the hash table to search\n  key (uint): The key to search for in the hash table\n\nReturns:\n  u_short: The value at offset 0x7a from the entry, converted from network byte order to host byte order; returns 0 if entry not found\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entry not found: Returns 0\n  - Critical section lock: Automatically released after extracting the value\n  - Network byte order: Result is converted from network (big-endian) to host byte order",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
