      "name": "ProcessContextOrSendSocketData",
      "signature": "uint ProcessContextOrSendSocketData(void * pContext, uint dwSocketKey, uint dwUnused_param3, uint dwCallbackParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes context callback or delegates to socket data transmission based on context state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pContext pointer is non-null (return 0 if null)\n2. Load context state field from offset +0x86c\n3. Check if context state equals 1 or 2 (active states)\n4. If state matches active condition AND callback pointer at offset +0xbcc is non-null:\n   a. Push dwCallbackParam onto stack\n   b. Call context callback function (indirect call through +0xbcc)\n   c. Return callback result in EAX\n5. If state does not match or callback is null:\n   a. Push dwSocketKey onto stack\n   b. Call SendSocketDataUsingHashKey function\n   c. Return socket operation result in EAX\n\nParameters:\npContext (void *) - Pointer to context structure with minimum size 0xbcc+4 bytes containing state and callback\ndwSocketKey (uint) - Hash key for socket table lookup when context inactive\ndwUnused_param3 (uint) - Reserved parameter (not used in function logic)\ndwCallbackParam (uint) - Parameter passed to context callback when state is active\n\nReturns:\nCallback function return value (any) if context state is 1 or 2 and callback exists\nSendSocketDataUsingHashKey result (typically 0 or 1) when state inactive or callback null\n0 if pContext is null (error path)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nContext state values: 0=inactive, 1/2=active\nNull context returns 0 immediately\nNull callback with active state falls back to socket path",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:3",
