      "name": "TrackSocketConnectionByIdentifier",
      "signature": "void TrackSocketConnectionByIdentifier(uint dwConnectionId, char * lpszData, uint dwDataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Tracks a socket connection by its unique identifier and associates provided data with the connection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate initialization flag at offset +0xbd0 (return if not initialized)\n2. Calculate hash bucket index by applying mask to connection ID\n3. Compute lock address using bucket index (stride calculation: (index * 3) << 3)\n4. Initialize critical section lock at calculated address\n5. Acquire critical section lock via g_pfnEnterCriticalSection\n6. Search linked list at bucket for matching connection ID\n   - Start from bucket head at offset +0x14 (bucket array) + index*4\n   - Traverse linked list via offset +0x4 (next pointer)\n   - Compare connection ID at offset +0x0 of each node\n7. Extract socket address from node at offset +0x18 if match found\n8. Release critical section lock via g_pfnLeaveCriticalSection\n9. Validate connection data structure integrity using ValidateDataStructureIntegrity\n10. If socket address valid (not NULL), insert/update tracked address in hash table with provided data\n\nParameters:\n  connectionId - Unique identifier for the socket connection (searched in linked list)\n  pData - Pointer to data buffer to associate with connection\n  dataSize - Size of data buffer in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initialization flag at +0xbd0 is 0, function returns immediately without processing\n  - If connection ID not found in bucket list, socketAddress remains NULL and data tracking is skipped\n  - Critical section ensures thread-safe access to connection list during lookup and lock operations\n  - Connection list uses linked list structure with connection ID at +0x0 and socket address at +0x18",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
