      "name": "ProcessAndTrackSocketAddress",
      "signature": "void ProcessAndTrackSocketAddress(void * pConnectionManager, uint dwSocketIndex, char * szIPAddressString, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process socket connection and track IP address in database\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection manager initialization (BX != 0)\n2. Calculate critical section offset: (socketIndex & mask) * 24 bytes per entry\n3. Acquire critical section lock for thread-safe access\n4. Search linked list at socket entry for matching socket ID\n5. Release critical section lock\n6. If entry not found: Insert IP address string into hash table with flags\n7. If entry found: Convert IP string to network format and update tracking\n\nParameters:\npConnectionManager: Pointer to ClientConnection structure with socket array\nsocketIndex: Socket index (masked to valid range, multiplied by 4 for array lookup)\npIPAddressString: Null-terminated IP address string to track/convert\nflags: Initialization and tracking flags\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If connection manager not initialized (offset 0xbd0 is null), exits early\n- Socket index is masked with value at offset 0xc to enforce valid range\n- Critical sections indexed by masked socket ID with 24-byte stride\n- Linked list traversal searches for matching socket ID at offset 0x0\n- Magic constant 0x7a7 used for validation (possibly line number for error reporting)\n- Two hash tables referenced: one for new entries, one for existing entry updates\n\nStructure Layout:\nConnection Manager offsets:\n  0x000 - Socket entry array base\n  0x00c - Socket index mask value\n  0x01c - Critical section array base\n  0x014 - Socket entry list pointers\n  0xbd0 - Initialization flag",
