      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates and logs duplicate or suspicious connection attempts from client IP address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract client IP address (S_addr) from in_addr parameter\n2. Load hash table mask from server context at offset +0xc\n3. Acquire critical section lock at offset +0x28 for thread safety\n4. Calculate hash bucket index by ANDing IP address with mask\n5. Load hash table base pointer from server context at offset +0x20\n6. Retrieve hash table bucket entry at calculated index\n7. Traverse hash chain comparing each entry's IP at offset +0x18 with target\n8. Continue following chain via next pointer at offset +0x1c until match or end\n9. Release critical section lock\n10. If matching entry found (IP already in table), validate permission mask\n11. If ValidatePermissionMask returns 0 (permission valid), log suspicious activity\n12. Convert IP address to ASCII string using inet_ntoa()\n13. Call InitializeNetworkConnection to setup logging context\n14. Track suspicious connection by socket ID (offset +0x0) using TrackSocketConnectionByIdentifier\n15. Return 1 (always succeeds regardless of validation result)\n\nParameters:\n  pClientAddress: in_addr* - Client IP address as union containing S_addr field\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (success/completion indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic numbers: Hash table offset +0x20, mask offset +0xc, IP field offset +0x18,\n  next chain pointer offset +0x1c, socket ID offset +0x0, critical section offset +0x28\n  Thread safety: Critical section protects hash table traversal against concurrent modifications\n  Always succeeds: Function returns 1 regardless of whether entry was found or permissions valid\n  Error handling: No error returns; all code paths lead to return 1",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:aaea9cdf27c54d43dbe2680acc41f722",
