      "name": "InitializeNetworkMode",
      "signature": "int InitializeNetworkMode(int * pNetworkMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes Winsock networking and routes to appropriate socket initialization based on network mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x190 bytes (400 bytes) on stack for WSADATA structure\n2. Call WSAStartup(0x101, &wsaData) to initialize Winsock 2.1 API\n3. If WSAStartup fails (startupResult != 0), return 0 immediately without further initialization\n4. Check mode flag value at [pNetworkMode]: if value != 0, initialize server mode socket\n5. If mode flag == 0, initialize client mode socket via InitializeNetworkServerSocket()\n6. Return socket handle from the appropriate initialization function\n\nParameters:\npNetworkMode (int *): Pointer to 4-byte mode flag controlling socket initialization mode\n  - Value 0: Initialize client mode socket\n  - Value != 0: Initialize server mode socket\n\nReturns:\nint: Valid socket handle (SOCKET type) on successful initialization\n     Returns 0 on WSAStartup failure, indicating initialization could not proceed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- WSAStartup failure is fatal: function immediately returns 0 without attempting socket creation\n- Mode flag determines execution path but does not affect Winsock initialization\n- Stack allocation of 0x190 bytes (400 bytes) matches WSADATA structure size (Win32 Winsock structure)",
