      "name": "WaitOrProcessContextSlots",
      "signature": "uint WaitOrProcessContextSlots(int * pContextState, uint timeoutMs)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Conditionally processes active context slots or waits on synchronization handle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if context state flag at offset 0 is non-zero\n2. If non-zero, call ProcessActiveSlots() to handle active slots immediately\n3. If zero, retrieve synchronization handle from context offset +0xbdc\n4. Call WaitForSingleObject with handle and timeout parameter\n5. Return TRUE if wait returned WAIT_OBJECT_0, FALSE on timeout/failure\n\nParameters:\npContextState: Pointer to game context/state structure\n  - First DWORD (offset 0) is status flag (0=wait mode, non-0=process mode)\n  - Offset +0xbdc contains HANDLE for synchronization object\ntimeoutMs: Timeout in milliseconds for wait operation\n\nReturns:\nBOOL - TRUE (1) if ProcessActiveSlots completed successfully or WaitForSingleObject returned WAIT_OBJECT_0\n       FALSE (0) if wait operation timed out or failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit via return in process branch if context status flag is non-zero\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with callee cleanup (RET 0x8)\n- Handle access via array indexing: param_1[0x2f5] = offset +0xbdc\n- Result comparison: Tests if waitStatus == 0 and converts to boolean via SETZ instruction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
