      "name": "GetCrashDumpFileSize",
      "signature": "long GetCrashDumpFileSize(char * szFilePrefix)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "long",
      "comment": "Gets the file size of a crash dump file by closing any open handle, formatting a date-based filename, opening the file, seeking to end, and reading the position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section mutex (g_hCrashDumpMutex) for thread safety\n2. Call CloseCrashDumpFileByName with pFilePrefix to close any open handle\n3. Get current system time via GetLocalTime\n4. Extract year, month, day from SYSTEMTIME structure\n5. Convert year to 2-digit format via IDIV by 100\n6. Build filename using sprintf with format szCrashDumpFileNameFormat: \"%s%s%02d%02d%02d.txt\"\n7. Call OpenFileForCrashDump to open the formatted crash dump file\n8. If file opened successfully (pCrashDumpFile != NULL):\n   a. Seek to end of file with SEEK_END (2)\n   b. Get current file position with _ftell to obtain file size\n   c. Close file with _fclose\n9. Release critical section mutex (g_hCrashDumpMutex)\n10. Return file size in EAX/EDI or 0 if file failed to open\n\nParameters:\npFilePrefix (char*): Prefix string for the crash dump filename (e.g., \"crash_\")\n\nReturns:\nlong: File size in bytes if successful, or 0 if file open failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if OpenFileForCrashDump fails (file does not exist or permission denied)\n- Critical section protection ensures thread-safe access to global crash dump file handle\n- Date format is hardcoded as YYMMDD based on system time\n- File mode \"r\" is used for read-only access",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:a75521a2f961dfe442281672ad583a28",
