      "name": "ProcessInventoryItem",
      "signature": "void ProcessInventoryItem(int nPathType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Constructs the Diablo II project installation path and stores it in global variable.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 260-byte stack buffer (projectPathBuffer) for path construction\n2. Load buffer address into ESI register and initialize with null terminator\n3. Call ExtractModuleDirectory() to validate base installation path\n4. If validation succeeds (pathCheckResult != 0):\n   - Call AppendPathComponent() to append g_szPathSeparator (\"\\\\\") to buffer\n   - Call CreateDirectoryPathRecursive() to ensure directory exists\n5. Call sprintf() with format string g_szFilePathFormat (\"%s%s\") to concatenate paths\n6. Store result in global szGameInstallPath variable\n7. Clean up stack and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  nPathType (EDX): Integer path type identifier/index passed to sprintf() formatting\n\nReturns:\n  void (callee removes 4-byte parameter via RET 0x4)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Path validation failure (ExtractModuleDirectory returns 0) skips AppendPathComponent\n    and CreateDirectoryPathRecursive, proceeding directly to sprintf formatting\n  - 260-byte buffer (0x104) matches Windows MAX_PATH limit for path strings\n  - g_szFilePathFormat uses \"%s%s\" to concatenate validated base path with path type identifier\n  - Calling convention is __stdcall: all parameters on stack, callee cleanup\n\nStructure Layout:\nStack Layout (from ESP):\n  Offset  Size  Purpose                    Description\n  ------  ----  -------------------------  -----------\n  +0      4     Return Address             Pushed by CALL instruction\n  +4      1     nPathType Parameter        Path type identifier\n  +8      260   projectPathBuffer          Stack-allocated path buffer (260 bytes)\n  +108    4     g_szPathSeparator Address  Reference to global separator string\n  +112    4     Callee Cleanup             RET immediate (0x4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
