      "name": "LogFormattedMessage",
      "signature": "void LogFormattedMessage(char * formatString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Logs a formatted message to the application message queue with error handling and cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate formatString parameter is not NULL\n   - If NULL: Call GetReturnAddress() to get return context\n   - Call WSACleanup() to shutdown Winsock\n   - Call LogErrorAndShutdown(6, &DAT_6ff768ec, 0x13c) to log critical error\n   - Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit() to cleanup\n   - Call _exit(-1) to terminate process\n2. Check return address validation from GetReturnAddress()\n   - If EAX is NULL: Use default error data structure at &DAT_6ff768ec\n   - Otherwise: Use EAX value as base pointer\n3. Call FUN_6ff68770() to queue formatted message with parameters:\n   - First param: base pointer (default or validated)\n   - Second param: 1 (severity/type flag)\n   - Third param: 0 (formatting flag)\n   - Fourth param: formatString (format string)\n   - Fifth param: stack pointer to variadic arguments\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nformatString (char*): Pointer to format string for logging. If NULL, triggers full shutdown sequence.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function does not return on NULL formatString (calls _exit). Otherwise returns to caller.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL formatString: Triggers critical shutdown sequence\n- GetReturnAddress() validation: Used to determine logging destination structure\n- Variadic arguments: Passed through stack to FUN_6ff68770 for formatting\n- Error severity: Always logs with error type 6 (critical)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:e1a5ba279fa3738eb0dcd832b1ee7928",
