      "rvas": {
        "LoD/1.11": "0x16250",
        "LoD/1.11b": "0x13CC0",
        "LoD/1.12a": "0x195F0",
        "LoD/1.13c": "0x18D50",
        "LoD/1.13d": "0x120B0"
      },
      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.11": 571,
        "LoD/1.11b": 571,
        "LoD/1.12a": 571,
        "LoD/1.13c": 571,
        "LoD/1.13d": 571
      },
      "name": "FindOrCreateLogFileSlot",
      "signature": "FILE * FindOrCreateLogFileSlot(char * pLogFileName, uint * pOutSlotIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "FILE *",
      "comment": "Searches for or creates a log file slot with LRU cache replacement policy.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetTickCount() to capture current system milliseconds timestamp\n2. Initialize three candidate slot indices to -1 (unset): best_unexamined, best_timestamp, best_lru\n3. If search name is null or first byte is 0x00, skip to step 7 (direct slot selection)\n4. Validate search name length is less than 0x14 (20 bytes), else error exit\n5. Iterate through global log file slot array (20 slots at 0x6ff816f8, 0x10 bytes each):\n   a. Load slot filename at offset 0x00 (16-byte string buffer)\n   b. Compare bytes pairwise against pLogFileName until mismatch or null terminator\n   c. If exact match found, check if FILE* already open - if yes, return it immediately\n   d. If no match, evaluate slot for replacement: empty FILE*, no config, or oldest access time\n   e. Track best_unexamined (first unused slot), best_timestamp, and LRU candidates\n   f. Advance to next slot and continue until end of array (address 0x6ff81838)\n6. Select best candidate: prefer unused > unexamined > oldest access time (LRU)\n7. If selected slot has open FILE*, close it and clear pointer\n8. Validate search name length is less than 0x10 (16 bytes); if >= 16, log error 0x335 and exit\n9. Copy pLogFileName bytes (including null terminator) to selected slot storage\n10. Call CreateCrashDumpLogFile(pLogFileName) to open file; returns FILE* in EAX\n11. Record current timestamp in two arrays: g_LogFileFirstAccessTime and g_LogFileLastAccessTime\n12. Check if config data pointer exists at offset [g_LogFileConfigData + slotIndex*4]\n13. Store returned FILE* in g_LogFilePointers[slotIndex]\n14. If config exists AND FILE* valid, call WriteRealmStartupInfo() to write file header\n15. Else if no config or file open failed, check if pLogFileName is valid before calling WriteLogFileHeader()\n16. Load final FILE* pointer from g_LogFilePointers[slotIndex]\n17. If FILE* is valid (not null) and pOutSlotIndex is valid, write slotIndex to *pOutSlotIndex\n18. Return FILE* pointer (null if file open failed)\n\nParameters:\n  pLogFileName - Pointer to null-terminated log filename string to find or create (char*)\n  pOutSlotIndex - Pointer to UINT to receive selected slot index [0..19] if successful\n\nReturns:\n  FILE* - Valid file pointer if file opened successfully; NULL if file open failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Null/empty name: First byte = 0x00 triggers immediate slot selection without search\n  Name too long: Length >= 16 bytes causes error log (code 0x335) and process termination via _exit()\n  Duplicate names: If name already exists in slot with open file, returns that file immediately\n  Cache eviction: LRU policy selects least recently accessed slot when no unused slots available\n  File closure: Automatically closes and clears FILE* in selected slot before opening new file\n  Config verification: Only writes file header if config data pointer is valid and non-zero\n  Timestamp tracking: Maintains dual timestamp arrays for cache replacement decisions\n\nGlobal Data Accessed:\n  g_LogFileNameSlots (0x6ff816f8) - 20 slot array, 0x10 bytes each, filename strings\n  g_LogFilePointers (0x6ff81900) - 20 FILE* pointers (dword array)\n  g_LogFileConfigData (0x6ff81850) - 20 config data pointers (dword array)\n  g_LogFileFirstAccessTime (0x6ff81950) - 20 timestamp values (initial open time)\n  g_LogFileLastAccessTime (0x6ff818a8) - 20 timestamp values (last access time for LRU)\n  g_dwResourceAccessTimestamps - Secondary timestamp array for comparison logic\n  g_szErrorMessageSourceLocationTable - Error table for LogErrorAndShutdown()\n  g_szUnrecoverableErrorMessage - Error message string for length validation failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:9dd289fc0554abb7607a85e926bcfcd0",
