      "name": "ValidateParameterOrInitiateShutdown",
      "signature": "void ValidateParameterOrInitiateShutdown(char * szParameterValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates a parameter and processes it if valid, or initiates graceful shutdown if NULL.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter from stack and test for NULL\n2. If NULL: Get return address, cleanup Winsock, log error 0x14f, shutdown resources, exit -1\n3. If valid: Call LogFormattedMessage to process parameter and return\n\nParameters:\nszParameterValue - Parameter string pointer; cannot be NULL\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Returns to caller if valid; exits process if NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic number 0x14f indicates unrecoverable error. Called from entry point and IOCP handler.",
