      "name": "ValidateAndProcessCharacterDataWithFilter",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndProcessCharacterDataWithFilter(int * pFilterWidth, char * pCharData, int nCharacterCount, int nBitWidth, int nAdjustment)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates character data pointers and counts, then iterates through character array\nprocessing each character through a filter buffer until null terminator or limit reached.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize character index counter to 0\n2. Validate pFilterWidth pointer is not NULL; error code 0x6e if invalid\n3. Validate pCharData pointer is not NULL; error code 0x6f if invalid\n4. Validate nCharacterCount is not zero; error code 0x70 if invalid\n5. Validate *pFilterWidth value is not zero; error code 0x71 if invalid\n6. Call InitializeCharacterFilterBuffer to initialize local filter buffer with nCharacterCount\nand nBitWidth parameters\n7. Calculate maximum character count: multiply filterWidth * nBitWidth, add 7, right-shift by\n3 (divide by 8) for byte alignment\n8. If nAdjustment flag is nonzero, decrement maxCharCount by 1\n9. Load first character from pCharData array start\n10. Loop while current character is not null AND characterIndex less than maxCharCount:\n    a. Increment characterIndex counter\n    b. Sign-extend current character value to signed int for lookup\n    c. Load value at offset (currentChar + 4) for character processing\n    d. Call ProcessCharacterData with filter buffer, character value, and filterWidth\n    e. Advance to next character in pCharData array\n    f. Load next character byte from pCharData[index+1]\n11. After loop exits due to null or limit: check if nAdjustment flag set OR characterIndex\nless than maxCharCount\n12. If either condition true, call ProcessCharacterData with null terminator (0) to finalize\n13. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pFilterWidth: Pointer to 32-bit filter width value (DWORD); must not be NULL; value\n  must be greater than zero\n- pCharData: Pointer to null-terminated character array; must not be NULL; array contains\n  character codes to process\n- nCharacterCount: Count of characters for filter initialization; must not be zero\n- nBitWidth: Bit width parameter used in maximum character count calculation\n- nAdjustment: Adjustment flag; nonzero value decrements max count and forces null\n  terminator processing\n\nReturns:\n- void (function does not return a value to caller)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error codes: 0x6e (pFilterWidth NULL), 0x6f (pCharData NULL), 0x70 (nCharacterCount\n  zero), 0x71 (*pFilterWidth zero) trigger cleanup and process termination\n- Null terminator: 0x00 character in pCharData terminates iteration early regardless of\n  character count\n- Offset calculation: Character lookup uses (characterValue + 4) offset, suggesting lookup\n  table or array indexing\n- Maximum count formula: (filterWidth * nBitWidth + 7) >> 3 calculates aligned byte count\n- Character sign extension: Character byte sign-extended to 32-bit int for offset calculation\n- Global data: g_szErrorMessageSourceLocationTable and g_szUnrecoverableErrorMessage used\n  for error reporting and cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:b09840cd01112e9afd3badbe97749979",
