      "name": "BuildPKWareHuffmanDecodeTables",
      "signature": "int BuildPKWareHuffmanDecodeTables(byte * pCodeLengthArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Builds PKWARE Implode Huffman decoder lookup tables from code length array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Read 256-byte code length array with symbol values 0-15\n2. Count frequency of each symbol (0-15) in the input array\n3. Normalize frequencies using cumulative sum (backward iteration)\n4. Rearrange input symbols into buckets by frequency\n5. Transform rearranged data by reading back through frequency offsets\n6. Compute canonical Huffman code lengths via bit-shifting\n7. Build two-stage decode table: codes <= 8 bits in fast path, long codes in second table\n8. Return 1 on success, 0 if input validation fails\n\nParameters:\n  pCodeLengthArray: Pointer to 256-byte input array containing symbol values (0-15)\n\nReturns:\n  1 if decode tables successfully initialized\n  0 if input validation fails (less than 256 bytes)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Processes exactly 256 bytes of input before building tables\n  - Symbol values must be 0-15; values >= 16 or 0 terminate input early\n  - Codes <= 8 bits use fast decode path with left-shift: (code << (8 - length))\n  - Codes > 8 bits use second-level table with right-shift: (code >> (length - 8))\n  - All results written to g_pHuffmanFastDecodeTable and g_pHuffmanSecondDecodeTable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:2874c737d0c62d69660bb270902b806a",
