      "comment": "Constructs a canonical Huffman code table from symbol frequencies.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if numSymbols is 0\n2. Special case: if numSymbols is 1, set first element to 0\n3. Merge phase: add frequencies[1] to frequencies[0]\n4. Build Huffman tree: merge pairs using two-pointer technique (leftIdx, rightIdx)\n   - Compares elements from left and right, adds smaller to merged tree\n   - Uses in-place array manipulation for memory efficiency\n5. Backtracking phase: traverse merged tree to assign code bit lengths\n   - Indirect array lookup to compute depth for each symbol\n6. Code assignment phase: generate canonical code values\n   - Counts zero-length codes and fills code array with sequential values\n   - Handles multiple symbols per bit length\n\nParameters:\n- numSymbols (ECX): Number of symbols to process\n- pFreqArray (EAX): Pointer to frequency array (modified in-place)\n  - Input: frequencies at indices [0..numSymbols-1]\n  - Output: canonical code values at same indices\n\nReturns:\n- void; pFreqArray is modified with canonical Huffman code assignments\n\nStructure Layout - Frequency/Code Array:\nOffset   Size   Field Name       Type    Description\n+0x0     4      freq/code[0]     int     First symbol frequency or code\n+0x4     4      freq/code[1]     int     Second symbol frequency or code\n+0x8     4      freq/code[2]     int     Third symbol frequency or code\n+0x4n    4      freq/code[n]     int     nth symbol frequency or code value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- numSymbols = 0: Early return without modification\n- numSymbols = 1: Single symbol assigned code value 0\n- numSymbols >= 2: Full canonical Huffman tree construction via merging\n\nAlgorithm Correctness Notes:\nThis implementation uses canonical Huffman coding, which generates the minimum-length\nprefixes for code values by assigning sequential binary values to symbols grouped by\ncode length. The merge phase builds an implicit tree, the backtracking phase computes\ncode lengths, and the final phase assigns canonical codes.",
