      "name": "HashStringDefault",
      "signature": "uint HashStringDefault(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Computes a 32-bit hash value for a null-terminated string using default parameters.\n\nThis is a convenience wrapper around ComputeStringHash that provides a simplified interface\nfor hashing strings when no special hash parameters (seed/flags) are needed. It's commonly\nused in hash table initialization and string lookup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Accept string pointer in pString parameter\n2. Push seed value (0) onto stack\n3. Push flags value (0) onto stack\n4. Call ComputeStringHash with (pString, 0, 0)\n5. Return hash value in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pString: Pointer to null-terminated string to be hashed\n\nReturns:\n  uint: 32-bit unsigned hash value suitable for hash table indexing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  NULL pointer: Behavior undefined, no input validation performed\n  Empty string: Returns hash of empty string (only null terminator)\n\nSee Also:\n  ComputeStringHash: Underlying hashing algorithm with seed/flags support",
