      "name": "DeallocateResourcePoolNode",
      "signature": "void DeallocateResourcePoolNode(ResourcePoolNode * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Recursively deallocates a binary search tree of ResourcePoolNode structures.\n\nThis function performs a post-order depth-first traversal to ensure child nodes are\ndeallocated before their parent. This is essential for proper resource cleanup in\nhierarchical tree structures where each node manages subordinate child nodes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX (node parameter) and ESI registers to preserve caller state\n2. Copy node pointer from ECX to ESI for manipulation\n3. Load left child pointer from node offset +0x24\n4. Test if left child pointer is NULL\n5. If left child exists, recursively call DeallocateResourcePoolNode on left subtree\n6. Load right child pointer from node offset +0x28\n7. Test if right child pointer is NULL\n8. If right child exists, recursively call DeallocateResourcePoolNode on right subtree\n9. Setup parameters for DeallocateResourcePoolElement: push type flag 0x346\n10. Push pool descriptor address 0x6ff78360 as second parameter\n11. Load address of local node copy into ECX register for first parameter\n12. Clear EAX register (implicit context parameter)\n13. Store node pointer at correct stack offset\n14. Call DeallocateResourcePoolElement to deallocate current node\n15. Pop and restore ESI register\n16. Pop and restore ECX register\n17. Return to caller (implicit 0 bytes stack cleanup via RET)\n\nParameters:\n  pNode (ECX at entry): Pointer to ResourcePoolNode structure being deallocated.\n    The structure contains:\n    - Left child pointer at offset +0x24\n    - Right child pointer at offset +0x28\n    This pointer is passed to DeallocateResourcePoolElement for final deallocation.\n\nReturns:\n  void: No explicit return value; deallocates the tree in-place via side effects.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Leaf nodes: Both left and right child pointers are NULL; function skips to node\n    deallocation after testing both children.\n  Post-order traversal: Children are deallocated before parent (opposite of pre-order),\n    ensuring all references are cleaned before parent is freed.\n  Recursive calls: Self-calls at offsets +0xab and +0xb7 deallocate subtrees.\n  Magic constants: Type flag 0x346 identifies the resource type to DeallocateResourcePoolElement;\n    Address 0x6ff78360 contains pool descriptor metadata (source file path in this context).\n\nStructure Layout - ResourcePoolNode:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name       Type      Description\n  0x0     4     parent           pointer   Parent node pointer (if part of larger tree)\n  0x24    4     pLeftChild       pointer   Left subtree root (NULL for leaf nodes)\n  0x28    4     pRightChild      pointer   Right subtree root (NULL for leaf nodes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:1bc0cd1606e51ffb1888b87d4313eaf0",
