      "name": "DeallocateResourceElementPair",
      "signature": "void DeallocateResourceElementPair(uint * pResourceElement)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Deallocates two linked resource pool elements in a single paired operation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register to preserve register state across function\n2. Load pResourceElement parameter from stack at [ESP + 0x8]\n3. Dereference pResourceElement to extract nested resource pointer value\n4. Prepare first deallocation call with mode indicator 0x9a\n5. Push nested resource pointer onto deallocation context structure\n6. Push resource context metadata address 0x6ff78360 (Excel.cpp)\n7. Load address of deallocation context structure via LEA [ESP + 0x10]\n8. Zero EAX register and call DeallocateResourcePoolElement for nested pointer\n9. Prepare second deallocation call with mode indicator 0x9b\n10. Push original pResourceElement pointer onto deallocation context structure\n11. Push resource context metadata address again\n12. Load deallocation context structure address via LEA [ESP + 0x10]\n13. Zero EAX register and call DeallocateResourcePoolElement for original pointer\n14. Restore ESI register and return with stack cleanup of 4 bytes (stdcall)\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceElement: Pointer to a resource pool element structure containing a nested\n                   resource pointer; both elements are deallocated sequentially\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; function uses __stdcall calling convention with caller's\n        4-byte parameter automatically cleaned up by RET 0x4 instruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic numbers 0x9a and 0x9b indicate different resource element types or\n  deallocation modes passed to DeallocateResourcePoolElement\n  Context address 0x6ff78360 is embedded as immediate value in both calls\n  Both deallocations are unconditional; no error checking performed\n  RET 0x4 ensures callee performs stack cleanup (stdcall convention)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:5",
