      "comment": "Inserts a uint value into a sorted array while maintaining sort order using binary search.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pArrayDesc pointer is not NULL; error if NULL (0x3d1)\n2. Check array initialized flag at offset +0xc; must equal 0; error if flags != 0 (0x3d8)\n3. Compare count vs capacity at [EBX+4] vs [EBX+0]; if count > capacity, array is full\n4. If array needs expansion (count <= capacity): allocate new buffer with capacity+0x40 entries\n5. Calculate new memory size: (count + 0x40) * 8 bytes per [value, index] pair entry\n6. Clear newly allocated memory using REP STOSD for 0x80 DWORDs (32 qwords)\n7. Perform binary search on existing entries in range [0, capacity)\n8. Compare uValue against midpoint element to determine search direction\n9. Adjust search bounds: if uValue > mid_value, search upper half; else search lower half\n10. When bounds converge, insertion point (iVar4/ESI register) is at first element >= uValue\n11. If insertion point < count, use memmove to shift elements right by 1 entry (8 bytes each)\n12. Store uValue at array[insertion_point] offset, store count at array[insertion_point+4]\n13. Increment capacity counter (stores total inserted count)\n14. Return inserted value stored in EAX from array[insertion_point+4]\n\nParameters:\n- pArrayDesc: Pointer to SortedArrayDescriptor structure containing array metadata\n  * Offset +0x0 (capacity): Max entries before expansion (updated after insertion)\n  * Offset +0x4 (count): Current number of sorted entries\n  * Offset +0x8 (pData): Pointer to uint[2] array storing [value, index] pairs\n  * Offset +0xc (flags): Initialization status flag (must be 0)\n- uValue: uint value to insert maintaining sorted order in array\n\nReturns:\n- EAX contains the count value stored at array[insertion_point+4] after insertion\n- Caller receives the value that was inserted into the sorted position\n\nStructure Layout (SortedArrayDescriptor):\nOffset | Size | Field    | Type              | Description\n-------|------|----------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------\n0x0    | 4    | capacity | uint              | Max capacity; incremented after each insert\n0x4    | 4    | count    | uint              | Current number of sorted entries in array\n0x8    | 4    | pData    | uint[2]* pointer  | Pointer to [value, index] pair array (8 bytes each)\n0xc    | 4    | flags    | uint              | Status/initialization flag; must be 0\nTotal: 16 bytes\n\nArray Entry Layout (8 bytes each):\nOffset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n-------|------|-------|------|------------------------------------------\n0x0    | 4    | value | uint | The sorted value being tracked\n0x4    | 4    | index | uint | Associated index/count value at insertion time\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check: If pArrayDesc==NULL, calls LogErrorAndInitiateShutdown with code 0x3d1\n- Uninitialized array: If flags field != 0, calls error handler with code 0x3d8\n- Array capacity expansion: Stride of 0x40 entries (64 items); clears new memory with REP STOSD\n- Binary search division: Uses signed SAR instruction for midpoint; handles truncation correctly\n- Insertion at end: If iVar4 >= count, memmove is skipped (no elements to shift)\n- Memory clearing: Clears 0x80 DWORDs = 32 qwords = 256 bytes after expansion",
