      "comment": "Enqueues network packet data for asynchronous socket transmission.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate a new queue buffer structure via AllocatePoolSlot()\n2. If allocation fails, log error and shutdown application\n3. Copy source packet data to allocated buffer using optimized copy:\n   - First loop: copy full 32-bit dwords (dataSize >> 2 iterations) using MOVSD\n   - Second loop: copy remaining 1-3 bytes individually (dataSize & 3 iterations) using MOVSB\n4. Store original data size at buffer[0] offset +0x0\n5. Clear buffer[1] reserved field at offset +0x4 to zero\n6. Retrieve list head pointer from context structure at offset +0x74\n7. If list is empty (head == NULL), insert buffer as new head\n8. If list has existing nodes, traverse linked list following next pointers (offset +0x4 in each node) to find tail node\n9. Append newly allocated buffer to tail node's next pointer at offset +0x4\n\nParameters:\n- pContextSocket: Pointer to socket context structure containing send queue list head at offset +0x74\n- pDataBuffer: Source pointer to network packet data to copy\n- dataSize: Number of bytes to copy (0-N range), typically size of network packet payload\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If AllocatePoolSlot() returns NULL, function immediately calls LogErrorAndShutdown(2, ...) to terminate application\n- Data copy uses rep MOVSD for dword-aligned efficiency, then rep MOVSB for remainder bytes\n- Linked list traversal is O(n) where n is queue depth; no optimization for tail pointer caching\n- Buffer node structure: [size_field @ +0][reserved @ +4][data_payload @ +8...]\n- Context structure requires send queue list at offset +0x74 with next pointers at offset +0x4 per node",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:10c847a8e9b4b77bbf6cb145b9ba5290",
