      "name": "InitiateAsyncFileRead",
      "signature": "int InitiateAsyncFileRead(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initiates asynchronous file read operation with critical section protection\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire context lock for synchronization\n2. Calculate available buffer space (0x5b4 - current offset)\n3. Return early if buffer full (no space available)\n4. Validate async operation not already in progress (state flag bit 2)\n5. Set async operation flag to prevent concurrent operations\n6. Validate no pending overlapped read operation exists\n7. Verify I/O handle is valid (not -1)\n8. Increment atomic read counter at offset 0x8\n9. Issue ReadFile syscall with overlapped I/O structure\n10. Handle read result: ERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5) treated as success\n11. Release context lock\n12. Return read success status (0=error, 1=pending, nonzero=complete)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EDI: AsyncIOContext pointer\n  +0x08: LONG readCounter (atomic)\n  +0x10: HANDLE fileHandle (-1 if invalid)\n  +0x2c: CRITICAL_SECTION contextLock\n  +0x44: OVERLAPPED readOverlapped\n  +0x54: DWORD pendingReadCount\n  +0x58: DWORD stateFlags (bit 2 = async in progress)\n  +0xa8: int currentBufferOffset\n  +0xac: DWORD bytesReadOutput\n  +0xb0: BYTE[0x504] readBuffer\n\nReturns:\nint: 0 on error, 1 if read initiated/pending, nonzero if complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- ERROR_IO_PENDING (0x3e5) is treated as success\n- Buffer limit: 0x5b4 (1460) bytes\n- Concurrent async prevented via state flag bit 2\n- Invalid handle triggers cleanup without logging",
