      "name": "ProcessIocpCompletionWithTimeout",
      "signature": "uint ProcessIocpCompletionWithTimeout(void * this, int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes asynchronous I/O completion events from IOCP with 100ms timeout window.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize result to 0 and capture initial tick count for timeout tracking\n2. Calculate elapsed time; exit early if 100ms timeout already exceeded\n3. Loop iteration: Call GetQueuedCompletionStatus on IOCP handle with zero timeout\n4. If GetQueuedCompletionStatus fails (no completion):\n   a. Check if error is WAIT_TIMEOUT (0x102) and return 0 if so\n   b. Otherwise log fatal unrecoverable error and call _exit\n5. If GetQueuedCompletionStatus succeeds (has completion):\n   a. Extract completion key from return and use as packet ID\n   b. Mask completion key with context->dwHashMask to get hash table slot\n   c. Calculate critical section offset as slot * 0x18 (3 * 8 bytes)\n   d. Enter critical section protecting the slot's packet list\n   e. Search packet list for entry matching completion key ID\n   f. Leave critical section and check if packet found\n6. If packet found, extract completion type flags from overlapped->Internal:\n   a. Bit 0 set = receive completion (isReceiveCompletion flag)\n   b. Bits 0-1 = 2 means error/cleanup completion (isSendCompletion flag)\n7. Process based on completion type:\n   a. For receive: Call ProcessDequeuedPacket, clear 0x04 busy flag, increment byte count\n   b. For send: Clear 0x04 busy flag, increment transferred bytes counter, update elapsed time\n   c. Call ProcessClientConnectionData to handle processed packet\n8. Decrement packet refcount using interlocked operation\n9. If refcount reaches 0: Call optional cleanup callback and remove from hash tables\n10. Check if 100ms time budget remaining via comparison of elapsed time\n11. Loop back for next completion if time budget exists, else return result\n\nParameters:\npServerContext: void * - Server context object (this pointer, implicit ECX)\nslotIndex: int - Index into IOCP handle array to select which queue to poll\n\nReturns:\nuint - Returns 1 if data was successfully processed, 0 if timeout or no completions\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- 100ms: Hard timeout window for polling\n- 0x102: Windows error code for WAIT_TIMEOUT\n- 0xc08: Base offset in context for IOCP handle array\n- 0xbc8: Offset to optional completion callback function pointer\n- Critical sections at offset 0x2c within packet structure\n- Hash table indexing uses AND mask at context+0xc\n- Packet refcount at offset +8, decremented via InterlockedDecrement\n- Overlapped.Internal flags at overlapped[1].Internal byte offset\n\nData Structure Offsets:\nContext struct (pServerContext):\n  +0x0c: AND mask for hash table indexing\n  +0x14: Pointer to array of packet list heads (per slot)\n  +0x1c: Pointer to array of critical section structures\n  +0xc08 + slotIndex*4: IOCP handle for this slot\n  +0xbc8: Optional completion callback function pointer\n\nPacket entry struct:\n  +0x00: Packet ID / completion key\n  +0x04: Packet list forward link\n  +0x08: Reference count (interlocked operations)\n  +0x0c: Callback handler pointer\n  +0x10: Reserved field (checked for 0xFFFFFFFF)\n  +0x2c: Critical section for state protection\n  +0x58: State flags (bit 2 = busy flag)\n  +0x9c: Elapsed time field\n  +0xa8: Bytes transferred accumulator",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
