      "name": "ServerConnectionIOProcessor",
      "signature": "uint ServerConnectionIOProcessor(int * pSlotInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes network I/O for a server connection slot in an event loop, managing socket operations and maintaining high-precision performance counters for latency analysis.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract base address and slot index from pSlotInfo parameter\n2. Cache initial system tick count for timeout management\n3. Enter main event loop that continues until slot becomes active\n4. Retrieve current tick count and check if slot is marked active; exit if so\n5. Calculate elapsed milliseconds with signed arithmetic to handle tick wrapping\n6. If elapsed time exceeds 2000ms threshold, reset reference tick to prevent drift\n7. If no timeout pending (current == previous tick), call ProcessConnectionTimeouts()\n8. Prepare select() call: read socket set with no write/error sets and zero timeout\n9. Call select() to check if socket has pending data (result: -1=error, 0=timeout, >0=ready)\n10. On select error (-1), return 1 immediately without processing\n11. On select timeout (0), sleep 20ms (0x14) and loop back\n12. On select success (>0): capture high-precision performance counter before processing\n13. Check thread priority and adjust if not at infinity mark (0x7fffffff)\n14. Call AcceptAndInitializeServerConnection to accept and process incoming connection\n15. Capture performance counter after processing for latency measurement\n16. Enter critical section at base+0x8b4 to protect performance counter updates\n17. Calculate processing latency (end_counter - start_counter) as 64-bit value\n18. Accumulate latency into counter at base+slot*0xb0+0x8cc (with high part at +0x8d0)\n19. Perform 9-level rotating buffer shift: each level copies from previous level\n20. Ring buffer at offsets 0x91c-0x960 stores 9 successive 64-bit timing samples\n21. Calculate 8 delta values between consecutive ring buffer levels (high to low index)\n22. Accumulate all deltas into their respective counters (offsets 0x8e4-0x914)\n23. Calculate final delta (level0 - level8) and add to counter at +0x8dc\n24. Leave critical section and update wake time with fixed increment 0xb21642c8\n25. Sleep 0ms and loop back to step 4\n\nParameters:\n  pSlotInfo: Pointer to array with [baseAddress, slotIndex] structure at offset 0-4\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (slot marked active)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Signed tick count arithmetic with CDQ/XOR handles tick counter wrapping\n  - 2000ms threshold prevents reference tick from drifting on slow systems\n  - 9-level ring buffer implements exponential latency sampling (captures 8 deltas)\n  - Performance counters are 64-bit values split across +0 and +4 byte offsets\n  - Critical sections protect counter updates from race conditions\n  - Thread priority check (0x7fffffff magic) indicates max priority state\n  - Wake time calculation uses fixed 32-bit increment with carry propagation\n\nStructure Offsets (relative to pBaseConnectionArray):\n  +0x8b4: Critical section for counter protection (281 bytes)\n  +0x854: Critical section for slot status (282 bytes)\n  +0xb90+[slot*4]: Socket handle (HANDLE type)\n  +0xbd8+[slot*4]: Thread handle (HANDLE type)\n  +0xbf8+[slot*4]: Slot active flag (0=inactive, nonzero=active)\n  +0x8cc,+0x8d0: Accumulated processing latency (64-bit)\n  +0x8dc,+0x8e0: Final delta latency (64-bit)\n  +0x8e4-0x914: Accumulated level deltas [1-8] (8 counters, 64-bit each)\n  +0x91c-0x920: Ring buffer level 0 (64-bit)\n  +0x924-0x928: Ring buffer level 1 (64-bit)\n  +0x92c-0x930: Ring buffer level 2 (64-bit)\n  +0x934-0x938: Ring buffer level 3 (64-bit)\n  +0x93c-0x940: Ring buffer level 4 (64-bit)\n  +0x944-0x948: Ring buffer level 5 (64-bit)\n  +0x94c-0x950: Ring buffer level 6 (64-bit)\n  +0x954-0x958: Ring buffer level 7 (64-bit)\n  +0x95c-0x960: Ring buffer level 8 (64-bit)\n  Per-slot allocation: 0xb0 bytes per slot (176 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:926639796b2bbba8183855250f701a19",
