      "name": "InitializeNetworkServer",
      "signature": "SOCKET InitializeNetworkServer(u_short serverPort)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "SOCKET",
      "comment": "Initialize Windows Sockets infrastructure and create server listener socket.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate 0x190 bytes on stack for WSADATA structure\\n2. Set WSA initialized flag at implicit game context (ESI) offset 0x884 to 1\\n3. Call WSAStartup(0x101) to initialize Winsock 1.1 with WSADATA\\n4. Test WSAStartup return value for success (0 = success)\\n5. If initialization failed, return 0 (INVALID_SOCKET) to caller\\n6. On success, load serverPort parameter from stack and call InitializeServerListener\\n7. Return the listening socket handle (SOCKET type from EAX)\\n\\nParameters:\\nserverPort (u_short): Port number on which to listen for incoming connections\\n\\nReturns:\\nSOCKET: Valid listening socket handle on success, 0 (INVALID_SOCKET) if WSAStartup fails\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- WSAStartup version 0x101 = Winsock 1.1 (legacy protocol support)\\n- Game context implicit in ESI register (preserved from caller)\\n- Stack parameter cleanup via RET 0x4 (callee responsibility)\\n- WSADATA structure size hardcoded to 0x190 bytes\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Function part of network initialization sequence: called by InitializeNetworkMode\\n- Subsequent socket creation handled by InitializeServerListener\\n- Winsock 1.1 compatibility for legacy system support",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
