      "name": "CleanupResourcesAndResetContext",
      "signature": "void CleanupResourcesAndResetContext(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup context resource handles and reset internal state flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test processed flag (bit 0 of offset +0x48); if set, skip to exit (early termination if already processed)\n2. Load event handle pointer from offset +0x38 (pEventHandle field)\n3. Test if event handle pointer is non-null\n4. If valid, dereference event handle and call ResetEvent() via function pointer at 0x6ff7501c\n5. Set event state flag at offset +0x4 (relative to handle) to 1\n6. Clear event flags at offset +0x8 (relative to handle) to 0\n7. Clear event handle pointer at offset +0x38 by setting to 0\n8. Load resource pointer from offset +0x0 and test for non-null\n9. If resource is valid, call ReleaseResourceHandle() at 0x6ff5ce3c to release resource\n10. Clear resource pointer at offset +0x0 by setting to 0\n11. Load status flags from offset +0x48 and set processed bit (0x1) via OR operation\n12. Load pending work value from offset +0x30 and test for non-zero\n13. If no pending work, skip to exit (no additional processing needed)\n14. If pending work exists, save value and call DeallocateResourcePoolElement() with pending work value\n15. Copy pending work source values from offsets +0x30/+0x34 to target offsets +0x3c/+0x40\n16. Clear pending work array (offsets +0x1c through +0x30) by XORing ECX and storing zero dwords\n\nParameters:\npContext: Pointer to context structure containing resource handles, event pointers, and pending work data\n  Implicit in EAX, __stdcall calling convention\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. All operations modify context structure in-place.\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name              | Type       | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | resourcePointer         | void*      | Resource handle to release (cleared to 0 after cleanup)\n+0x04  | 4    | eventState              | uint       | Event signaling state (set to 1 after ResetEvent)\n+0x08  | 4    | eventFlags              | uint       | Event flag field (cleared to 0 after reset)\n+0x1c  | 36   | pendingWorkArray        | byte[36]   | Pending work slots array (cleared to all zeros)\n+0x30  | 4    | pendingWorkValue        | uint       | Primary pending work data to process\n+0x34  | 4    | pendingWorkValue2       | uint       | Secondary pending work data\n+0x38  | 4    | pEventHandle            | void*      | Pointer to event handle (set to 0 after reset)\n+0x3c  | 4    | targetPendingValue1     | uint       | Target for primary pending work copy\n+0x40  | 4    | targetPendingValue2     | uint       | Target for secondary pending work copy\n+0x48  | 4    | statusFlags             | uint       | Status flags (bit 0 = processed flag, upper bits = signature/validation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nAlready Processed: If processed flag (bit 0 of +0x48) is set on entry, function exits immediately without any cleanup operations, protecting against double-cleanup.\nNull Event Handle: If event handle pointer at +0x38 is null, skips ResetEvent call but continues with resource cleanup and flag setting.\nNull Resource: If resource pointer at +0x0 is null, skips ReleaseResourceHandle call but continues with flag setting and pending work processing.\nNo Pending Work: If pending work value at +0x30 is zero, skips DeallocateResourcePoolElement call and field clearing, exiting after flag setup.\nUsed By: DestroyEntity, ValidateContextAndWaitHandle, InitializeGameSessionConfig, AllocateEventHandleSlot, ValidateContextSignatureAndWaitThread",
