      "name": "SearchStringTable",
      "signature": "uint SearchStringTable(uint searchKey, StringSearchTable * pTableHeader, uint * pOutField1, uint * pOutField2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Linear search through string lookup table for matching key\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load entry count from table header at offset +0x4\n2. Initialize index counter to 0\n3. Calculate first entry pointer (header + 0x8)\n4. Loop through entries (stride 0xc):\n   a. Compare key at [entry+0x0] with search parameter\n   b. On match: copy [entry+0x4] to *pOutField1\n   c. On match: copy [entry+0x8] to *pOutField2\n   d. On match: return 0 (success)\n   e. If no match: increment index, advance to next entry\n   f. If index < count: continue loop\n5. After loop: return 0x16 (error - not found)\n\nParameters:\nsearchKey: DWORD to find in table\npTableHeader: Pointer to table with count at +0x4, entries at +0x8\npOutField1: Output buffer for matching entry's field 1\npOutField2: Output buffer for matching entry's field 2\n\nReturns:\n0: Entry found, output fields populated\n22: Entry not found in table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:2",
