      "name": "ComputeScaledArrayOffset",
      "signature": "int ComputeScaledArrayOffset(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Computes a scaled array offset using index-based calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Take input index parameter (passed in EAX via __stdcall)\n2. Multiply index by 3 using LEA EAX, [EAX + EAX*2]\n3. Multiply result by 4 and add 8 using LEA EAX, [EAX*4 + 0x8]\n4. Return final scaled offset in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- nIndex (int): Array index value to scale\n\nReturns:\n- int: Scaled offset calculated as (nIndex * 12) + 8\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Pure mathematical computation with no validation\n- Stride multiplier of 12 with base offset 8 indicates access to array of 12-byte structures\n- No boundary checking; caller is responsible for valid indices\n- Uses only LEA instructions for CPU efficiency\n\nNotes:\n- Currently unreferenced in binary; may be part of unused code path or library code\n- Typical usage pattern: array base address + ComputeScaledArrayOffset(index)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:aefe2839e846cd74c36b581cbfc159f1",
