      "name": "GetReturnAddress",
      "signature": "void * GetReturnAddress(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Retrieves the return address from the stack for debugging or logging purposes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the return address from the current stack pointer (ESP) into EAX\n2. Return the loaded address to the caller\n\nParameters:\nNone. This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\nReturns the address of the instruction that called this function, suitable for stack trace analysis, logging, or debugging operations.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis function accesses the top of the current call stack frame. The return address is located at [ESP] before the function executes, containing the exact address that will be resumed when this function returns. This value is useful for implementing stack walks, crash dump analysis, or function call tracing.",
