      "name": "DetectSystemConfiguration",
      "signature": "void DetectSystemConfiguration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Detects and stores Windows version and system configuration information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create OSVERSIONINFOA structure with dwOSVersionInfoSize = 0x94 bytes\n2. Call GetVersionExA() to retrieve Windows version and platform information\n3. If GetVersionExA succeeds, convert dwMinorVersion to float with sign adjustment\n4. If dwMinorVersion < 0, add sign adjustment constant (0x6ff78fe0)\n5. Enter multiply loop: while g_fVersionThreshold < minorVersionAccumulator, multiply by g_fVersionMultiplier\n6. Multiply result by g_fVersionCoefficient and store in g_fVersionInfo\n7. Convert dwMajorVersion to float with sign adjustment if negative\n8. Add major and minor float calculations together, store in g_fVersionInfo\n9. Determine OS type based on dwPlatformId (1=Win9x, 2=NT-based, other=unknown):\n   - Platform 1 (Win9x): Check dwMinorVersion against 0x5a (90) threshold\n     - If dwMinorVersion < 10: Set OS type 1 (Win95)\n     - If 10 <= dwMinorVersion < 90: Set OS type 2 (Win98)\n     - If dwMinorVersion >= 90: Set OS type 3 (WinMe)\n   - Platform 2 (NT-based): Set OS type 4 (WinNT4), then check dwMajorVersion > 4\n     - If major > 4: Check dwMinorVersion thresholds\n       - If dwMinorVersion < 2: Set OS type 6 (WinXP) or 5 (Win2000)\n       - If dwMinorVersion >= 2: Set OS type 7 (Win2003+)\n   - Other platforms: Set OS type 0 (unknown)\n10. Call GlobalMemoryStatus() to get memory information\n11. Extract dwTotalPhys and store in g_dwTotalPhysicalMemory\n12. Call GetSystemInfo() to get processor information, store at g_SystemInfo\n13. Set g_dwSystemConfigInitialized = 1 to mark initialization complete\n14. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone - function detects system configuration and stores results in global variables\n\nReturns:\nvoid - all results stored in global variables\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative version numbers are sign-adjusted using g_fVersionSignAdjustment constant\n- The multiply loop for minor version scaling may iterate 0+ times based on threshold\n- SBB instruction at 0x6ff6036c implements conditional subtraction: EBX gets -1 if dwMinorVersion < 0x5a, 0 otherwise\n- Calling convention: __stdcall with 0x0 bytes of parameter cleanup\n- Function allocates 0xb8 bytes (184 bytes) of local stack space for OSVERSIONINFOA and MEMORYSTATUS structures\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_fVersionInfo @ 0x6ff82f04: Combined major/minor version float calculation\n- g_dwOSType @ 0x6ff82f00: OS type code (0=unknown, 1=Win95, 2=Win98, 3=WinMe, 4=WinNT4, 5=Win2000, 6=WinXP, 7=Win2003+)\n- g_dwTotalPhysicalMemory @ 0x6ff82f08: Total system RAM in bytes\n- g_SystemInfo @ 0x6ff82f10: SYSTEM_INFO structure with processor details\n- g_dwSystemConfigInitialized @ 0x6ff82efc: Initialization flag (set to 1 on completion)",
