      "name": "CalculateJulianDayNumber",
      "signature": "void CalculateJulianDayNumber(int * pAdjustedYear, int * pAdjustedMonth, int * pAdjustedDay)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts calendar date to Julian Day Number using proleptic Gregorian calendar.\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input value exceeds threshold 0x8fc1d (589341 days)\n2. If above threshold: Apply high-value adjustment by converting offset values\n3. Add fixed offset 0x5f4 (1524 days, aligning to Gregorian epoch)\n4. Compute day offset using 365-day multiplication and floating-point conversion\n5. Compute month value by converting and subtracting 1 from conversion result\n6. Apply month boundary adjustment: If month > 12, subtract 13 to normalize\n7. Compute year value by subtracting magic value 0x126b (4715 years)\n8. Apply year adjustment: If month > 2, subtract additional 1 for Gregorian epoch\n9. Apply day sign adjustment: If year < 1, decrement by 1\nParameters:\npAdjustedYear: Pointer to output year value (adjusted with 4715 or 4716 offset)\npAdjustedMonth: Pointer to output month value (range 0-11 for Jan-Dec)\npAdjustedDay: Pointer to output day offset (days from reference epoch)\nReturns:\nvoid - All results written through output pointers via __stdcall callee cleanup\nSpecial Cases:\nThreshold 0x8fc1d: Separates high/low value adjustment paths for large offsets\nMagic 0x126b: Years per Gregorian calendar epoch (proleptic Gregorian constant)\nMonth > 12: Triggers -13 subtraction for year rollover handling\nMonth <= 2: Affects year computation for Gregorian leap year boundaries",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:d66397783b8041ac4efdaa82059d5768",
