      "name": "CalculateDateOffsetValue",
      "signature": "int CalculateDateOffsetValue(int nDayValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculate date offset value for log file retention\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that nDayValue is non-zero; return 0 if invalid\n2. Sign-extend negative days by adding 1\n3. Apply additional adjustment (-1) if day value is less than 3\n4. Calculate divisor: (nDivisorParam + 13) for small params, (nDivisorParam + 1) otherwise\n5. Configure floating-point rounding mode via SUB82\n6. Load adjusted day value and divisor into FPU\n7. Multiply divisor by g_dblFinalDayMultiplier (0x6ff78fe8) with rounding\n8. Multiply adjusted day by g_dblDayScalingMultiplier (0x6ff79038) with rounding\n9. Add nParamC (64-bit value) to accumulated FPU result\n10. Add g_dblOffsetConstant (0x6ff79030) to result\n11. Convert FPU result to 64-bit integer via ConvertFloatToInt64WithRounding\n12. Calculate compound index: ((nDivisorParam + nAdjustedDay * 0xC) * 0x1F) + nDayValue\n13. If compound index >= 0x8FC1D, apply correction with floor multiplications\n14. Return calculated offset in EAX\n\nParameters:\nnDayValue [EAX]: Day value (1-31) used as base input for offset calculation\nnDivisorParam [EBX, implicit]: Auxiliary parameter determining divisor selection\nnParamC [ESI:EDI, implicit]: 64-bit parameter used in floating-point accumulation\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Calculated date offset value (signed 32-bit integer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nZero day value returns 0 immediately. Negative days are sign-adjusted before processing. Days less than 3 receive additional -1 adjustment. Large compound indices (>= 0x8FC1D) trigger correction logic using g_dblScalingMultiplier (0x6ff79028) and g_dblCorrectionFactor (0x6ff79020).",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:63040bde48870168b6a8fefd32484c76",
