      "signature": "void FormatAndDisplayErrorDialog(uint nErrorCode, char * pszSourceFilePath, int nErrorLevel, va_list pMessageArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats error message with optional source context and displays in dialog box\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate stack buffers: 4096B szErrorMsg, 4096B szFinalErrorMsg, 256B szErrorTitle\n2. Call __chkstk() to probe stack allocation for 0x3100 bytes (12544 bytes total)\n3. Initialize network connections via InitializeNetworkConnection() (3 times)\n4. Build Diablo log header using BuildDiabloLogHeader()\n5. If pSourceFilePath provided (has context):\n   - Call StripSourcePathPrefix() to extract filename\n   - Format with FILE:LINE using sprintf() with szFileLineFormatString\n   - Log formatted message via LogFormattedMessage()\n6. Check if pFormatStringPtr is NULL:\n   - If NULL: emergency shutdown sequence (GetReturnAddress, WSACleanup, LogErrorAndShutdown(6), ShutdownResourcesAndExit, _exit(-1))\n   - If non-NULL: continue to message formatting\n7. Format variadic message arguments into szFormattedErrorMsg using __vsnprintf() with 0x1000 size limit\n8. Initialize bNullTerminator to 0\n9. Branch on error context:\n   - If pSourceFilePath == NULL (no context): copy szFormattedErrorMsg to szErrorMsg byte-by-byte\n   - Else (has context): lookup error message from g_pErrorMessageTable[nErrorLevel] and format with sprintf() using szContextMessageFormat\n10. Format error title: sprintf(szErrorTitle, szErrorTitleFormat, g_DiaboIIGameTitle) \u2192 \"[Code] - Diablo II\"\n11. Copy szErrorMsg to szFinalErrorMsg byte-by-byte, scanning for null terminator\n12. Locate string end in szFinalErrorMsg, append 2-byte g_wLineTerminator (0x0A00)\n13. Call ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig() to setup network state\n14. Call ShutdownResourcesAndExit() for cleanup\n15. Display MessageBoxA(NULL, szFinalErrorMsg, szErrorTitle, 0x30) where 0x30 = MB_ICONWARNING | MB_OK\n16. Return with callee cleanup of 0x8 bytes (2 stack parameters)\n\nParameters:\n- nErrorCode (ECX, __fastcall): Error code (typically 0-0x7FFFFFFF)\n- pSourceFilePath (EDX, __fastcall): Pointer to source file path string or NULL if no context\n- nErrorLevel (Stack [ESP+0x3110]): Index into g_pErrorMessageTable for error message lookup\n- pMessageArgs (Stack [ESP+0x3114]): va_list containing format string pointer and variadic arguments for __vsnprintf()\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function never returns normally; always terminates via _exit() or implicit process termination\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Emergency shutdown: Triggered when pFormatStringPtr is NULL (format string missing)\n- String buffers: All 4KB; format output truncated to 0x1000 bytes\n- Error lookup table: g_pErrorMessageTable is array of pointers indexed by nErrorLevel\n- String terminator: g_wLineTerminator contains 2-byte value (typically CRLF 0x0D0A or newline 0x0A00)\n- Multiple byte-copy loops: Each scans entire source for null terminator (inefficient but safe)\n- Stack usage: 4096 + 4096 + 256 + 8452 = 16904 bytes allocated at function entry\n- Network operations: Three InitializeNetworkConnection() calls and ValidateAndInitializeNetworkConfig() called regardless of error path\n- Title format: Result from sprintf() produces format like \"[ErrorCode] - Diablo II\"\n\nMemory Layout (ESP-relative from entry):\nOffset     | Size    | Field Name          | Type      | Purpose\n-----------|---------|---------------------|-----------|----------------------------------------\n+0x108     | 4096    | szErrorMsg          | char[]    | Formatted error message with context\n+0x1108    | 4096    | szFinalErrorMsg     | char[]    | Final message before display\n+0x2108    | 256     | szErrorTitle        | char[]    | Error dialog title bar text\n+0x3100    | 4       | returnAddress       | void*     | Saved return address\n-----------|---------|---------------------|-----------|----------------------------------------\nTotal      | 8448    | Stack frame         |           | Allocated for function execution",
