      "name": "FormatDebugMessageWrapper",
      "signature": "void FormatDebugMessageWrapper(byte debugFlags, char * pFormatString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that forwards debug message formatting to FormatAndLogDebugMessage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load second parameter (pFormatString) from stack at ESP+0x8 into ECX\n2. Load first parameter (debugFlags) from stack at ESP+0x4 into EDX\n3. Calculate address of variadic arguments (ESP+0xc) to create va_list pointer in EAX\n4. Push va_list pointer (EAX) as third parameter\n5. Push pFormatString (ECX) as second parameter\n6. Push debugFlags (EDX) as first parameter\n7. Call FormatAndLogDebugMessage to process and output the formatted debug message\n8. Return to caller with __stdcall callee cleanup (RET)\n\nParameters:\n- debugFlags (byte): Control flags for debug message output\n  * Bit 0 (0x1): Enable network configuration initialization\n  * Bit 1 (0x2): Skip OutputDebugStringA call (suppress debug output)\n  * Bit 2 (0x4): Prepend system timestamp to message\n  * Bit 3-4 (0x18): Check caps lock state via GetKeyState\n- pFormatString (char *): Printf-style format string for message substitution\n- ... (variadic): Variable number of arguments matching format string specifiers\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n- Function returns via __stdcall convention with 12-byte stack cleanup (RET 0xc implicit in calling convention)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a minimal wrapper with no business logic; all actual processing occurs in FormatAndLogDebugMessage\n- Variadic arguments are forwarded by address (va_list) rather than individual stack values\n- The va_list pointer points to the first variadic argument on the caller's stack (ESP+0xc)\n- Referenced from function pointer table at 0x6ff7d9a8, suggesting it may be dispatched indirectly\n- __stdcall convention ensures proper stack cleanup when called through pointer table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
