      "name": "FormatAndOutputDebugString",
      "signature": "void FormatAndOutputDebugString(char * szFormatString)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Formats and outputs a debug string with variadic arguments to the debugger.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 4092-byte stack buffer for formatted output string (via __chkstk prologue)\n2. Initialize buffer with null terminator at offset 0\n3. Scan buffer from offset 1 until finding the null terminator (loop_scan_string_end -> loop_check_string_end)\n4. Calculate remaining buffer space: 0x1000 - (bytes scanned)\n5. Format variadic arguments using vsnprintf, writing at current buffer position\n6. Ensure null terminator remains after formatted content at offset 0xfff\n7. Call OutputDebugStringA to send formatted buffer to debugger\n8. Deallocate stack buffer (ADD ESP, 0x1000) and return\n\nParameters:\nformatString : char * - Printf-style format string with format specifiers (%d, %s, %x, etc.)\n... : Variadic arguments - Arguments corresponding to format specifiers in formatString\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, output sent directly to debugger when debugger is attached\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Maximum output size: 4092 bytes (0x1000 - 1 for null terminator)\n- Uses alloca-style stack allocation via __chkstk stack probe call at entry\n- Output only visible when debugger is attached to process\n- String scanning loop ensures buffer is always null-terminated\n- Uses __vsnprintf for safe formatted output with size limiting\n- Final output buffer is null-terminated at offset 0xfff (0x6ff60e16-0x6ff60e1e)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
