      "comment": "Initialize game instance with system validation, configuration loading, and subsystem startup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set up stack frame with 8-byte alignment (AND ESP, 0xFFFFFFF8)\n2. Allocate 0x9C (156) bytes of stack space for local variables\n3. Initialize debug subsystem with initial parameters (0x104, ECX, 0x6ff7fcd8)\n4. Cache nCmdShow parameter in EBX for later use\n5. Check if hPrevInstance is non-null:\n   - If previous instance exists, call debug init with different parameters\n   - This handles multi-instance detection\n6. Check initialization flag g_dwGameInitialized @ 0x6ffa6e78:\n   - If already initialized (flag != 0), skip to cleanup handler at 0x6ff613b0\n   - Prevents double initialization\n7. Zero-fill 148-byte OS version info buffer on stack using STOSD.REP (37 DWORDs)\n8. Load OS version information:\n   - Call GetVersionExA via g_pfnGetVersionExA @ 0x6ff75054\n   - Store size 0x94 (148 bytes) in buffer\n   - Validate config count at offset +0x10 equals 2\n   - Set g_dwConfigValid flag based on validation result\n9. Initialize logging subsystem:\n   - Call log function pointer g_pfnLogFunction @ 0x6ff75038 twice\n   - First call: initialize console logging (0x6ff82aec)\n   - Second call: initialize file logging (0x6ff82c0c)\n10. Mark initialization complete by setting g_dwGameInitialized to 1\n11. Initialize graphics subsystem (call 0x6ff6cb50)\n12. Load version data into buffer:\n    - Call version loader (0x6ff5ce66) with parameters\n    - Extract version size from buffer offset +0xC\n    - Store size in g_dwVersionSize @ 0x6ff9af74\n13. Initialize display subsystem with parameters (0x8000, 0x40000, 0x6ff76bec, 0)\n14. Register unhandled exception filter:\n    - Call SetUnhandledExceptionFilter via g_pfnSetUnhandledExceptionFilter @ 0x6ff750dc\n    - Handler address: 0x6ff61160\n15. Perform post-initialization setup (call 0x6ff5fbc0)\n16. Execute version validation loop (32 iterations, ECX = 0 to 0x1F):\n    - Load version sentinel v1 from table @ 0x6ff76798[ECX*4]\n    - Compute expected bit mask: 1 << ECX\n    - Compare v1 against mask, jump to error handler if mismatch\n    - Load version sentinel v2 from table @ 0x6ff76818[ECX*4]\n    - Invert mask and compare v2, jump to error handler if mismatch\n    - Increment index and continue loop until all 32 checks pass\n17. If all version checks pass:\n    - Call validation function (0x6ff602c0)\n    - Initialize game state (0x6ff69530)\n18. Check if command line arguments present (lpCmdLine != NULL):\n    - If arguments exist, call cleanup handler (0x6ff613b0)\n19. Register exit handler (0x6ff617e0) via atexit\n20. Store nCmdShow parameter in g_nCmdShow @ 0x6ffa6e6c\n21. Call final initialization callback (0x6ff664a0)\n22. Restore registers (EDI, ESI, EBX) and return with __stdcall cleanup (8 bytes)\n\nError Handling:\n- Version v1 mismatch (step 16): Call error logger chain, shutdown resources, exit(-1)\n- Version v2 mismatch (step 16): Call error logger chain, shutdown resources, exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n- hInstance: Application instance handle from WinMain\n- hPrevInstance: Previous instance handle (NULL in Win32, used for multi-instance check)\n- lpCmdLine: Command line string pointer (checked for non-null to determine argument processing)\n- nCmdShow: Window show command (SW_SHOW, SW_HIDE, etc.) - cached in EBX then stored in global\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Double initialization protection: Returns immediately if g_dwGameInitialized already set\n- Multi-instance handling: Uses hPrevInstance to detect and handle multiple running instances\n- Version validation failure: Logs error details and exits process with code -1\n- Stack alignment: Ensures 8-byte alignment for SSE/performance optimization\n- Command line processing: Conditional cleanup based on lpCmdLine presence\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_dwGameInitialized @ 0x6ffa6e78: Initialization sentinel flag (0=not init, 1=initialized)\n- g_pfnGetVersionExA @ 0x6ff75054: Function pointer to GetVersionExA API\n- g_dwConfigValid @ 0x6ffa6e74: Configuration validation flag (1=valid, 0=invalid)\n- g_pfnLogFunction @ 0x6ff75038: Function pointer to logging subsystem\n- g_dwVersionSize @ 0x6ff9af74: Size of loaded version data structure\n- g_pfnSetUnhandledExceptionFilter @ 0x6ff750dc: Function pointer to exception filter API\n- g_nCmdShow @ 0x6ffa6e6c: Cached window show command for later use\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x9C (156): Stack allocation size for local buffers\n- 0x94 (148): OS version info structure size (OSVERSIONINFOEXA)\n- 0x104 (260): Debug subsystem parameter (likely MAX_PATH)\n- 0x25 (37): DWORD count for STOSD.REP zero-fill operation (37*4=148 bytes)\n- 0x20 (32): Version validation loop iteration count (32 sentinel pairs)\n- 0x8000: Display initialization parameter\n- 0x40000: Display initialization parameter\n- 0xFFFFFFF8: Stack alignment mask (8-byte boundary)",
