      "name": "CalculateBufferChecksum",
      "signature": "uint CalculateBufferChecksum(byte * pBuffer, uint dwLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Calculates a checksum for a byte buffer using table-driven accumulation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load buffer pointer (ECX) and buffer length (EDX) from stack\n2. Calculate buffer end address: pBufferEnd = pBuffer + nLength\n3. Initialize checksum accumulator (EAX) to 0\n4. Test if buffer is empty by comparing pBuffer to pBufferEnd\n5. If buffer empty (JNC), jump to return\n6. For each byte in buffer:\n   a. Load byte value from current position and zero-extend to dword\n   b. Use byte value as index into g_dwChecksumLookupTable\n   c. Add looked-up dword value to checksum accumulator\n   d. Increment buffer pointer to next position\n   e. Test if more bytes remain by comparing to pBufferEnd\n   f. If bytes remain (JC), continue loop at loop_process_byte\n7. Return accumulated checksum value\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer: Pointer to input byte buffer to be checksummed\n  nLength: Length of buffer in bytes (0-255 typically)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Accumulated checksum value (32-bit sum of table lookups)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty buffer (nLength=0): Returns 0 immediately\n  - Lookup table g_dwChecksumLookupTable has 256 entries (0-255)\n  - Table lookup provides byte-to-dword mapping for polynomial checksums",
