      "name": "DecodeHuffmanSymbol",
      "signature": "uint DecodeHuffmanSymbol(BitReader * pBitReader, int * pHuffmanTree)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Decodes a symbol from a Huffman-encoded bit stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize tree traversal index to 0\n2. Extract bit from current byte position in the input stream\n3. Calculate new position in Huffman tree based on extracted bit value\n4. If leaf node reached (tree[index] >= 0), return the symbol value\n5. Otherwise, update tree index and repeat from step 2\n6. Handle byte boundary crossing when bit position reaches 8\n\nParameters:\n- pBitReader: BitReader structure containing stream pointer, byte offset, and bit position within current byte\n- pHuffmanTree: Array of Huffman tree node values; negative values indicate internal nodes (continue traversal), non-negative values are leaf symbols\n\nReturns:\n- uint: The decoded symbol value from the leaf node when traversal completes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit position wraps to 0 when reaching byte boundary (bit position == 8)\n- Byte pointer and byte offset counter both increment when crossing byte boundary\n- Tree navigation uses tree[treeIndex + bitValue] formula for internal nodes\n- Final symbol retrieved using tree[treeIndex + bitValue] for leaf nodes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1ac62d2102e9cbb05db3b587116eec03",
