      "name": "ToggleBitInArray",
      "signature": "void ToggleBitInArray(byte * pByteArray, uint dwBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Toggle a specific bit in a byte array using bitwise XOR.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Divide bitIndex by 8 to find the byte offset (SAR ECX, 0x3)\n2. Add pByteArray to byte offset to calculate target byte address\n3. Extract bit mask from precomputed table using lower 3 bits of bitIndex\n4. Load target byte and XOR with bit mask\n5. Store result back to target byte\n6. Return to caller (stdcall, callee cleans stack)\n\nParameters:\n- pByteArray (EDX, ESP+4): Pointer to byte array to modify\n- bitIndex (EAX, ESP+8): Index of bit to toggle (0-N where byte is bitIndex/8, bit is bitIndex%8)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies array in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Bit toggle is atomic operation (single XOR)\n- Bit masks loaded from table at 0x6ff76798 (standard 2^0 through 2^7)\n- __stdcall convention: callee pops 8 bytes (2 params \u00d7 4 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout:\ngdwBitMasks table at 0x6ff76798:\n  Offset  Size  Value  Description\n  +0      4     0x01   Mask for bit 0\n  +4      4     0x02   Mask for bit 1\n  +8      4     0x04   Mask for bit 2\n  +12     4     0x08   Mask for bit 3\n  +16     4     0x10   Mask for bit 4\n  +20     4     0x20   Mask for bit 5\n  +24     4     0x40   Mask for bit 6\n  +28     4     0x80   Mask for bit 7",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
