      "name": "SetBitInArray",
      "signature": "void SetBitInArray(byte * pBitArray, uint bitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a single bit to 1 in a bitfield array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate byte offset by right-shifting bitIndex by 3 (equivalent to dividing by 8)\n2. Add byte offset to pBitArray base pointer to locate the target byte\n3. Extract the bit position within the byte using bitIndex & 0x7 (modulo 8)\n4. Load the precomputed bitmask from g_BitMaskLookupTable for that position\n5. OR the bitmask into the target byte to set the bit to 1\n6. Write the modified byte back to the array\n\nParameters:\n- pBitArray: Pointer to byte array acting as bitfield storage (caller-allocated)\n- bitIndex: Zero-based bit index to set (0 sets first bit, 1 sets second bit, etc.)\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function, modifies bitfield array in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses right-shift by 3 for fast byte offset calculation (equivalent to division by 8)\n- Uses AND with 0x7 to extract bit position (equivalent to modulo 8)\n- g_BitMaskLookupTable contains 8 precomputed masks: [0x01, 0x02, 0x04, 0x08, 0x10, 0x20, 0x40, 0x80]\n- No bounds checking; undefined behavior if bitIndex exceeds array size\n- Calling convention: __stdcall (pBitArray on ESP+4, bitIndex on ESP+8, RET 0x8)\n\nStructure Layout:\nN/A (operates on raw byte array, no structured data accessed)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
