      "comment": "Extracts a signed integer value from a bit stream decoder by extracting the specified\nnumber of bits and performing sign extension on the result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ExtractBitsFromStream to extract raw unsigned bits from the decoder\n2. Validate that numBits < 32 (0x20) to ensure valid sign extension\n3. Calculate sign bit position: numBits - 1, masked with 0x1f for safety\n4. Create test mask: 1 << (numBits - 1) to isolate the sign bit\n5. Test if sign bit is set in the extracted value\n6. If sign bit is clear, return the extracted value as-is (positive)\n7. If sign bit is set:\n   a. Create shift amount = numBits\n   b. Create mask = 1 << numBits, then decrement to (1 << numBits) - 1\n   c. Invert mask to create sign extension mask: ~((1 << numBits) - 1)\n   d. OR the extracted value with sign extension mask to fill upper bits\n8. Return the sign-extended integer value\n\nParameters:\npDecoder (BitStreamDecoder *): Pointer to bit stream decoder context. The decoder\n  maintains current bit offset and byte pointer. Modified by ExtractBitsFromStream\n  to advance the bit position by numBits.\nnumBits (int): Number of bits to extract from the stream. Valid range is 1-31.\n  Values >= 32 will skip sign extension (handled by CMP with 0x20).\n\nReturns:\nint: Sign-extended integer value extracted from the bit stream. If the sign bit\n  (bit at position numBits-1) is set, the value is sign-extended by OR-ing with\n  a mask that fills all bits above bit numBits with 1s.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If numBits >= 32, CMP 0x20 causes JGE to skip extension and return raw value\n- Sign extension mask pattern: all bits set except bits [0..numBits-1]\n- Bit offset and byte pointer in decoder are modified by ExtractBitsFromStream call\n- Used for reading variable-length signed integers from compressed bit streams",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0cd8897451ee892b2955c11eb4f32c74",
