      "signature": "void CloseNetworkSocket(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__d2edicall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "\nSafely closes a network socket within the game context and clears all references.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that game context pointer (EDI) is non-null\n2. Load socket structure pointer from game context offset 0x110\n3. Verify socket structure pointer is valid and non-null\n4. Check socket reference count field (offset +0x0) is non-zero\n5. Verify socket handle field (offset +0x8) is non-null\n6. Call ValidateDataStructureIntegrity handler to notify of closure\n7. Enter critical section at socket structure offset +0xc to prevent race conditions\n8. Reload socket structure pointer for safety\n9. Load socket handle from offset +0x8 within socket structure\n10. Call CloseSocketImportThunk to close the OS socket handle\n11. Clear socket handle field to zero (offset +0x8)\n12. Clear socket structure reference counter to zero (offset +0x0)\n13. Exit critical section to release synchronization lock\n14. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT EDI: Pointer to game context structure containing network data\nThe EDI register holds the game context pointer using the __d2edicall convention\n\nReturns:\nNone (void function). Side effects: closes socket handle and clears socket structure fields.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If game context pointer (EDI) is null, function exits immediately without cleanup\n- If socket structure pointer at offset 0x110 is null, function exits\n- If socket reference count at offset 0x0 is zero, function exits without closing\n- If socket handle at offset 0x8 is null, function exits without attempting close\n- Magic constant 0x15f (351) passed to ValidateDataStructureIntegrity\n- Uses critical section synchronization to prevent concurrent access during closure\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset   Size   Field Name              Type            Description\n  ------   ----   ----------              ----            -----------\n  0x0      4      refCount                DWORD           Reference count or validation flag\n  0x8      4      socketHandle            SOCKET          Windows socket handle\n  0xc      variable criticalSection      CRITICAL_SECTION Lock for thread-safe socket access\n",
