      "name": "ReceiveNetworkDataLoop",
      "signature": "int ReceiveNetworkDataLoop(void * pConnectionContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Receives network data from a socket in a continuous loop, parsing and processing received packets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x2068 (8292) byte receive buffer on stack\n2. Load connection state pointer from context+0x110, spin-wait until initialized\n3. Check shutdown flag at context+0x124; if set, exit\n4. Verify connection validity: state pointer non-null, flags at state+0x2c and state+0x30 are zero\n5. Call CheckSocketReadiness (0x6ff66800) to prepare socket for receiving\n6. Verify state validity again after setup call\n7. If socket ready, enter main receive loop:\n   a. Load current connection state from context+0x110\n   b. Acquire critical section at state+0xc for thread-safe socket access\n   c. Call recv() on socket (state+0x8) to read up to (0x2064 - bufferOffset) bytes into buffer\n   d. Release critical section\n   e. If recv returned error (< 1), store WSA error code at state+0x34 and set error flag (4) at state+0x30\n   f. Check if error occurred or recv returned 0; if so, exit loop\n   g. Call ProcessNetworkPackets (0x6ff6e620) to parse received data with current buffer offset\n   h. If bytes received < remaining capacity (0x2064 - bufferOffset), exit inner loop\n   i. Otherwise, check shutdown flag and continue receiving\n8. Exit main loop when shutdown flag set, error detected, or socket closed\n9. Call CloseNetworkSocket (0x6ff6e550) for cleanup before returning\n10. Return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\npConnectionContext (void *): Pointer to connection context structure containing:\n- Offset 0x08: SOCKET handle for recv() operations\n- Offset 0x0C: CRITICAL_SECTION (24 bytes) protecting socket access\n- Offset 0x110: Pointer to connection state/initialization data\n- Offset 0x124: Shutdown flag (non-zero = exit)\n\nConnection State Structure Layout (at context+0x110):\nOffset 0x00: State initialization marker (non-zero = initialized)\nOffset 0x2C: Flag indicating error/invalid state\nOffset 0x30: Error status code (4 = recv error, 0 = ok)\nOffset 0x34: WSA error code from WSAGetLastError()\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 0 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initial spin-wait loop (0x6ff6e9f0) runs indefinitely until connection initialized\n- Critical section serializes all socket recv() operations across threads\n- Fixed buffer size 0x2064 bytes determines maximum data per recv() call\n- Loop exits on shutdown flag, recv error, or incomplete buffer fill\n- WSA error codes stored at state+0x34 for error diagnostics\n- Inner loop continues reading only if buffer not full (received < remaining capacity)",
