      "name": "DequeueAndCopyNodeData",
      "signature": "ushort DequeueAndCopyNodeData(void * pDestBuffer, uint dwBufferSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ushort",
      "comment": "Dequeues the first element from a linked list, copies its data to the destination buffer, and deallocates the node from the resource pool. Thread-safe operation protected by critical section.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Acquire mutex lock by entering critical section (EBX+4 points to CRITICAL_SECTION)\\n2. Validate context block integrity (check structure at EBX+4 with ValidateDataStructureIntegrity)\\n3. Load list head pointer from context at offset EBX+0x1c\\n4. Test if list is empty (list head == NULL, jump to list_empty_exit if so)\\n5. Read node size from first word of node (offset +0x0)\\n6. Compare node size against buffer size parameter (dwBufferSize)\\n7. If buffer size < node size, set error flag at EBX+0x0 and return 0\\n8. If size valid, perform bulk data copy:\\n   a. Convert node size to dword count (size >> 2) for aligned copy\\n   b. Copy dword-aligned data from node+0x8 using REP MOVSD\\n   c. Copy remaining bytes using REP MOVSB\\n9. Read next node pointer from current node at offset +0x4\\n10. Deallocate current node using DeallocateResourcePoolElement\\n11. Update list head to point to next node (store in EBX+0x1c)\\n12. If next node is NULL (last element removed), clear flag at EBX+0x20\\n13. Release critical section lock and return copied data size\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pDestBuffer [void *]: Destination buffer pointer where node data will be written\\n  Register: EDI (set from stack parameter at ESP+0x8)\\n- dwBufferSize [uint]: Buffer capacity in bytes, must be >= node size\\n  Register: Stack parameter (ESP+0x10)\\n- Implicit pContextBlock in EBX: Pointer to context structure containing:\\n  Offset +0x04: CRITICAL_SECTION for synchronization\\n  Offset +0x1c: Linked list head pointer (node array)\\n  Offset +0x20: Flag indicating list state (cleared when empty)\\n\\nReturns:\\n- ushort: Size of data copied from dequeued node\\n  Register: EAX (low word of EDI when successful)\\n  Value 0 returned if: list empty OR buffer size insufficient\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty list: Return size 0 without error flag set\\n- Size mismatch: Error flag (EBX+0x0 = 1) set, return 0\\n- Last element: When next node is NULL, clears state flag at EBX+0x20\\n- NULL destination: Data still copied internally but discarded (in-place copy)\\n\\nMemory Layout - Node Structure (linked list element):\\nOffset 0x00: WORD - Node data size (checked against buffer size)\\nOffset 0x02: WORD - Reserved/alignment\\nOffset 0x04: DWORD - Pointer to next node (or NULL if last)\\nOffset 0x08: [Variable] - Actual node data (copied to pDestBuffer)\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
