      "name": "EncodeIntegerValue",
      "signature": "byte * EncodeIntegerValue(byte * pOutputStart, int nValue, byte * pCurrentPos)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Encodes a signed integer value using variable-length format into output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Classify value by range: 8-bit (-128 to 127), 16-bit (-32768 to 32767), or 32-bit (all others)\n2. Calculate required output bytes: type 0x7 = 2 bytes, type 0x8 = 3 bytes, type 0x9 = 5 bytes\n3. Check if available space (ESI register) >= required bytes\n4. If insufficient space: set pOutputStart[0] = 0, return NULL (error indicator)\n5. If sufficient space: write type marker byte + value bytes to pCurrentPos\n6. Increment encoder context counter at [pEncoderContext + 0x144]\n7. Return updated write position (pCurrentPos + bytes_written)\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputStart (ECX): Pointer to buffer start (used as error marker location)\n- nValue (EDX): Signed integer to encode (-2147483648 to 2147483647)\n- pCurrentPos (Stack[0x4]): Current write position in buffer\n\nImplicit Parameters (register-preserved):\n- ESI: Available space remaining in buffer (bytes)\n- EDI: pEncoderContext pointer (structure with counter at offset 0x144)\n\nReturns:\n- Success: Updated position pointer (pCurrentPos incremented by 2, 3, or 5)\n- Error: NULL (0x0) when buffer space insufficient\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative values: handled with signed range checks; -1 fits in 8-bit type 0x7\n- Buffer overflow: detected before writing; error marker at pOutputStart[0] = 0\n- Type 0x7: 1-byte signed integer + 1-byte type marker = 2 bytes total\n- Type 0x8: 2-byte signed short + 1-byte type marker = 3 bytes total\n- Type 0x9: 4-byte signed int + 1-byte type marker = 5 bytes total\n- Counter location: EDI + 0x144 contains total count of encoded values\n- Calling convention: __fastcall with RET 0x4 (callee cleans 4 bytes from stack)\n\nStructure Layout (pEncoderContext):\nOffset  Size    Field Name              Type        Description\n0x144   4       nEncodedValueCount      int         Running count of encoded integer values",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
