      "name": "ParseExpressionToken",
      "signature": "char * ParseExpressionToken(char * pExpressionString, uchar * pOutTokenType, void * pLookupCallback, void * pValidateCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Parses next token from expression string and returns token type code.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace and quote characters at expression start\n2. Check if token is numeric (digit):\n   - Parse multi-digit decimal number, accumulate via expr = expr * 10 + digit\n   - Set token type to 0x10 (number), return next position after number\n3. Check if token is string literal (single quote):\n   - Parse string body until closing quote or null terminator\n   - Call pValidateCallback to lookup/validate string value\n   - If callback returns non-negative value, set type based on function call flag\n   - Return next position or NULL if callback failed\n4. Check if token is identifier (alphabetic):\n   - Parse identifier: accumulate alphanumeric characters (max 255)\n   - Check for function call syntax: if next char is '(' and pLookupCallback succeeds\n   - Set token type to 0x12 (function call) or 0x10 (identifier) accordingly\n   - Call pValidateCallback to validate/lookup identifier in context\n   - Return next position or NULL if validation failed\n5. Check for special case: period (.) for field/method access\n   - Parse field name after period until non-alphanumeric\n   - Call pValidateCallback with field name from context lookup tables\n   - Return next position or NULL if callback failed\n6. Match single and double-character operators via switch dispatch table:\n   - Single-char: ( ) + - * / : ? ^ , = ! < >\n   - Double-char: <= >= == !=\n   - Assign token type (0x00-0x0f) and return next position\n7. Return NULL if token is invalid or callback indicated error\n\nParameters:\npExpressionString [in] Pointer to current position in expression string\npOutTokenType [out] Pointer to byte for output token type code\npLookupCallback [in] Function pointer for identifier lookup/validation\npValidateCallback [in] Function pointer for token value validation\n\nToken Type Codes:\n0x00 = open paren '('          0x01 = close paren ')'       0x02 = comma ','\n0x03 = plus '+'                0x04 = minus '-'              0x05 = multiply '*'\n0x06 = divide '/'              0x07 = question '?'           0x08 = colon ':'\n0x09 = caret '^'               0x0a = less_equal '<='        0x0b = less '<'\n0x0c = greater '>'             0x0d = greater_equal '>='     0x0e = equal_equal '=='\n0x0f = not_equal '!='          0x10 = identifier/number      0x12 = function_call\n\nReturns:\nPointer to next character position after parsed token\nNULL if token invalid or callback returned error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Identifiers and string literals max 255 chars\n- Multi-digit numbers parsed as decimal\n- Period (.) triggers field name lookup with context offset calculations\n- Callbacks may return negative error codes to indicate validation failure\n- String/identifier buffer stored in local 256-byte tokenBuffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
