      "comment": "Encodes a sequence of tokens from a stack into a byte buffer with cost tracking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load token count from pTokenState[0x140] and check if any tokens exist\n2. Loop while tokens remain in stack:\n   a. Load current token byte from pTokenState[pTokenState[0x140]-1]\n   b. Validate token constraints:\n      - Token != 0x01 (reserved marker)\n      - Operation code != 0x01 (reserved)\n      - Token < 0x17 (max valid token 0x16)\n      - Token cost from g_TokenCostTable[tokenByte] <= nOperationCode (available budget)\n   c. Dispatch token via jump table (g_TokenDispatchTable):\n      - Token 0x15: Cost = 1 point\n      - Tokens 0x0A-0x14: Cost = 2 points\n      - Token 0x16: Cost = 3 points\n      - Token 0x01: Invoke pCallbackFunction callback (if provided)\n      - Other tokens: Cost = 0 points\n   d. Validate cost against budget: pTokenState[0x144] >= tokenCost\n   e. Write token byte to current output position\n   f. Update counters:\n      - Increment output position (currentOutputPos++)\n      - Decrement token count (pTokenState[0x140]--)\n      - Update budget: pTokenState[0x144] = pTokenState[0x144] + (1 - tokenCost)\n3. After loop, check finalization criteria:\n   a. If nOperationCode != 0x17 AND nOperationCode != 0x03:\n      - If nOperationCode != 0x00 (not terminator-only):\n        * Verify stack offset < 0x40 (maximum 64 entries)\n        * Store operation code at pTokenState[pTokenState[0x140]]\n        * Store callback parameter at pTokenState[0x40 + pTokenState[0x140]*4]\n        * Increment stack offset\n4. Return handling:\n   a. If nOperationCode == 0x00: Write NULL terminator byte to output, return output+1\n   b. If nOperationCode != 0x00: Return output position (no terminator)\n   c. On error (overflow/invalid token): Write 0x00 to pOutputBuffer[0], return NULL\n\nParameters:\n- pOutputBuffer: Destination buffer for encoded token stream (modified)\n- nMaxOutputSize: Maximum bytes available in output buffer\n- nOperationCode: Operation code (0x00-0x17) controlling finalization behavior\n- pCallbackFunction: Optional callback function invoked for token 0x01 (may be NULL)\n- nCallbackParam: Parameter passed to callback function via ECX register\n\nReturns:\n- Non-NULL: Pointer to next available position in output buffer on success\n- NULL: Error condition (buffer overflow, invalid token, or stack overflow)\n\nSpecial Cases and Magic Numbers:\n- Token stack location: pTokenState + 0x140 (token count/offset)\n- Cost budget location: pTokenState + 0x144 (remaining point budget)\n- Operation parameter storage: pTokenState + 0x40 (array of parameters by stack offset)\n- Maximum stack entries: 0x40 (64 operations)\n- Cost lookup table: g_TokenCostTable (indexed by token byte, returns cost points)\n- Jump table: g_TokenDispatchTable (22 entries, one per valid token)\n- Special operation code 0x17: Finalize without writing operation\n- Special operation code 0x03: Finalize without writing operation\n- Special operation code 0x00: Write NULL terminator to output\n- Error marker: 0x00 byte written to pOutputBuffer[0] on failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\n------  ----  -----------------   --------- -----------------------\n+0x140   4    nTokenCount        uint32    Token count / stack offset\n+0x144   4    nCostBudget        uint32    Remaining point budget\n+0x00    N    aOperationCodes    byte[]    Array of operation codes\n+0x40    N    aOperationParams   uint32[]  Array of operation parameters",
