      "name": "InterpretBytecodeProgram",
      "signature": "uint InterpretBytecodeProgram(uint * pBytecodeStream, int nBytecodeLength, void * pCallbackFunctions, int * pDataTable, int nDataTableCount, uint dwMiscParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Interprets and executes a stack-based bytecode program.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate bytecodeLength > 0; return 0 if invalid\n2. Initialize stack pointer to 0 and evaluation stack (64-entry capacity)\n3. Main loop: Iterate through bytecode stream fetching instructions\n4. For each bytecode instruction (opcode 1-22):\n   - Opcode 1: Load indexed - fetch byte offset from stream, lookup pDataTable entry, call indexed function handler\n   - Opcodes 4-6: Load constants - invoke pCallbackFunctions callback, push result to stack\n   - Opcodes 7-9: Push literals - load byte/word/dword literal from stream, push to stack\n   - Opcodes 10-15: Comparisons - pop two stack values, compare (LT, LE, GT, GE, EQ, NE), push bool result\n   - Opcodes 16-19: Arithmetic - pop two values, perform operation (ADD, SUB, MUL, DIV), push result\n   - Opcode 20: Power - pop two values (base, exponent), compute base^exponent, push result\n   - Opcode 21: Negate - pop one value, negate, push result\n   - Opcode 22: Conditional select - pop three values (condition, falseVal, trueVal), select result based on condition\n5. End of bytecode stream or invalid opcode: return top of stack (stackIndex-1) or 0 if empty\n\nParameters:\npBytecodeStream (uint *) - Pointer to bytecode instruction stream encoded as bytes/words/dwords\nbytecodeLength (int) - Number of bytecode elements to process (bounds for offset calculations)\npCallbackFunctions (void *) - Function pointer for loading constant values via opcodes 4-6\npDataTable (int *) - Array of [functionPtr, typeCode] pairs accessed as pDataTable[index*2] and pDataTable[index*2+1]\ndataTableCount (int) - Number of entries in pDataTable (validates index bounds for opcode 1)\nmiscParam (uint) - Additional parameter passed to callback functions\n\nReturns:\nuint - Value at top of evaluation stack on successful completion, or 0 if stack empty/error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Stack overflow: If stackIndex >= 0x40 (64), operation skipped but execution continues\n- Index out of bounds: If index >= dataTableCount, push 0 to stack and continue\n- Division by zero (opcode 19): Returns without pushing result, exits to caller\n- Empty stack on pop: Returns 0 as default for binary/unary operations\n- Invalid opcode (>0x15): Returns top of stack or 0\n\nStructure Layout (pDataTable entries, stride 8 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type      Description\n0x00    4     pFunction       void*     Function pointer for indexed operation\n0x04    4     typeCode        int       Type handler (0=call direct, 1-3=parameter handling)",
