      "name": "GenerateSequentialFloatValuesIntoBuffer",
      "signature": "void GenerateSequentialFloatValuesIntoBuffer(int outputFormat, void * pOutputBuffer, double startValue, int numElements, int endValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Generates a sequence of floating-point values into an output buffer with format conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate outputFormat parameter is valid (1=byte, 2=word, 4=dword)\n2. Validate numElements is non-negative; exit with error code 0xf if negative\n3. Validate startValue is within valid range [g_dblMinValueThreshold, g_dblMaxValueThreshold]; exit with error code 0x10 if out of range\n4. Initialize FPU state if g_dwFPUConfigEnabled is set by calling DispatchExtendedPrecisionFloatOperation\n5. Calculate iteration step size as (endValue - g_dblDenormalizedConstant)\n6. Loop iteration: Call DispatchDamageCalculationByFPUState to calculate next value\n7. Convert result to 64-bit integer via ConvertFloatToInt64WithRounding\n8. Store result in output buffer with format conversion (byte/word/dword) and advance pointer\n9. Increment currentValue by g_dblDenormalizedConstant step size and compare with iteration limit\n10. Repeat loop until currentValue >= iteration limit, return on completion\n\nParameters:\n- outputFormat (int): Element storage format (1=char/byte, 2=short/word, 4=int/dword)\n- pOutputBuffer (void*): Output buffer pointer for storing generated values\n- startValue (double): Initial value for generation sequence\n- numElements (int): Expected element count (validation parameter)\n- endValue (int): Upper bound for iteration count\n\nReturns: void (no return value; calls error handlers on validation failures)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0xe: outputFormat not in {1, 2, 4}; triggers LogErrorAndShutdown with code 0xe\n- Error code 0xf: numElements < 0; triggers LogErrorAndShutdown with code 0xf\n- Error code 0x10: startValue outside [g_dblMinValueThreshold, g_dblMaxValueThreshold]; triggers error handler\n- g_dwFPUConfigEnabled: If non-zero, FPU state is configured via dispatch before main loop\n- g_dblDenormalizedConstant: Step increment used in both iteration count and loop counter\n- g_dblMinValueThreshold, g_dblMaxValueThreshold: Range validation bounds for startValue\n- All float calculations use x87 FPU (FLD, FADD, FSUB, FMUL, FDIV instructions)\n- Error handlers call WSACleanup, LogErrorAndShutdown, ShutdownResourcesAndExit, and _exit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
