      "name": "CheckCPUCapabilitiesAndComputePower",
      "signature": "double CheckCPUCapabilitiesAndComputePower(double base, double exponent, uint param_3, uint param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "double",
      "comment": "CPU Capability Detection and Power Function Wrapper\n\nChecks CPU optimization flags and floating-point state before computing base^exponent.\nRoutes to either optimized SSE path (ComputePowerFunction) or standard C library fallback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if CPU optimization flag (0x6fc468fc) is enabled\n2. If disabled, jump to fallback handler at 0x6fc2ca14\n3. Save and verify MXCSR register for SSE state (bits 0x1f80)\n4. Verify FPU control word precision bits are set to 0x7f\n5. If all checks pass, jump to optimized ComputePowerFunction\n6. Otherwise, call standard fallback via __fload_withFB\n\nParameters:\n- base (double): Base value for exponentiation (ST0/ST1)\n- exponent (double): Exponent value (stack-based, varies by FPU state)\n\nReturns:\n- double: Result of base^exponent computation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- SSE disabled: MXCSR bits 0x1f80 not set = use fallback\n- FPU precision bits: 0x7f mask for extended precision\n- Optimization flag bypass: Can force fallback via 0x6fc468fc = 0\n- CPU state corruption: Either MXCSR or FPU check fails = fallback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:f2bf87e3d7716fbd4c27ab2a2f3f3401",
