      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup critical section embedded within object structure\n\nThis function serves as a destructor wrapper that cleans up a CRITICAL_SECTION\nembedded at offset +0x14 within a larger object structure. It adjusts the\nobject pointer to reference the embedded critical section and delegates\ncleanup to DeleteCriticalSectionWrapper.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load object base pointer from stack parameter [EBP+0x4]\n2. Calculate pointer to embedded critical section at offset +0x14\n3. Tail-call to DeleteCriticalSectionWrapper with adjusted pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pObject - Pointer to object containing embedded CRITICAL_SECTION at +0x14\n\nReturns:\n  void (tail-call optimization - no explicit return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses tail-call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET)\n  - Critical section is embedded at fixed offset 0x14 (20 bytes) from base\n  - Assumes object structure has CRITICAL_SECTION member at +0x14\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name           Type                Description\n  ------  ----  -------------------  ------------------  ---------------------\n  +0x00   20    (unknown fields)     varies              Object header/data\n  +0x14   24    criticalSection      CRITICAL_SECTION    Synchronization lock\n\nNote: This function cannot be decompiled due to tail-call optimization.",
