      "name": "AllocateAndValidateResourceSlot",
      "signature": "undefined4 * AllocateAndValidateResourceSlot(void * this, char * param_1, undefined4 param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined4 *",
      "comment": "AllocateAndValidateResourceSlot - Allocate and validate a resource pool slot\n\nPurpose:\nAttempts to allocate or validate a resource slot from a memory pool. If allocation\nfails, logs an error and triggers application shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save callee-preserved registers (EBX, ESI, EDI) on stack\n2. Load parameters: pPoolNode in ECX, dwContextFlags in EDX, pErrorMessage in EBX, dwErrorCode in EDI\n3. Load global state flag (g_dwStateUpdateFlag) from 0x6ff7f350\n4. Negate flag and sign-extend to full register (NEG + SBB trick)\n5. AND the sign-extended flag with dwContextFlags to conditionally mask context\n6. Call AllocateMemorySlotFromPool with masked context and pPoolNode parameters\n7. Store result in ESI\n8. Test result for null (TEST ESI, ESI)\n9. If not null (JNZ), jump to cleanup_and_return\n10. If null, push error parameters and call LogErrorAndShutdown with error code 2\n11. Clean up stack (ADD ESP, 0x10)\n12. Restore callee-preserved registers\n13. Return with stack cleanup (RET 0xC pops 12 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n- pPoolNode (ECX, __thiscall implicit): ResourcePoolNode* - pointer to the pool node to allocate from\n- dwContextFlags (EDX): uint - context/state flags that may be conditionally masked\n- pErrorMessage ([ESP+0x8]): char* - error message string for logging\n- dwErrorCode ([ESP+0x14]): uint - error code to pass to logging function\n\nReturn Value:\n- EAX: ResourcePoolNode* - pointer to allocated/validated resource slot, NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global state flag (g_dwStateUpdateFlag) controls context masking via NEG+SBB technique\n- When state flag != 0, context is masked to zero before allocation\n- Allocation failure triggers immediate error logging and shutdown\n- No error recovery - function does not return after failed allocation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "EXP",
      "index": "EXP:4",
